1
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:10,080
(Life Submission for Day 2)

2
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:11,950
That's right.

3
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:13,180
(The supermarket will be closed
the following day.)

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,480
That's right.

5
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:18,290
We should have listened to you
during lunch earlier.

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,190
- What did I say?
- You said we should get more...

7
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:21,460
and offered to give us ramyeon.

8
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,420
We should have gotten more during dinner.

9
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:25,690
- Exactly.
- But starving for a day is also...

10
00:00:25,690 --> 00:00:27,660
- We'll get to our senses when we starve.
- I should have bought more earlier.

11
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:28,830
Darn it.

12
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:31,170
Are you completely out of food?

13
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:33,500
We have four eggs left.

14
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:35,570
That's tough.

15
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,540
- Did you finish the red bean paste bread?
- Yes.

16
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:40,210
- That's tough.
- I have one ramyeon left.

17
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:41,380
- Okay.
- I'll give you that.

18
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,780
What will you eat tomorrow?

19
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,350
I can go without eating for a day.

20
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:45,410
- Really?
- Yes.

21
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:47,550
I normally refuse these kinds of offers,

22
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:50,250
but from what I've seen,
my team members...

23
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,890
go crazy when they're not fed.

24
00:00:51,990 --> 00:00:54,560
- I'll give it to you.
- I'll take it if you're offering.

25
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:56,290
He's already looking out for his members.

26
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:59,190
People like him
are usually the most loyal.

27
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:01,230
I'll be the first to die in my team.

28
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:03,430
(Life Submission for Day 2)

29
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,770
Today's my chance.

30
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,600
(Life Submission for Day 2: Salt, Pitou)

31
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,260
(Life Submission for Day 2:
Salt, Genie, Pitou)

32
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,830
Your life submission is complete.

33
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:39,400
Since I'm the leader,

34
00:01:39,830 --> 00:01:41,040
I could kill them.

35
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,340
Since it's so hard to persuade them,

36
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,140
I could just submit mine...

37
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:46,740
and kill them both.

38
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,910
"This is a survival game, after all.
It's just a game."

39
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:50,910
"I can be the only one who survives."

40
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:53,920
But I'm not sure I can make it...

41
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:56,780
through the rest of this on my own.

42
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:00,150
I need someone to talk to...

43
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:02,920
and support me through the days.

44
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:06,090
Having different opinions is fine with me.

45
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,660
I need those things more...

46
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:12,270
than being alone.

47
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:15,370
We don't have that many members
in the first place.

48
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:16,540
It's just the three of us.

49
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,640
"Would killing them be beneficial to me?"

50
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:22,210
That's what I thought.

51
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:28,980
- What's the matter?
- Are you feeling troubled?

52
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,020
- What did you say?
- Is our reality troubling you?

53
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:33,020
I really had a moment of hesitation.

54
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,820
To submit only one life?

55
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,830
It's really funny, isn't it?
Do you know what happens...

56
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:39,190
when you submit it?

57
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:41,030
The team members are in gray at first.

58
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,200
Once you submit the lives,
that person's picture gets color.

59
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:46,070
That's so cruel.

60
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,040
That's really stimulating.

61
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,840
They look like funeral portraits at first.

62
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:53,910
It's really stimulating.

63
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:57,650
It makes you think a lot.

64
00:02:57,650 --> 00:02:59,310
I was standing there, and...

65
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:06,890
(What will you do
if you get the next chance?)

66
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:09,360
(Salt, writer)

67
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:11,060
I don't think I'll hold back then.

68
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:16,500
Assign lives to the residents
of your choice.

69
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,370
(Life Submission for Day 2)

70
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:24,270
(Leia, Luna, Paul, Boss, Siseon,)

71
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:27,070
(Hamlet)

72
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:30,380
I'll issue diamonds.

73
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,920
(Team White discussed
issuing more diamonds.)

74
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:36,450
Thirty diamonds? We're honestly too nice.

75
00:03:36,450 --> 00:03:38,120
They'll say we're so naive.

76
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,850
Thirty-four? What do you think?

77
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:43,620
(They set the amount
to minimize changes in value.)

78
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:45,230
- It's just a good number.
- Thirty-four.

79
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,930
Please write the desired amount...

80
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:50,100
and submit it in the central box.

81
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:53,100
I submitted it.

82
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:57,210
Are you going to talk about
the code here, or...

83
00:03:57,470 --> 00:04:00,310
- I'll just share it with my authority.
- Right...

84
00:04:00,470 --> 00:04:02,810
It's for the public good,
so that would be fine.

85
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:05,710
It wouldn't be solved
if we only focused on one code.

86
00:04:05,710 --> 00:04:07,550
- It was set so we could work together.
- Right.

87
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:09,920
To a certain point,
we have to work together...

88
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:12,120
and solve it by sharing it.

89
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:15,390
We need to earn the resources quickly
and share them with the community...

90
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,760
to make the situation better.

91
00:04:17,930 --> 00:04:19,560
- I'll solve it with you.
- Okay.

92
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,730
All right.

93
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:24,670
Thirty-four diamonds have been issued.

94
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,000
So this is how they're given.

95
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,840
Thirty-four.

96
00:04:31,970 --> 00:04:33,240
Thank you.

97
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:41,280
(Resources After Day 2's Life Submission)

98
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,490
The official schedule for Day Two
has ended.

99
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:46,190
Black's supermarket...

100
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,420
will be closed tomorrow
due to insufficient lives.

101
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,930
The supermarket will be closed tomorrow?

102
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:53,690
- We received lives earlier.
- That's right.

103
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:55,460
Residents are free...

104
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:58,430
to rest and continue their conversations.

105
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,630
The supermarket is closed?

106
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:01,870
- I think we have to ask.
- Have a good night.

107
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,670
The supermarket is closed?

108
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:06,970
It's closed
because Black doesn't have lives.

109
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:09,180
- What?
- Are we supposed to starve tomorrow?

110
00:05:09,210 --> 00:05:10,480
What?

111
00:05:11,010 --> 00:05:12,050
This is trouble.

112
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,220
- Did something happen to Black?
- What's going on?

113
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,450
Is Black dead?

114
00:05:19,890 --> 00:05:22,390
We're suddenly hearing shocking news.

115
00:05:24,130 --> 00:05:26,460
(Dormitory for Black)

116
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,200
Ramyeon.

117
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,470
Ramyeon.

118
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:36,640
Yukgaejang.

119
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,870
I'll give them my precious yukgaejang.

120
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:42,210
(The leaders started sharing their codes.)

121
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:44,250
It doesn't add up.

122
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,350
Could you tell us what you got?

123
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:49,120
- What we got?
- Yes?

124
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,850
We received a hint...

125
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:54,690
saying there's a secret room
in the center.

126
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:57,090
- What?
- We've been searching for two days,

127
00:05:57,430 --> 00:05:59,630
- That was why...
- but we couldn't find...

128
00:05:59,890 --> 00:06:01,030
the entrance to the secret room.

129
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,700
I think we can get the rest of the hints
from your codes.

130
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:06,700
- Really?
- We've been searching...

131
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,140
the center since yesterday.

132
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:10,270
We thought it was getting impossible
to find it.

133
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,810
We'll tell you once we do.

134
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:14,380
Could you tell us the code?

135
00:06:14,510 --> 00:06:15,680
- Ours?
- Yes.

136
00:06:16,910 --> 00:06:17,950
Here.

137
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:21,020
- You're an angel.
- You're an angel.

138
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,080
This is all I have.

139
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:26,450
- That's a huge one.
- It's my precious...

140
00:06:26,450 --> 00:06:27,520
Seriously.

141
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,090
- Did you share the codes?
- Yes.

142
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:30,190
- Yes.
- Could you tell me...

143
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,530
He still needs to solve it.

144
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,090
- I think we have to decipher it.
- Right.

145
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:36,460
- What...
- This was ours.

146
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,570
- That's ours...
- What is this? C?

147
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:40,530
- It's C. CEN.
- What is that?

148
00:06:40,530 --> 00:06:42,240
CENS.

149
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,470
- You memorized that?
- Yes.

150
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:45,210
(Maillard told them the code
in a scrambled order.)

151
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:46,210
You memorized this?

152
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:48,940
- We shared our codes.
- Yes.

153
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:50,640
That would be a hint.

154
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:54,920
Will you go check it out
with your team members first?

155
00:06:55,050 --> 00:06:57,790
We'll solve it and tell you what we got.

156
00:06:57,790 --> 00:06:59,950
- You'll share it with us first.
- Yes.

157
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:02,060
I love this community based on trust.

158
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,330
But if the community based on trust
doesn't work,

159
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:07,160
- there's a new option we earned today.
- That's right.

160
00:07:07,430 --> 00:07:08,960
- We'll have to use that.
- That's right.

161
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,260
We have to start eliminating people.

162
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:11,730
Once one person starts betraying the team,

163
00:07:11,730 --> 00:07:12,730
- We can also go to war.
- it'll be war.

164
00:07:12,730 --> 00:07:14,270
- Of course.
- What's Team White's code?

165
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:16,170
- Team White's code...
- Yes.

166
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,510
I'll have to solve this today.

167
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:20,810
Can they be solved in the same way?

168
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:22,010
Yes. They're all the same.

169
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:23,510
It's also very easy.

170
00:07:23,510 --> 00:07:25,050
- You'll be able to solve it soon.
- Then...

171
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:27,310
- Three to the sixth power?
- Yes.

172
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,520
I just stood next to them naturally.

173
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,390
There were no more chairs.

174
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:33,290
It would have seemed
more natural if I were sitting down.

175
00:07:33,690 --> 00:07:37,790
I looked like a hyena
wandering around to get something.

176
00:07:38,030 --> 00:07:40,030
I didn't give up there.

177
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:41,800
I was determined to solve the codes first.

178
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,100
I should solve it first...

179
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,770
and get rid of the clues.

180
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:47,370
That's why I wrote them down.

181
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:49,770
Fortunately, Team White
and Team Blue weren't suspicious of me.

182
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,610
Team Red also easily gave me their code.

183
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:54,340
I think it was because
I gave him my ramyeon.

184
00:07:55,610 --> 00:08:00,280
Vector kept asking hurriedly,

185
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,320
"Tell me too."

186
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:04,790
"How do you solve this?"
He kept asking us that.

187
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:06,490
At first,

188
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:09,190
I thought he was writing them down...

189
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:11,990
to help us solve the codes,
but I don't think that was the case.

190
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:15,030
From the way he wrote them down,

191
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:16,630
I could feel the obsession.

192
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,070
He wasn't the usual cool Vector.

193
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,340
I'm quite worried.

194
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:24,510
I think he has a code,
but he's not telling us.

195
00:08:25,970 --> 00:08:27,370
- All right.
- Okay.

196
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:29,280
- I'll share it with you tomorrow.
- Thank you.

197
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,980
Please make it quick.

198
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,310
- All right.
- Yes.

199
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:34,050
- Please...
- Thank you for this.

200
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:35,850
- Yes. Enjoy.
- Goodness.

201
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,490
We're in trouble.

202
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,760
Why?

203
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:44,930
Didn't you hear the announcement?

204
00:08:45,690 --> 00:08:47,530
- The supermarket...
- It won't open tomorrow.

205
00:08:47,730 --> 00:08:50,000
- Anyway...
- We have no food.

206
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,500
- Some bananas...
- We have six bananas...

207
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:52,700
- Eggs.
- and eggs.

208
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,700
These are all we have.
We have to get by with these.

209
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,540
So we can't eat anything tomorrow?

210
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:57,940
- We'll have those.
- That's why...

211
00:08:57,940 --> 00:09:00,440
That's why we had to buy
many things this afternoon.

212
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,240
We have to survive on those
throughout tomorrow?

213
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,680
- Yes.
- There's some bread as well.

214
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,450
There's a team that finished their bread.

215
00:09:05,450 --> 00:09:07,110
- The day after tomorrow will be chaos.
- There's a team...

216
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:08,350
- with no food.
- It'll be chaos.

217
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,920
Does gum have calories?

218
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,120
I bought zero-calorie gum.

219
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,350
It'll make you hungrier.

220
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:16,190
I shared this with everyone.

221
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,530
- Why?
- They solved this.

222
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:20,060
- Theirs?
- We can solve it...

223
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,200
once we put all the codes together.

224
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:23,000
We need to put the codes together.

225
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,200
We shared our codes...

226
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:26,370
on the condition that they'll share theirs
with us once they solve it.

227
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,200
What we know...

228
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:30,870
is that there's a secret room...

229
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,310
somewhere here.

230
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,580
That was why I saw...

231
00:09:34,810 --> 00:09:36,410
Team Red going around places.

232
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:37,610
We'll be able to solve this soon.

233
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:39,550
- I'll write it down.
- There's a calculator as well.

234
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:41,580
The way of solving
would be different from ours.

235
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,480
It's the same. These numbers...

236
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,890
are only split by this plus sign.

237
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:47,920
(Team White's Wall Code)

238
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:50,560
Hint.

239
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,560
- Look...
- You're right.

240
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,930
"Placed within."

241
00:09:58,270 --> 00:09:59,670
It's placed within somewhere.

242
00:09:59,970 --> 00:10:01,240
That's right. Also...

243
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:10,480
"Tell these words in the center."

244
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:13,280
"Tell these words in the center."

245
00:10:13,510 --> 00:10:15,650
Something's missing. Black has a code.

246
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,820
We have to get his as well.

247
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:20,750
Black has a code, but he keeps saying
he doesn't have it.

248
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,320
How do we kill Black?

249
00:10:24,190 --> 00:10:26,290
We can't solve this without Black.

250
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,030
Then,

251
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:31,330
if we deduce the order,

252
00:10:31,570 --> 00:10:33,000
- this is the fourth one.
- Right.

253
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,170
"Tell these words."

254
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:36,370
"In the center."

255
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:39,970
"Placed within secret room."

256
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:42,110
- We need all four codes.
- Yes.

257
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,810
It looks like Black has the words.

258
00:10:44,950 --> 00:10:46,610
We need to know those words.

259
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:50,450
The truth of the weapon dealer...

260
00:10:50,820 --> 00:10:52,650
placed within secret room of center.

261
00:10:54,490 --> 00:10:57,830
(The empty second box
is for "Truth of the Weapon Dealer.")

262
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:00,460
Black took the codes too.

263
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:02,300
And he didn't give you any?

264
00:11:02,630 --> 00:11:04,670
- Black will definitely solve the codes.
- Right.

265
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,200
He'll take this.

266
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:12,340
How far is Black going to take this?

267
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,280
What will happen if I get caught?

268
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:18,950
Will I die if I get caught?

269
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:20,480
Will I die?

270
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,350
What happens if I get caught?

271
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:24,920
Goodness.

272
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,530
Help me.

273
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:33,760
I hope people
are not in their right minds tomorrow...

274
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,300
because of the hunger.

275
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:37,200
Yes?

276
00:11:39,330 --> 00:11:40,600
Vector.

277
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,140
Give me the code quickly. You have a code.

278
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:45,310
We need four codes to solve this.

279
00:11:45,410 --> 00:11:47,840
- I really don't have it.
- It's in here.

280
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,740
We can't solve this
if you don't share the code with us.

281
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:51,510
I really don't have it.

282
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:53,850
Then can I tell the others tomorrow...

283
00:11:53,850 --> 00:11:55,450
that we can't solve the code
because Black isn't telling us his?

284
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:57,890
Then people will start suspecting me.

285
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:00,550
Exactly. Give me the code now.
I know you have it.

286
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:02,420
- I really don't know the code.
- I know you do.

287
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:04,190
I'll make you look suspicious
if you don't tell me.

288
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:07,900
- I mean...
- That's how things look right now.

289
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,460
- Come in and see.
- No one is going to believe that.

290
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,470
I'm not the only one
who won't believe you.

291
00:12:11,470 --> 00:12:12,470
When I tell the other leaders tomorrow,

292
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:13,800
they won't believe it either.

293
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,540
They shared their codes,

294
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,940
and I shared mine as well.

295
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:19,710
The only one missing is Black's code.

296
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,680
That will definitely...

297
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,640
make you look suspicious tomorrow.

298
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:26,750
I shared our code, Blue shared theirs,
and White shared theirs.

299
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:29,580
We're just missing one,
and that's Black's code.

300
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:33,620
Do you think people will believe you
if you explained that?

301
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:35,960
You earned all the codes today.

302
00:12:36,890 --> 00:12:37,930
Seriously.

303
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:40,030
You earned everything
and didn't give out yours.

304
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:41,330
I really don't have anything.

305
00:12:41,330 --> 00:12:43,130
I think he's trying to get something
out of this and just take off.

306
00:12:43,130 --> 00:12:45,430
- Black might disappear tomorrow.
- I really don't have it.

307
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:46,430
That's really not true.

308
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:48,000
We can't do anything
since he's saying he doesn't have it.

309
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,670
- I'm telling the truth.
- He can't run his business either.

310
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:53,340
- We're going to go hungry tomorrow.
- You're not keeping it from us?

311
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,680
Did you hear about the cup noodle
I gave him?

312
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:56,180
- Are you telling the truth?
- I'm really not hiding the code.

313
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:57,240
Really?

314
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,780
- I...
- Just trust me this once.

315
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:00,610
- I...
- Think about it.

316
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:03,020
- I think Vector...
- If they were trying to create a mole,

317
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,850
do you think they'd make it this obvious?

318
00:13:05,090 --> 00:13:06,750
You're not making it obvious.
You're doing a good job.

319
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,420
That's why it's more...

320
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,120
It looks more suspicious.

321
00:13:10,820 --> 00:13:12,260
I want you to come and look inside.

322
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,430
I wanted to go there since this morning.

323
00:13:13,430 --> 00:13:15,460
There is no code in my room. Seriously.

324
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:17,630
Black knows the amount
of all the resources.

325
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,130
Why aren't you telling us properly?

326
00:13:19,130 --> 00:13:21,870
I never told you.

327
00:13:21,870 --> 00:13:22,870
You're a liar.

328
00:13:22,870 --> 00:13:25,770
I was trying to be fair to everyone.
Oh, dear.

329
00:13:25,770 --> 00:13:27,540
If you know everything, you'd know
that the numbers are wrong.

330
00:13:28,510 --> 00:13:29,580
Goodness.

331
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:32,510
I'm in trouble. What should I do?

332
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,180
How do I survive?

333
00:13:34,450 --> 00:13:36,680
As soon as I walked out,
he started coming at me.

334
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,450
He asked me what the code was.
I really didn't have the code.

335
00:13:39,650 --> 00:13:40,950
It felt so unfair.

336
00:13:40,950 --> 00:13:43,360
Of course, I'm the weapon dealer,

337
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:45,690
so I feel sorry for Maillard.

338
00:13:45,690 --> 00:13:48,660
Since he solved it the first day,
he knows the pattern...

339
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:50,730
and the content.
He said one code was missing.

340
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,800
That's how dangerous the situation is.

341
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,670
They'll discover my identity
when they find the last code.

342
00:13:55,970 --> 00:13:57,700
I felt really troubled.

343
00:13:57,970 --> 00:14:00,240
I've never had people
come at me like this before.

344
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,010
Of course, he was on the right page.
I really respect Maillard.

345
00:14:03,010 --> 00:14:04,010
But still,

346
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,310
I hope he would take it a little easy.

347
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,320
I told him to put him
in a conflicted position,

348
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,520
but he reacted emotionally.

349
00:14:12,590 --> 00:14:15,490
That could also be an act, though.
He's a smart person.

350
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:19,760
I'm going to tell the other leaders
tomorrow morning...

351
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,360
that I couldn't solve it...

352
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,830
because we don't have Vector's code.

353
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:28,840
I think Vector would need
to get some pressure...

354
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,400
from the other leaders about this.

355
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:32,010
They would question Black.

356
00:14:32,370 --> 00:14:35,710
But what kind of mission
does Black have...

357
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,340
that he's not telling us
even in that situation?

358
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:39,580
I shouldn't have given him my code.

359
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:43,320
It didn't cross my mind
that Black could use it.

360
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,720
That was my mistake.

361
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,090
If this results...

362
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:50,090
in a negative impact
on the whole community,

363
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:52,230
that means I played really badly today.

364
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,870
Black, this guy...

365
00:14:59,530 --> 00:15:00,730
Also,

366
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:04,300
Black had one life from the beginning.

367
00:15:05,370 --> 00:15:09,110
So I think that changes
our calculations a bit.

368
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,610
Team Blue may have had
more lives than we thought.

369
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:13,580
What led to all this?

370
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,050
I asked Black,

371
00:15:15,050 --> 00:15:19,320
"On the first day,
didn't you say you had enough lives..."

372
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,860
"to open the supermarket
to last us throughout the period?"

373
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:24,260
According to the rule now,

374
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,760
you can't participate
in the life-credit trades.

375
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,630
- I can't.
- So you have enough lives...

376
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:31,270
to last you through
the remaining days, right?

377
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:32,670
- That's right.
- Then...

378
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:33,800
(Vector lied to them
saying he had enough lives on Day One.)

379
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,240
He said he had no lives.

380
00:15:36,270 --> 00:15:39,010
Then the number of lives doesn't add up.

381
00:15:39,010 --> 00:15:41,110
Someone has more lives...

382
00:15:41,110 --> 00:15:42,240
That would be Blue.

383
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:44,680
They're pretending
they don't have that many lives.

384
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:46,910
Right now,

385
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:48,120
Team Blue has enough lives.

386
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:50,450
Black has only one life.

387
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:51,650
That's right.

388
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:54,790
He has no way to get more lives,
so he made a deal with Team Blue.

389
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:55,790
Right.

390
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,760
"I'll manipulate the information for you,"

391
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:00,590
"so give me one life."

392
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,460
We made...

393
00:16:02,630 --> 00:16:04,260
a black-market deal earlier.

394
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:06,570
We can't get anything in return for it,

395
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:07,940
and neither can he.

396
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:10,440
- It's gone?
- It's gone.

397
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:14,370
- Was it taken?
- Yes. It was useless.

398
00:16:14,370 --> 00:16:16,380
It's gone? What a waste.

399
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,610
I just put it in the market.

400
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:20,880
Team Blue might ask me about it tomorrow,

401
00:16:21,050 --> 00:16:23,220
so I'll just make something up.

402
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:26,590
It was destroyed because the system...

403
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:27,720
didn't recognize it as a valid life.

404
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,160
But it's safe in my room.

405
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:32,030
It's just there in the market.

406
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:33,530
It's like a trophy for me.

407
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,000
(The life from the black-market deal
still remains as Blue's resource.)

408
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:42,140
If Black is still wishy-washy tomorrow,

409
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:43,970
I'm going with White.

410
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:45,510
We're going to war, 9 to 3.

411
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:49,040
Then we should lay
the groundwork with White.

412
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,040
That's right.

413
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:51,710
Let's do that
if something seems off tomorrow.

414
00:16:52,250 --> 00:16:53,480
Without making any deals.

415
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,220
They'll issue more diamonds tomorrow.

416
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:57,650
They'll have them tomorrow.
We can take lots of weapons...

417
00:16:57,650 --> 00:16:59,020
- and teach Team Blue...
- Yes.

418
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,650
a lesson.

419
00:17:00,650 --> 00:17:03,190
We'll tell Vector to stay out of it.

420
00:17:03,190 --> 00:17:05,060
"The numbers have been off
from the start."

421
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:08,000
- We need to normalize things.
- Yes.

422
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:09,430
They're getting full of themselves.

423
00:17:09,430 --> 00:17:12,530
They can't keep doing this...

424
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:15,440
- when they have a lot of lives.
- They can't hide them anymore.

425
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:17,170
"Show us your cards."

426
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:20,910
And what I wanted to share with you...

427
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:23,780
is that Team Blue's bond...

428
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:25,910
isn't very strong.

429
00:17:25,910 --> 00:17:26,910
Right.

430
00:17:26,910 --> 00:17:28,720
Genie and Salt...

431
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:30,220
seem to have different ideas.

432
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:34,190
At least Salt feels indebted to us...

433
00:17:34,590 --> 00:17:36,290
- for everything we've given them.
- Right.

434
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:38,830
They'd know that they deceived us.

435
00:17:38,830 --> 00:17:40,730
We gave them many things
despite their deception,

436
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,030
so Genie and Pitou...

437
00:17:43,030 --> 00:17:45,200
might think they got lucky.

438
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,040
But Salt feels a little bad about it.

439
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:51,910
Also, they really know
the rules inside and out now.

440
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:56,080
They gave us many credits earlier...

441
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:58,250
and even went pollution-free.

442
00:17:58,450 --> 00:18:01,210
They're faithfully working
for the public good.

443
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:04,550
So if we want to play smart,

444
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,790
it could be wise to team up with Team Red.

445
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:09,360
What we've been talking about...

446
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:12,830
was that Team White is really powerful
and they also have a strong bond.

447
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:15,130
So it would be advantageous...

448
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:17,100
- Naturally.
- to go on a 9-to-3 battle.

449
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:19,630
But if we team up with Team Red,

450
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:20,900
go 6 against 6, and we win,

451
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:23,240
we'll take half their resources,

452
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,610
and three people
will have to be eliminated that day.

453
00:18:26,110 --> 00:18:30,110
It's a chance to cut Team White in half.

454
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:32,950
As the days go by,

455
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:36,820
there'll come a time when our lives
are no more than theirs.

456
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:39,790
Of course, they say they want
to go peacefully, but we can't trust them.

457
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:41,490
Team White's way of coexistence...

458
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:43,620
is basically just,
"Keep cutting down our lives."

459
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:46,460
There's no sacrifice on their part...

460
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,930
in their whole "We want peace" stance.

461
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,360
It's been, "We want peace,
give us your lives."

462
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,000
If Team White hasn't teamed up
with anyone yet,

463
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,470
we have to hurry.

464
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:57,440
Let's divide them.

465
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:00,170
The twin forces of desire.

466
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:03,310
One is obsessed with desire,

467
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:05,750
and the other is just plain crazy.

468
00:19:07,510 --> 00:19:09,920
What Team White keeps saying
is that they don't want war.

469
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:11,380
They want this to last
as long as possible.

470
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:13,690
The way to survive as long as possible...

471
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:16,460
is our continuous supply of lives.

472
00:19:16,690 --> 00:19:20,290
"You have to keep giving us
your lives for our coexistence."

473
00:19:20,290 --> 00:19:21,830
That's...

474
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:23,900
not an alliance.

475
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:26,400
This is just a colony.

476
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:28,670
We're like Team White's colony.

477
00:19:28,870 --> 00:19:30,900
We give them our lives,

478
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:32,410
and they build up their wealth.

479
00:19:32,410 --> 00:19:34,510
This is unacceptable.

480
00:19:34,510 --> 00:19:35,980
We might as well strike first.

481
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:38,040
Then we should persuade Team Red,
no matter what.

482
00:19:38,350 --> 00:19:40,980
It seemed like a lot had been discussed...

483
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:43,820
while I was at the leader negotiation.

484
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,320
So they had already decided...

485
00:19:45,990 --> 00:19:49,360
that although we made
an alliance with Team White today,

486
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:52,730
we'll end up getting eliminated anyway.

487
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:55,260
Whether it turns into
an every-man-for-himself fight later...

488
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:58,000
or starts as early as tomorrow,
it's going to get pretty brutal.

489
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:01,570
War is the last thing I want,

490
00:20:01,570 --> 00:20:04,500
but if someone picks a fight with us,
we should just have fun with it.

491
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,670
If the other teams start the fight,

492
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:08,740
(Salt, Writer)

493
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:12,550
we can't just give them everything
to stop the war.

494
00:20:12,550 --> 00:20:14,180
We should protect what we can.

495
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:20,520
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

496
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:23,690
(4. Peace on the Trigger)

497
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:26,390
Day Three has begun.

498
00:20:26,390 --> 00:20:27,390
(Day 3)

499
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,060
Let's go!

500
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:40,610
(Town Hall)

501
00:20:46,150 --> 00:20:50,080
(A weapon dealer's morning
starts with eavesdropping)

502
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:51,990
I'll put in the other two.

503
00:20:51,990 --> 00:20:53,690
- Sounds good. Let's share it.
- Okay.

504
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:55,220
They're dividing up the food.

505
00:20:55,990 --> 00:20:57,260
All right.

506
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:00,290
We have six eggs,

507
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:02,760
so that's one egg per person.

508
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,130
We just have to decide when to have it.

509
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:06,370
Good thing there are six.

510
00:21:07,070 --> 00:21:08,840
- Good call buying three.
- I know.

511
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:10,540
This is just enough
to get us through today.

512
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,670
A bite of bread,

513
00:21:11,670 --> 00:21:12,810
one egg,

514
00:21:12,910 --> 00:21:14,270
- and one dumpling each.
- One dumpling each.

515
00:21:14,270 --> 00:21:16,880
How should we divide them
between the three meals?

516
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,750
Aren't there 12 dumplings?

517
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:20,350
There are 12, so we can have 2 each.

518
00:21:20,450 --> 00:21:22,220
Right, two each.

519
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:24,150
- One or two makes such a big difference.
- Of course.

520
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:25,820
- Psychologically, I mean.
- One dumpling...

521
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:26,990
feels too stingy.

522
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:29,160
Sorry, I'm still half asleep.

523
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:31,490
- But we can't eat all of this today.
- No.

524
00:21:31,490 --> 00:21:33,290
- It has to last through tomorrow.
- Right.

525
00:21:33,290 --> 00:21:35,800
We can't go to the supermarket
tomorrow morning, right?

526
00:21:35,930 --> 00:21:37,800
- It opens at lunch.
- We went at lunchtime before.

527
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:42,540
But at today's leader negotiation,

528
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:44,370
even if we have to twist their arm,

529
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:47,040
we have to make them give us a life.

530
00:21:47,210 --> 00:21:50,310
We can get through today, but later?
What about tomorrow?

531
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:52,450
The condition is far from being ideal.

532
00:21:52,950 --> 00:21:55,120
We have to open the supermarket.

533
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:59,320
Team Blue absolutely has to give
one life to the supermarket.

534
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:00,790
And...

535
00:22:00,850 --> 00:22:02,190
the second I woke up,

536
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:04,360
this thought hit me.

537
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:08,060
Before we declare war,
we should go to Team Red.

538
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,030
If they're going to go to war anyway,

539
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:12,370
wouldn't it be better to lose less...

540
00:22:12,370 --> 00:22:14,130
of our actual prize money?

541
00:22:14,130 --> 00:22:16,570
If we say we'll devalue our currency,

542
00:22:16,570 --> 00:22:17,870
then naturally,

543
00:22:17,870 --> 00:22:19,710
it will inevitably look like an alliance.

544
00:22:19,810 --> 00:22:21,710
That would be a huge loss for me.

545
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:24,680
I need to bring up
something a little uncomfortable.

546
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:27,210
I think we need rules of war, too.

547
00:22:27,210 --> 00:22:28,520
Before we go to war,

548
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:30,820
we should set a red line.

549
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:32,520
If they cross it,

550
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:34,220
then we have no choice. It is war.

551
00:22:34,250 --> 00:22:37,020
We should decide on a line
we absolutely will not let them cross...

552
00:22:37,020 --> 00:22:38,590
and tell them in advance.

553
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:39,730
That sounds good.

554
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,530
We cannot lose the majority.

555
00:22:41,530 --> 00:22:43,060
We need at least three people.

556
00:22:43,060 --> 00:22:44,100
- Right.
- Two?

557
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:46,100
I was also thinking minus two lives.

558
00:22:46,170 --> 00:22:47,870
If they kill two members of Team White,

559
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:49,570
it is war.

560
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:54,010
(Wiretap: Team Red's dormitory)

561
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:55,980
- But what if today...
- Yes.

562
00:22:56,210 --> 00:22:59,010
war is the better choice?

563
00:22:59,050 --> 00:23:00,380
Would you be willing to do it?

564
00:23:00,450 --> 00:23:02,850
What if Team Blue actually...

565
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:05,420
has more lives hidden away?
We count eight right now,

566
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:06,750
- but maybe they have around 20?
- Right.

567
00:23:06,850 --> 00:23:08,560
Then we should stage a revolution.

568
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:11,360
I should eat an egg.

569
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,830
Yes, eat one. You need to.

570
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:14,730
We need to prepare well,

571
00:23:14,730 --> 00:23:16,600
go in at our absolute best,

572
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:17,730
and answer them all correctly.

573
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:22,240
Assuming they produced nothing yesterday,

574
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:23,640
do they have eight right now?

575
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,040
- That is my estimate.
- Yes.

576
00:23:25,270 --> 00:23:27,910
- They probably got four right.
- Then...

577
00:23:27,910 --> 00:23:31,040
they could have around 14 to 16.

578
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,480
Goodness, 14 is right. That is incredible.

579
00:23:36,280 --> 00:23:38,650
Team leaders can now be changed...

580
00:23:38,650 --> 00:23:41,220
at the Community Center.

581
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:43,390
- I think...
- Yes.

582
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,790
he's doing a great job.

583
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:47,230
Should we reappoint him permanently?

584
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:48,630
Let us make his appointment permanent.

585
00:23:48,630 --> 00:23:50,130
- Do not.
- No, but right now,

586
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:52,270
this is our team's overall approach.

587
00:23:52,270 --> 00:23:54,070
- If we suddenly change the leader,
- Right.

588
00:23:54,070 --> 00:23:55,470
- we could be completely overpowered.
- Yes.

589
00:23:55,570 --> 00:23:59,310
Different times require different leaders.

590
00:23:59,310 --> 00:24:01,940
War could start at the slightest spark.

591
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,810
- Like Trump's second term...
- Yes.

592
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:06,150
Make Red Great Again.

593
00:24:07,650 --> 00:24:08,920
So we need...

594
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:10,750
a strong leader for this era.

595
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:12,890
- Maillard.
- Maillard.

596
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:15,760
I wonder who Team Blue's leader is today.

597
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:18,120
If they take turns, it should be Pitou.

598
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:20,430
They need a strong leader, too.

599
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:22,030
I wonder about Team Blue.

600
00:24:22,030 --> 00:24:23,600
(Salt, Genie, Pitou)

601
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:24,960
You are the leader today.

602
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:26,330
Would you like to lead one more day?

603
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,440
One more day?

604
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,340
No, not today.

605
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:32,810
I think we should try someone else.

606
00:24:33,770 --> 00:24:35,980
What I really want to know is...

607
00:24:36,080 --> 00:24:39,450
- say the three of us have to vote.
- Yes.

608
00:24:39,450 --> 00:24:42,050
Would two votes guarantee a win?

609
00:24:42,220 --> 00:24:44,180
- There are only three of us.
- Yes.

610
00:24:44,180 --> 00:24:47,090
Okay, let us keep one leader throughout.

611
00:24:47,090 --> 00:24:49,860
How do three people vote in secret?

612
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:52,690
Is there any point? Can we just decide?

613
00:24:52,690 --> 00:24:54,890
Will they not just tell us to decide?

614
00:24:55,730 --> 00:24:57,400
I will be the leader.

615
00:24:58,300 --> 00:24:59,700
We say this,

616
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:01,230
but when we vote,

617
00:25:01,230 --> 00:25:03,500
with two votes, it will be you anyway.

618
00:25:03,570 --> 00:25:06,140
Then we will say, "Let us just vote..."

619
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:08,170
I will say I am stepping out.

620
00:25:08,410 --> 00:25:09,680
- Then I will pretend...
- You...

621
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:11,040
I cannot choose between you.

622
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:12,450
That is fine with me.

623
00:25:14,050 --> 00:25:15,650
As for Genie,

624
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,050
on the first day,

625
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,850
she did not share anything with us.

626
00:25:20,220 --> 00:25:21,690
We were not told we could assign lives...

627
00:25:21,750 --> 00:25:23,090
or that the leader could ultimately...

628
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:25,190
decide who lives and who dies.

629
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:27,030
None of that was shared on Day One.

630
00:25:27,260 --> 00:25:28,930
I felt uneasy.

631
00:25:28,930 --> 00:25:30,900
I thought it would happen near the end.

632
00:25:30,930 --> 00:25:32,400
Actually, not even that late.

633
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:34,330
Maybe around Day 6 or 7,

634
00:25:34,330 --> 00:25:36,140
she might abandon us.

635
00:25:36,340 --> 00:25:37,540
I still worry about that.

636
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:41,410
I did not know the leader...

637
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:44,680
held that kind of power
over life and death.

638
00:25:44,740 --> 00:25:46,880
All of that made me think...

639
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,720
we should...

640
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:50,550
keep Genie in check,

641
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:56,660
and Pitou and I kept agreeing on that.

642
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:59,360
Things are fine. Why change now?

643
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,360
(Team Blue leader change)

644
00:26:00,630 --> 00:26:01,960
Salt will hand leadership...

645
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:03,700
over to Pitou.

646
00:26:04,260 --> 00:26:06,070
(Pitou)

647
00:26:06,070 --> 00:26:07,430
(Team Blue's leader: Pitou)

648
00:26:07,430 --> 00:26:08,770
Why did you do this?

649
00:26:09,470 --> 00:26:10,640
This was originally...

650
00:26:10,700 --> 00:26:12,870
The leader change is complete.

651
00:26:13,810 --> 00:26:15,640
Will you not be exhausted?

652
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:17,040
No, I am fine.

653
00:26:17,180 --> 00:26:19,480
Do not worry. I will be tired today.

654
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:22,380
Please make sure we survive to the end.

655
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:24,280
Please help us win a large prize.

656
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:28,920
Then let us vote on reappointing
our leader.

657
00:26:29,290 --> 00:26:32,130
I mentioned this before.

658
00:26:32,130 --> 00:26:33,790
I did want to give it a try.

659
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:36,760
The reason I did not step up yesterday...

660
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,670
was because you are doing so well.

661
00:26:38,970 --> 00:26:42,570
I thought I could serve in other areas.

662
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:45,640
So I saw no need to change our leader yet.

663
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,510
Let us keep it this way,

664
00:26:47,510 --> 00:26:50,010
but if one person leads for too long,

665
00:26:50,110 --> 00:26:54,280
they may monopolize information,
and other side effects could arise.

666
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:56,480
I saw Team Blue rotating leaders,

667
00:26:56,580 --> 00:27:00,520
so I thought we should take turns too.

668
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:04,320
But rotating like Team Blue...

669
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:05,460
actually seems riskier to me.

670
00:27:05,460 --> 00:27:08,160
Reappointing could show...

671
00:27:08,260 --> 00:27:09,630
- a strong unity within our team.
- That could...

672
00:27:09,630 --> 00:27:11,300
- be a good indicator too.
- Yes.

673
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:15,130
- It would show that we all agree.
- That is right.

674
00:27:15,130 --> 00:27:17,670
- Did you not want to be a leader before?
- For me,

675
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:19,010
that feeling is completely gone.

676
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:21,510
It is simple. I really like it now.

677
00:27:21,510 --> 00:27:23,510
- I really like it.
- You are a very compelling character.

678
00:27:23,510 --> 00:27:25,680
- I like it this way.
- Anyway, let us discuss it later.

679
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:26,750
- Okay.
- We have plenty of time today.

680
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:27,880
- Good.
- That sounds good.

681
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:30,420
It would be good to talk now, though.

682
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:31,520
Would you like to go see them now?

683
00:27:31,620 --> 00:27:32,990
Let's go for now.

684
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:34,820
We can just knock and talk to them.

685
00:27:36,620 --> 00:27:38,120
- Yes?
- Yes?

686
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:39,690
Is that Team Blue?

687
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:41,860
Coming!

688
00:27:43,860 --> 00:27:45,330
Could we...

689
00:27:45,730 --> 00:27:48,030
- Wait... All of us?
- Yes.

690
00:27:48,470 --> 00:27:49,540
Team Blue is here.

691
00:27:49,540 --> 00:27:51,170
- Could we talk for a moment?
- Yes.

692
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,610
- Hello.
- Hello.

693
00:27:53,610 --> 00:27:54,810
- This is...
- Hello.

694
00:27:54,810 --> 00:27:56,180
Did your leader just get to continue?

695
00:27:56,340 --> 00:27:58,310
- Yes.
- Yes. He's in power permanently.

696
00:27:59,050 --> 00:28:00,210
- Yes.
- Good.

697
00:28:00,210 --> 00:28:01,250
Are you on your way to
the Community Center?

698
00:28:01,250 --> 00:28:02,680
We are pretending to head there.

699
00:28:04,380 --> 00:28:05,520
- That makes it...
- Yes.

700
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:08,150
- look less suspicious...
- It seems like a natural encounter.

701
00:28:08,690 --> 00:28:09,690
- May I ask...
- Yes.

702
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:11,590
- Let me ask you directly.
- Yes.

703
00:28:11,590 --> 00:28:13,690
Are you considering going to war?

704
00:28:14,490 --> 00:28:17,500
- Only if we run out of lives.
- If you run out.

705
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:19,330
It would have to be our last resort.

706
00:28:19,700 --> 00:28:21,330
Against us?

707
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,570
We have the fewest lives.

708
00:28:22,570 --> 00:28:24,840
What we originally discussed was...

709
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:27,110
an alliance with Team White.

710
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:31,010
That was basically what we discussed
yesterday.

711
00:28:31,010 --> 00:28:33,880
But we have given it more thought.

712
00:28:34,010 --> 00:28:36,720
Team White simply has too many people.

713
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:39,050
They are simply too powerful as they are.

714
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:41,890
And the resources we issue...

715
00:28:41,890 --> 00:28:43,790
can always be issued again,

716
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:46,530
but we can never issue diamonds.

717
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:48,430
Team White has a monopoly.

718
00:28:48,530 --> 00:28:50,630
Structurally, that means...

719
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:52,930
we need to form a coalition
to check them...

720
00:28:53,170 --> 00:28:55,640
and cut their power in half.

721
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:56,970
That is what I started to think.

722
00:28:56,970 --> 00:28:59,040
- Even split it three, three, three.
- So...

723
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:00,810
if this alliance is solid,

724
00:29:00,810 --> 00:29:03,380
then when we trade lives,

725
00:29:03,380 --> 00:29:07,110
we should consider Team Red first.

726
00:29:07,110 --> 00:29:08,380
They have many people to feed.

727
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:09,920
- They do.
- They have so many people.

728
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:11,750
- They are bound to be hungry.
- We need to reduce their numbers.

729
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:14,190
And if everyone is to survive,

730
00:29:14,190 --> 00:29:18,490
could Team Blue help to open
the supermarket?

731
00:29:18,490 --> 00:29:20,330
- Of course.
- But I also think...

732
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:21,760
we should...

733
00:29:21,830 --> 00:29:24,300
reduce their numbers first,

734
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:26,370
- and then think it over.
- Yes.

735
00:29:26,730 --> 00:29:28,740
For now,

736
00:29:28,970 --> 00:29:32,270
we agree on reducing Team White's numbers.

737
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,610
- Okay.
- And...

738
00:29:33,610 --> 00:29:36,980
if we cannot secure enough lives
within the next day or two,

739
00:29:36,980 --> 00:29:41,280
- we saw war as our only option.
- Right.

740
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:44,850
We agree with what you have said.

741
00:29:45,420 --> 00:29:46,690
As for Team Red,

742
00:29:46,690 --> 00:29:48,290
honestly, if war breaks out,

743
00:29:48,290 --> 00:29:49,790
we do not have much to lose.

744
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:51,690
We have few resources others would want.

745
00:29:51,760 --> 00:29:54,590
We would rather not lead a war.

746
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:56,660
We would rather join an alliance.

747
00:29:56,660 --> 00:29:59,130
So Team Blue reaching out first...

748
00:29:59,130 --> 00:30:00,770
works in our favor.

749
00:30:00,930 --> 00:30:03,970
Team Blue also feels pressure to wage war.

750
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:06,640
But I still think that even in a war,

751
00:30:06,710 --> 00:30:08,610
even if we are outnumbered,

752
00:30:08,670 --> 00:30:11,080
our team could still win.

753
00:30:11,140 --> 00:30:14,350
So I think this is definitely a rule
worth considering.

754
00:30:15,050 --> 00:30:16,320
We will go to war?

755
00:30:17,350 --> 00:30:18,950
Team Blue must be feeling pressured.

756
00:30:19,490 --> 00:30:21,820
We need to develop the bomb.
Coming up with the technology...

757
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:23,660
- is what we need.
- We have to hurry.

758
00:30:23,660 --> 00:30:25,660
- Can we solve the skill question?
- Even just this one.

759
00:30:25,660 --> 00:30:27,030
- Shall I submit it and come back?
- What is it?

760
00:30:27,030 --> 00:30:28,230
It says "New Deal policy."

761
00:30:28,230 --> 00:30:30,330
- I think "New Deal policy" is wrong.
- Right.

762
00:30:30,330 --> 00:30:31,660
I will submit it and bring it back.

763
00:30:31,660 --> 00:30:32,700
It should work now, right?

764
00:30:49,420 --> 00:30:51,150
- Are you going to solve the question?
- Yes.

765
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:53,850
- But right now...
- Yes.

766
00:30:54,090 --> 00:30:55,220
Come over here.

767
00:30:56,690 --> 00:30:58,660
- Things are going very badly.
- Why?

768
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:00,660
Our codes were exposed.

769
00:31:01,530 --> 00:31:03,600
- We need to keep the secret hidden.
- Yes.

770
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:05,400
We need to sabotage things
as much as we can.

771
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:07,570
- Here is what happens.
- Yes.

772
00:31:07,570 --> 00:31:09,400
All the prize money we earned disappears.

773
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,040
- Our prize money disappears?
- Yes.

774
00:31:12,170 --> 00:31:13,370
- I understand.
- Every bit of it.

775
00:31:14,870 --> 00:31:17,280
(Day 1 Resident Registration)

776
00:31:17,610 --> 00:31:21,410
Please check your values code as well.

777
00:31:25,620 --> 00:31:29,120
These instructions are for Donkey only.

778
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:33,760
You were assigned to Red,

779
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:36,430
but you are actually Black's ally.

780
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:41,570
For details, check the rule card
in the central box,

781
00:31:41,570 --> 00:31:44,470
destroy it, and return it.

782
00:31:44,470 --> 00:31:45,870
(Ally's Rule)

783
00:31:55,450 --> 00:31:59,090
Your true role is
the weapon dealer's ally.

784
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:02,490
The ally must approach
the weapon dealer...

785
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:06,160
and ask,
"In war, what is sacrificed first?"

786
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:07,660
Then...

787
00:32:07,660 --> 00:32:10,230
you must hear the answer, "Truth."

788
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:14,500
(Day 1 Evening)

789
00:32:14,500 --> 00:32:15,900
Then this is...

790
00:32:28,810 --> 00:32:30,650
- Vector, one moment, please.
- Yes.

791
00:32:32,150 --> 00:32:35,920
In war, what is sacrificed first?

792
00:32:36,090 --> 00:32:37,320
Truth.

793
00:32:37,620 --> 00:32:38,790
Understood.

794
00:32:39,530 --> 00:32:40,960
- I look forward to working with you.
- Yes.

795
00:32:42,930 --> 00:32:46,870
The ally can only earn prize money...

796
00:32:46,870 --> 00:32:48,800
from war fees and weapon sales.

797
00:32:49,970 --> 00:32:52,100
After all activities end,

798
00:32:52,100 --> 00:32:54,310
the ally and weapon dealer will agree...

799
00:32:54,310 --> 00:32:56,440
on how to split the final prize.

800
00:32:56,940 --> 00:32:59,680
However, if the ally is eliminated,

801
00:32:59,680 --> 00:33:03,480
the weapon dealer's final prize is halved.

802
00:33:03,850 --> 00:33:05,790
The ally's role is to help Black...

803
00:33:05,790 --> 00:33:08,350
make the other teams fight
as much as possible...

804
00:33:08,350 --> 00:33:10,990
and help Black take as much...

805
00:33:10,990 --> 00:33:14,130
of the resulting profit as possible.

806
00:33:14,830 --> 00:33:18,030
It looks like we will fight Team Blue.

807
00:33:18,030 --> 00:33:20,200
Do we take half of what they have?

808
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:22,400
If we win, it is a revolution. We get 11.

809
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:23,470
That is impressive.

810
00:33:23,470 --> 00:33:25,240
See? War is worth considering.

811
00:33:26,540 --> 00:33:27,810
Did you see the war fee?

812
00:33:27,810 --> 00:33:29,380
Yes. Was it 15?

813
00:33:29,380 --> 00:33:30,380
It seemed reasonable.

814
00:33:30,380 --> 00:33:32,240
The war fee was much lower than expected.

815
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:34,480
- Today is not a bad day.
- Right. Shall we start one now?

816
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:36,080
Because if trade keeps declining...

817
00:33:37,020 --> 00:33:39,020
For the ally, war is definitely...

818
00:33:39,020 --> 00:33:41,420
the better outcome.

819
00:33:41,420 --> 00:33:44,260
So Maillard calling for war...

820
00:33:44,260 --> 00:33:45,860
is actually good for me.

821
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:47,760
Someone belongs to two teams?

822
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:52,700
Could there be someone like that on Black?

823
00:33:52,700 --> 00:33:54,000
Team Black?

824
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,640
- Part of Team Black...
- And part of Team White?

825
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:58,940
So they are completely neutral.

826
00:33:59,070 --> 00:34:00,340
- An ally.
- Right.

827
00:34:00,340 --> 00:34:01,370
- Right.
- Right.

828
00:34:01,370 --> 00:34:03,180
This person is clearly on another team...

829
00:34:04,040 --> 00:34:05,510
But from what I can tell,

830
00:34:05,510 --> 00:34:08,250
Maillard seems a little suspicious of me.

831
00:34:08,350 --> 00:34:10,580
Is he just testing me, or did he...

832
00:34:10,580 --> 00:34:13,620
notice something? That concerns me.

833
00:34:13,790 --> 00:34:15,590
For now, I need to build his trust.

834
00:34:15,890 --> 00:34:19,630
Do you know the condition
for Team Red to start a war?

835
00:34:19,630 --> 00:34:22,560
Team Blue seems to want to start a war.

836
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:24,030
- Team Blue does? Against whom?
- Yes.

837
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,730
They want to attack Team White,

838
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:27,430
since they have a lot of members,

839
00:34:27,430 --> 00:34:29,440
- by joining forces with Team Red.
- They want to reduce their numbers.

840
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:30,740
They want to eliminate a few from White.

841
00:34:30,740 --> 00:34:33,640
That would reduce the lives they need.

842
00:34:33,940 --> 00:34:35,070
That is their plan.

843
00:34:35,070 --> 00:34:37,610
I think war will break out
today or tomorrow.

844
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:38,710
- Okay.
- Yes.

845
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:40,080
Shall we talk on the way down?

846
00:34:40,080 --> 00:34:41,250
- I will go down first.
- All right.

847
00:34:54,030 --> 00:34:55,630
- So right now...
- Yes.

848
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:58,830
- exposing the codes is risky.
- Yes.

849
00:34:58,830 --> 00:35:01,830
We need to cause as many wars as possible.

850
00:35:01,830 --> 00:35:04,170
- They will suspect me now, so Donkey...
- Yes.

851
00:35:04,170 --> 00:35:06,270
- Understood. By the way,
- Please help me as much as you can.

852
00:35:06,270 --> 00:35:08,170
is there a way you can be eliminated?

853
00:35:08,170 --> 00:35:10,680
- I actually cannot be eliminated.
- You cannot?

854
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:12,410
- But you can be eliminated.
- Right.

855
00:35:12,410 --> 00:35:14,310
I have to keep you alive.

856
00:35:14,410 --> 00:35:16,350
- What I would like to suggest is...
- Yes.

857
00:35:16,350 --> 00:35:19,820
if I can keep Team Red alive
to the end, I...

858
00:35:19,820 --> 00:35:22,250
- I have no choice but to save them.
- Yes.

859
00:35:22,250 --> 00:35:25,360
Saving you alone is highly unlikely.

860
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:27,330
- I understand.
- We are short on time, so hurry.

861
00:35:27,330 --> 00:35:28,430
- We need to do this.
- All right.

862
00:35:28,860 --> 00:35:33,070
I also have my teammates' codes.

863
00:35:33,070 --> 00:35:35,470
If we ever need to use them...

864
00:35:35,670 --> 00:35:38,770
- Can you tell me the codes?
- But I would rather you not...

865
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:41,640
use them right away.

866
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:42,940
- I will just keep them in mind.
- All right.

867
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:45,110
- Whose? Maillard's?
- Maillard's.

868
00:35:45,640 --> 00:35:47,280
It is U2. U2.

869
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:48,450
What about the other person?

870
00:35:48,510 --> 00:35:51,420
I think Izaha's was SM.

871
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:53,620
- I do not remember the number exactly.
- Okay.

872
00:35:53,850 --> 00:35:55,190
- Thank you.
- Of course.

873
00:35:55,450 --> 00:35:57,620
Maillard and Izaha...

874
00:35:57,620 --> 00:35:59,390
do not take very good care
of their notebooks.

875
00:35:59,390 --> 00:36:01,230
So I felt safe enough...

876
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:03,200
to look at theirs.

877
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:05,660
(Donkey, stand-up comedian)

878
00:36:05,660 --> 00:36:07,170
What I told him when I shared them was...

879
00:36:07,170 --> 00:36:09,300
not to hurt them for now.

880
00:36:09,300 --> 00:36:12,370
They matter to me,
so leave them alone for now.

881
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:13,610
At the decisive moment,

882
00:36:13,610 --> 00:36:16,680
I think Vector will use that information.

883
00:36:16,680 --> 00:36:17,910
I will get going.

884
00:36:17,910 --> 00:36:19,080
- Good luck.
- Good luck.

885
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:20,750
I will make sure you get a large prize.

886
00:36:21,550 --> 00:36:24,480
Let us try to encourage a war today.

887
00:36:24,480 --> 00:36:25,550
Okay.

888
00:36:29,390 --> 00:36:30,520
I am back.

889
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:34,030
- It was occupied the whole time,
- Yes, okay.

890
00:36:34,030 --> 00:36:35,060
so I waited.

891
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,260
Who was in there?

892
00:36:36,260 --> 00:36:37,500
Black was there.

893
00:36:37,500 --> 00:36:39,400
Fine. Let him take everything for himself.

894
00:36:45,940 --> 00:36:49,210
Today's production activity
will begin shortly.

895
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:51,540
Today's production keyword is...

896
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:54,150
Truth in the Blanks.

897
00:36:54,710 --> 00:36:56,720
What is "Truth in the Blanks"?

898
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,520
Truth in the Blanks.

899
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:01,020
I guess we have to fill in the blanks.

900
00:37:01,690 --> 00:37:04,360
Skill development is also underway.

901
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:06,890
Teams that decode
the skill development code...

902
00:37:07,430 --> 00:37:10,000
must visit
during Community Center hours...

903
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:12,400
and tag their answer sheet.

904
00:37:13,230 --> 00:37:16,040
The rest can solve
the skill questions here.

905
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:17,400
Should we split evenly or unevenly?

906
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:20,070
- Splitting evenly seems risky.
- Right.

907
00:37:20,070 --> 00:37:22,470
- How about 4 to 2?
- I think either 1 to 5 or 4 to 2.

908
00:37:22,470 --> 00:37:24,210
- With 1 to 5, one person is too isolated.
- Right.

909
00:37:24,210 --> 00:37:26,780
- How about 2 to 4?
- Could I be one of the 4?

910
00:37:26,780 --> 00:37:29,950
If we solve the skill question,
I do not think I will be much help.

911
00:37:29,950 --> 00:37:31,150
Does the leader have to be there?

912
00:37:31,150 --> 00:37:33,120
- They never said that.
- That is not required, right?

913
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:34,790
- Then two people stay here?
- Yes.

914
00:37:34,790 --> 00:37:36,260
(Production: Leia, Siseon, Boss, Hamlet
Skill development: Luna, Paul)

915
00:37:37,560 --> 00:37:39,460
Now that I know, going down is scarier.

916
00:37:39,460 --> 00:37:40,730
This weighs heavily on me.

917
00:37:41,260 --> 00:37:42,800
Let us accomplish as much as we can.

918
00:37:43,630 --> 00:37:46,130
Welcome to the production site.

919
00:37:46,170 --> 00:37:48,600
- Please take your seats.
- All right.

920
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:49,670
You brought the credit, right?

921
00:37:49,670 --> 00:37:52,000
Before production, Team Blue...

922
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:54,610
will be told the total life supply.

923
00:37:54,610 --> 00:37:57,010
The remaining lives...
How many did they mine yesterday?

924
00:37:57,010 --> 00:37:58,340
- We can see it now.
- We need to calculate it.

925
00:37:58,580 --> 00:38:03,480
There are currently 43 lives in total.

926
00:38:03,950 --> 00:38:06,450
Then they barely produced any lives.

927
00:38:07,820 --> 00:38:10,320
- So the number we know is basically...
- Right.

928
00:38:10,660 --> 00:38:11,990
- almost exactly right.
- Yes.

929
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:14,960
That was exactly the number I expected.

930
00:38:14,960 --> 00:38:18,360
Team Red mined credits that day,

931
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:21,100
so only Team White would have mined lives.

932
00:38:21,430 --> 00:38:23,840
I thought they mined two at best.

933
00:38:23,840 --> 00:38:26,540
Exactly two were gone besides ours.

934
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:29,010
The total of 43 means...

935
00:38:29,010 --> 00:38:33,010
that when we are competing for the share,
we are bound to take the majority.

936
00:38:33,010 --> 00:38:35,480
But we will always be the majority here.

937
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:37,020
If we still fail to do our part,

938
00:38:37,980 --> 00:38:40,220
it could ultimately end...

939
00:38:40,590 --> 00:38:42,820
in the worst case of mutual destruction.

940
00:38:43,120 --> 00:38:46,330
- I think we can spend more credits today.
- We can.

941
00:38:46,330 --> 00:38:48,990
We should spend as many as we can.

942
00:38:48,990 --> 00:38:51,500
True, but if we think only of us,

943
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:53,530
we also have to think about
tomorrow and the next day.

944
00:38:53,530 --> 00:38:54,830
- Since they are not going...
- Right.

945
00:38:54,830 --> 00:38:56,170
to produce credits,

946
00:38:56,170 --> 00:38:58,400
- spending too many ourselves is risky.
- They are not producing credits either.

947
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:00,740
Right. They are not producing any,
but they gave us this.

948
00:39:01,010 --> 00:39:03,810
I appreciate it,
but we still need to use some of it.

949
00:39:03,810 --> 00:39:05,710
In any case, no more are being produced.

950
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:07,450
When we answer the quiz tomorrow...

951
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:09,650
for the common good,
we need credits left over.

952
00:39:09,650 --> 00:39:12,320
Of course we need some left.
We cannot spend them all.

953
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:15,590
But I think we can be fairly generous.

954
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:18,690
Once you choose the resource to produce,

955
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:20,830
ring the bell and state your choice.

956
00:39:20,860 --> 00:39:21,890
Lives.

957
00:39:21,890 --> 00:39:23,530
(Team Blue chooses lives)

958
00:39:23,660 --> 00:39:25,730
- We have to choose lives, right?
- Siseon, yes.

959
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:27,030
- Yes, for now.
- Of course.

960
00:39:27,030 --> 00:39:28,930
Lives, please.

961
00:39:29,900 --> 00:39:31,170
- Lives, right?
- Yes.

962
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:34,110
We will choose lives.

963
00:39:34,110 --> 00:39:35,270
(Team Red chooses lives)

964
00:39:35,270 --> 00:39:38,910
Please insert one credit
into the credit box.

965
00:39:39,780 --> 00:39:40,850
Good luck.

966
00:39:41,580 --> 00:39:43,550
Today's production activity is...

967
00:39:43,550 --> 00:39:46,250
- Truth in the Blanks.
- Truth in the Blanks.

968
00:39:46,250 --> 00:39:47,790
Truth in the Blanks.

969
00:39:47,790 --> 00:39:49,460
Here is the first question.

970
00:39:50,190 --> 00:39:52,620
"The Republic of Korea shall endeavor
to maintain international peace..."

971
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:54,760
"and shall renounce blank wars?

972
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:55,930
(Q1. From Chapter 1 of the Constitution,
what belongs in the blank?)

973
00:39:55,930 --> 00:39:57,200
(Art. 5.1. Korea shall seek global peace
and renounce blank wars.)

974
00:39:57,260 --> 00:39:58,400
It's the Constitution.

975
00:39:58,700 --> 00:40:01,570
Izaha studied the Constitution yesterday.

976
00:40:02,130 --> 00:40:05,300
I will memorize the whole Constitution.
"The rights and duties of citizens."

977
00:40:05,900 --> 00:40:08,910
"The rights and duties of citizens..."

978
00:40:08,910 --> 00:40:10,240
"and the right to pursue happiness."

979
00:40:10,380 --> 00:40:13,050
"Korea shall seek global peace."

980
00:40:13,050 --> 00:40:14,910
I think it'll be
something like "aggression."

981
00:40:15,550 --> 00:40:16,820
- Renounces all wars of aggression?
- That's it.

982
00:40:16,820 --> 00:40:19,320
That popped into my head too.
"Renounces all wars of aggression."

983
00:40:19,550 --> 00:40:22,820
- The answer is aggression.
- Aggression.

984
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:23,990
That is correct.

985
00:40:24,890 --> 00:40:26,160
Thank you so much.

986
00:40:26,490 --> 00:40:28,090
- Nice.
- Bring it.

987
00:40:28,330 --> 00:40:29,730
- It was worth the read.
- I'm impressed.

988
00:40:29,730 --> 00:40:31,400
- It was left in your subconscious mind.
- Right.

989
00:40:31,630 --> 00:40:33,370
There's your reason to read books.

990
00:40:33,900 --> 00:40:35,500
We could be facing a war soon,

991
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:36,800
so reading that gives me
a strange feeling.

992
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,770
- Wars of something.
- Yes, that.

993
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:40,710
- Wars of something.
- That must be it.

994
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:43,280
It renounces something like that.

995
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:44,280
Violence.

996
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:47,550
- But wars are naturally violent.
- Yes, they're violent.

997
00:40:47,550 --> 00:40:48,910
Chaotic wars?

998
00:40:48,910 --> 00:40:50,520
Is there any war that isn't chaotic?

999
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:51,650
Aggression.

1000
00:40:51,650 --> 00:40:53,190
"Aggression" sounds funny.

1001
00:40:53,190 --> 00:40:54,490
I know. It doesn't fit.

1002
00:40:54,490 --> 00:40:57,190
Violence does seem like
the opposite of peace.

1003
00:40:57,190 --> 00:40:59,090
- Violence.
- Should we just go with that?

1004
00:40:59,090 --> 00:41:00,960
Thinking more about it is only...

1005
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:03,430
- a waste of time at this point.
- Yes, let's save time.

1006
00:41:03,430 --> 00:41:05,460
- Go ahead.
- Renounces...

1007
00:41:05,460 --> 00:41:07,370
- all wars of violence.
- You sound so unsure.

1008
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:08,770
That is incorrect.

1009
00:41:08,770 --> 00:41:09,870
- Let's move on.
- Pass.

1010
00:41:09,870 --> 00:41:10,870
Pass.

1011
00:41:10,870 --> 00:41:12,200
Next question.

1012
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:13,670
Universal Declaration of Human Rights.

1013
00:41:13,670 --> 00:41:15,140
Excerpt of the translation.

1014
00:41:15,140 --> 00:41:17,680
(Article 3:
Everyone has the right to life, A, and B.)

1015
00:41:17,980 --> 00:41:19,610
Today's questions are tough.

1016
00:41:19,610 --> 00:41:21,250
(Article 3:
Everyone has the right to life, A, and B.)

1017
00:41:21,250 --> 00:41:22,950
Liberty.

1018
00:41:22,950 --> 00:41:24,620
- One was to be liberty, right?
- Yes.

1019
00:41:25,480 --> 00:41:27,590
Liberty has to be one of them, right?

1020
00:41:28,550 --> 00:41:30,390
The right to dignity?

1021
00:41:30,660 --> 00:41:31,760
Dignity sounds good.

1022
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:34,230
Everyone has the right to life,

1023
00:41:34,230 --> 00:41:36,860
- liberty, and dignity.
- And dignity.

1024
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:38,460
That is incorrect.

1025
00:41:38,460 --> 00:41:39,970
Okay, we'll pass.

1026
00:41:39,970 --> 00:41:41,630
Would a hint have made a difference?

1027
00:41:41,630 --> 00:41:43,470
I wonder what the hint would've been.

1028
00:41:43,470 --> 00:41:45,400
Would the hint be in English?

1029
00:41:45,900 --> 00:41:47,710
Then the answer will come right to you.

1030
00:41:48,170 --> 00:41:49,310
We'll take a hint.

1031
00:41:49,310 --> 00:41:50,310
(Team White and Team Red
trade in a credit for a hint.)

1032
00:41:50,310 --> 00:41:51,680
We'll take a hint.

1033
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:55,650
Please insert one credit
into the credit box.

1034
00:41:55,650 --> 00:41:57,220
Here's your hint.

1035
00:41:57,220 --> 00:41:59,520
(Everyone has the right
to life, A, and B.)

1036
00:41:59,820 --> 00:42:02,090
I was right. We got the English version.

1037
00:42:02,090 --> 00:42:06,360
"Right to life, liberty, and security..."

1038
00:42:06,730 --> 00:42:08,530
