00:50:05,970 --> 00:50:09,070
We'll go with protection and cooperation.

1289
00:50:09,410 --> 00:50:11,540
A is mercy,

1290
00:50:11,540 --> 00:50:13,510
and B is protection.

1291
00:50:13,510 --> 00:50:14,650
That is incorrect.

1292
00:50:15,710 --> 00:50:17,220
Should we take a hint?

1293
00:50:17,350 --> 00:50:19,720
Taking a hint and retrying
will cost us two credits.

1294
00:50:19,720 --> 00:50:22,350
We should only use a hint
before making our first attempt.

1295
00:50:22,590 --> 00:50:24,720
It's better to just retry twice.

1296
00:50:24,720 --> 00:50:26,320
Yes, you're right.

1297
00:50:26,590 --> 00:50:29,430
Protection and good faith.

1298
00:50:29,660 --> 00:50:30,700
That is incorrect.

1299
00:50:30,700 --> 00:50:31,730
(Incorrect)

1300
00:50:32,430 --> 00:50:34,100
Rather than having regrets,

1301
00:50:34,100 --> 00:50:35,870
- let's just go for it.
- Let's spend one.

1302
00:50:35,870 --> 00:50:37,540
This is why we got them
in the first place.

1303
00:50:38,070 --> 00:50:39,270
Protection and favor.

1304
00:50:39,270 --> 00:50:40,370
That is incorrect.

1305
00:50:40,710 --> 00:50:42,440
- Let's pass.
- Okay, pass.

1306
00:50:42,610 --> 00:50:44,210
Here's the correct answer.

1307
00:50:45,010 --> 00:50:48,450
- Seriously? Assistance.
- Assistance.

1308
00:50:49,180 --> 00:50:50,620
- That was a waste. What a bummer.
- Right.

1309
00:50:50,620 --> 00:50:52,620
- Still, we did our best.
- We tried our best.

1310
00:50:52,750 --> 00:50:54,790
- We did our best.
- The production activity is over.

1311
00:50:55,290 --> 00:50:57,190
- We did great. It was efficient.
- Nice job, guys.

1312
00:50:57,190 --> 00:50:58,390
- What a relief.
- We're the best.

1313
00:50:58,920 --> 00:51:01,360
Okay, we earned a life with seven credits.

1314
00:51:01,360 --> 00:51:02,590
- Good job, guys.
- Nicely done.

1315
00:51:06,060 --> 00:51:07,230
- Here we go.
- We're back.

1316
00:51:07,230 --> 00:51:08,670
Good job, guys!

1317
00:51:08,670 --> 00:51:10,370
- Did you do well?
- Hi.

1318
00:51:10,370 --> 00:51:12,240
- Here's how we did.
- Sure.

1319
00:51:13,370 --> 00:51:15,240
We earned two lives.

1320
00:51:15,270 --> 00:51:17,110
(They earned 2 lives
which was their goal.)

1321
00:51:17,110 --> 00:51:19,080
- And you didn't lose any.
- Good job, guys.

1322
00:51:19,080 --> 00:51:20,210
How were things back here?

1323
00:51:20,880 --> 00:51:22,910
We were still on the hunt for the answer.

1324
00:51:22,910 --> 00:51:23,920
- Right.
- The hunt?

1325
00:51:23,920 --> 00:51:26,250
We haven't found the right answer yet,

1326
00:51:26,550 --> 00:51:29,490
but this is what we came up with.

1327
00:51:29,490 --> 00:51:31,290
The reduction of reserved lives.

1328
00:51:31,590 --> 00:51:33,160
The reduction?

1329
00:51:33,730 --> 00:51:36,760
(While Team Production was producing)

1330
00:51:37,460 --> 00:51:40,270
(Oil reserves)

1331
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:43,900
(Paul thinks lives could be related
to oil reserves.)

1332
00:51:44,070 --> 00:51:46,640
Here's a thought that just came to me.

1333
00:51:46,640 --> 00:51:49,010
- This relates to skill development,
- Right.

1334
00:51:49,270 --> 00:51:51,580
and solving this question opens the lock.

1335
00:51:51,580 --> 00:51:53,110
Assuming oil represents lives,

1336
00:51:53,750 --> 00:51:54,980
oil reserves are equivalent...

1337
00:51:54,980 --> 00:51:56,010
- to reserved lives.
- Right.

1338
00:51:56,410 --> 00:51:58,020
Following that logic,

1339
00:51:58,020 --> 00:52:01,090
anything related to reserved lives
could change.

1340
00:52:01,090 --> 00:52:02,590
- That could be it.
- I might be wrong,

1341
00:52:02,590 --> 00:52:04,090
but I'm just throwing it out there.

1342
00:52:04,560 --> 00:52:07,760
Acquiring the skill benefits our team,

1343
00:52:07,960 --> 00:52:11,500
but it's also going to put
our selfishness...

1344
00:52:11,500 --> 00:52:13,430
and community peace to the test.

1345
00:52:13,700 --> 00:52:16,800
Taking all of that into account,
I guess the answer will lean...

1346
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:18,270
toward the negative.

1347
00:52:18,540 --> 00:52:20,910
- So...
- We gain a massive advantage,

1348
00:52:20,910 --> 00:52:22,410
- That's right.
- but it'll also drop a disaster...

1349
00:52:22,410 --> 00:52:23,680
right into our laps.

1350
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:27,550
What will affect us all,
regardless of teams,

1351
00:52:27,550 --> 00:52:28,610
is the reserved lives.

1352
00:52:28,750 --> 00:52:30,150
Then we're caught in a dilemma.

1353
00:52:30,150 --> 00:52:32,850
We all have a nuclear button, right?

1354
00:52:32,850 --> 00:52:34,490
It's a classic prisoner's dilemma.

1355
00:52:34,990 --> 00:52:36,220
If everyone hits the button, we all die,

1356
00:52:36,220 --> 00:52:37,990
- but we benefit from pressing it first.
- Right.

1357
00:52:38,160 --> 00:52:39,890
Someone will choose to press it.

1358
00:52:40,130 --> 00:52:43,230
For that reason, we should look
at a truce as a suppression tactic...

1359
00:52:43,390 --> 00:52:44,700
- We should.
- and agree not to press our buttons.

1360
00:52:44,700 --> 00:52:46,660
- We should at least discuss it.
- Right.

1361
00:52:47,030 --> 00:52:50,000
- Hold on.
- Wait, I think we need a plan.

1362
00:52:50,140 --> 00:52:52,170
We have 14 lives right now.

1363
00:52:52,170 --> 00:52:55,740
Are we agreeing not to share any
with Team White?

1364
00:52:55,740 --> 00:52:58,640
Why don't we just tell them
we only earned three today?

1365
00:52:58,640 --> 00:53:02,210
Team Red could request three lives.

1366
00:53:02,450 --> 00:53:04,520
Even if we give them three...

1367
00:53:04,520 --> 00:53:06,890
- I think that's acceptable.
- I'm fine with that.

1368
00:53:06,890 --> 00:53:08,890
We'll share with Team Red.

1369
00:53:09,520 --> 00:53:12,360
- We'll hide it from Team White.
- We'll tell Team White we earned three.

1370
00:53:12,690 --> 00:53:13,860
I don't mind...

1371
00:53:14,260 --> 00:53:16,730
not trading with Team White at all today.

1372
00:53:17,260 --> 00:53:19,160
- Let's quickly trade with Team Red and...
- Right.

1373
00:53:19,560 --> 00:53:21,470
- Then go back to our place.
- Don't come out.

1374
00:53:21,470 --> 00:53:23,500
We'll ignore them
even if they're at our door.

1375
00:53:23,500 --> 00:53:25,570
- We have the right to decline.
- Just stay inside.

1376
00:53:25,900 --> 00:53:29,670
That will take a fun turn
when we meet up for dinner.

1377
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:31,680
We have no other choice.
Even if we tell them...

1378
00:53:31,680 --> 00:53:33,550
that we only earned three lives today,

1379
00:53:33,680 --> 00:53:35,750
they won't think we're being truthful.

1380
00:53:36,080 --> 00:53:39,680
Rather than blatantly lying,
I think it's better to just avoid them.

1381
00:53:39,680 --> 00:53:42,020
- Am I being avoidant?
- That's avoidance.

1382
00:53:42,020 --> 00:53:43,090
You're being avoidant.

1383
00:53:43,090 --> 00:53:46,190
We had already formed an alliance
with Team Red,

1384
00:53:46,190 --> 00:53:47,830
agreeing to share the lives we had earned.

1385
00:53:47,960 --> 00:53:51,560
We couldn't afford to give any
of our lives to Team White today.

1386
00:53:51,560 --> 00:53:53,100
To feel guilty over that?

1387
00:53:53,100 --> 00:53:55,700
There is plenty else to feel bad about,
so I won't dwell on it.

1388
00:53:57,540 --> 00:54:00,070
All the productive activities are over.

1389
00:54:00,070 --> 00:54:02,140
(Team White's produced resource: 2 lives)

1390
00:54:02,140 --> 00:54:03,910
(Team Red's produced resource: 2 lives)

1391
00:54:03,910 --> 00:54:05,710
(Team Blue's produced resource: 5 lives)

1392
00:54:05,780 --> 00:54:12,750
(Resources After Day 3's Production:
White, Blue, Red)

1393
00:54:12,750 --> 00:54:14,820
(Resources After Day 3's Production:
White, Blue, Red)

1394
00:54:15,450 --> 00:54:18,420
Still, I feel at ease
after earning two lives.

1395
00:54:18,420 --> 00:54:19,720
Tell me about it.

1396
00:54:20,060 --> 00:54:21,830
We managed to buy ourselves another day.

1397
00:54:22,030 --> 00:54:25,800
But let's imagine
this was a real-life situation...

1398
00:54:26,260 --> 00:54:27,570
and not a game.

1399
00:54:27,770 --> 00:54:29,600
Wouldn't we have tried everything
to avoid a war?

1400
00:54:29,730 --> 00:54:31,600
If death was the real penalty, I mean.

1401
00:54:31,740 --> 00:54:34,010
If these lives
really meant actual survival,

1402
00:54:34,010 --> 00:54:35,770
we could've been much more ruthless.

1403
00:54:35,970 --> 00:54:37,910
Society is maintained because we have...

1404
00:54:37,910 --> 00:54:39,410
- That's right.
- an abundance of resources.

1405
00:54:39,410 --> 00:54:41,410
No one must starve for peace to be intact.

1406
00:54:41,410 --> 00:54:42,780
- I see. You're right.
- Right.

1407
00:54:42,850 --> 00:54:44,350
However, we're pretty hungry right now.

1408
00:54:45,150 --> 00:54:47,250
- No wonder we're ruthless.
- Peace is bound to shatter.

1409
00:54:47,450 --> 00:54:48,520
This is delicious.

1410
00:54:48,950 --> 00:54:50,120
- Are you satisfied?
- Savor it.

1411
00:54:50,120 --> 00:54:51,860
Keep it in your mouth
for as long as possible.

1412
00:54:52,320 --> 00:54:54,830
- I'm really taking my time with it.
- Don't swallow just yet.

1413
00:54:55,630 --> 00:54:57,700
Don't they do that a lot in the military?

1414
00:54:58,260 --> 00:55:00,100
- Do what?
- Giving you less food.

1415
00:55:00,800 --> 00:55:03,130
We were just left to survive
in the woods for four days.

1416
00:55:03,270 --> 00:55:04,300
What did you eat?

1417
00:55:04,300 --> 00:55:05,540
Only army rations?

1418
00:55:06,100 --> 00:55:07,710
Rabbits and chickens are also released
into the woods.

1419
00:55:09,110 --> 00:55:10,170
What?

1420
00:55:10,380 --> 00:55:12,280
- For you to catch?
- Yes.

1421
00:55:12,340 --> 00:55:14,110
- But...
- Rabbits?

1422
00:55:14,380 --> 00:55:16,550
- Did you roast them over a fire?
- Yes.

1423
00:55:17,480 --> 00:55:19,680
- We should treat you better.
- That's pure survival.

1424
00:55:19,980 --> 00:55:21,150
We should be nicer to you.

1425
00:55:21,520 --> 00:55:24,190
There are a lot of rabbits
and chickens out there.

1426
00:55:24,460 --> 00:55:26,620
- Really? Should I cook us some?
- I mean, Team Blue and Team Red.

1427
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:30,030
Can you tear them apart?

1428
00:55:30,030 --> 00:55:32,400
Harming people is where I draw the line.

1429
00:55:32,400 --> 00:55:35,330
So much for telling me
not to tease her. Come on.

1430
00:55:37,470 --> 00:55:40,000
(Vector is watching and listening in.)

1431
00:55:40,370 --> 00:55:42,140
Why don't we go to Team Red...

1432
00:55:42,370 --> 00:55:45,480
and say we'll give them 2
out of the 5 we earned?

1433
00:55:46,810 --> 00:55:47,980
They earned five?

1434
00:55:49,080 --> 00:55:51,250
(Quickly checking the production results)

1435
00:55:51,250 --> 00:55:52,350
They earned too many.

1436
00:55:54,050 --> 00:55:55,650
I'd like to keep three on us,

1437
00:55:55,650 --> 00:55:57,520
but that's just not possible.

1438
00:55:57,820 --> 00:55:59,890
We'll tell Team Red we'll give them 2
and Vector 1.

1439
00:56:00,830 --> 00:56:02,030
None for Team White.

1440
00:56:04,060 --> 00:56:07,070
- My stomach feels upset.
- I should tell Team White to start a war.

1441
00:56:07,600 --> 00:56:08,700
It's good.

1442
00:56:09,030 --> 00:56:12,500
If Team Blue only shares their lives
with Team Red...

1443
00:56:15,070 --> 00:56:16,540
I think we're in for a war today.

1444
00:56:17,580 --> 00:56:23,850
(Away)

1445
00:56:24,750 --> 00:56:26,350
The wall code...

1446
00:56:26,850 --> 00:56:28,620
I don't think Vector's got it yet.

1447
00:56:29,050 --> 00:56:33,190
Wouldn't it be more valuable for us
to crack it first?

1448
00:56:34,630 --> 00:56:36,960
When I first talked to Vector,

1449
00:56:37,200 --> 00:56:39,200
he said that activating it...

1450
00:56:39,530 --> 00:56:43,070
would result in the loss
of our entire prize money.

1451
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:45,870
Fortunately, no war has broken out,

1452
00:56:46,270 --> 00:56:47,370
so no prize money has been collected yet.

1453
00:56:48,240 --> 00:56:50,810
Maillard is absolutely fixated on this.

1454
00:56:50,940 --> 00:56:54,350
He said he'd crack the code even if
that's the last thing he does here.

1455
00:56:54,480 --> 00:56:56,150
We'll eventually get around to it,

1456
00:56:56,310 --> 00:57:00,150
so I figured we should crack it
while there isn't any prize money yet.

1457
00:57:00,790 --> 00:57:02,720
You know what, Maillard?

1458
00:57:03,220 --> 00:57:05,560
The answer could be right in front of us.

1459
00:57:06,160 --> 00:57:08,760
If we assume
that the second sentence is meaningless...

1460
00:57:09,730 --> 00:57:11,500
All we have to do...

1461
00:57:11,800 --> 00:57:14,100
is shout "secret room of center"
at the center.

1462
00:57:15,170 --> 00:57:16,170
Right.

1463
00:57:16,300 --> 00:57:17,770
We can't go to
the Community Center right now,

1464
00:57:18,300 --> 00:57:19,740
- but we can go there later.
- Right.

1465
00:57:19,970 --> 00:57:22,210
Let's shout "secret room of center"
while we're there.

1466
00:57:22,210 --> 00:57:23,270
Okay.

1467
00:57:23,440 --> 00:57:26,180
Why isn't the trading round beginning?
What's going on?

1468
00:57:27,950 --> 00:57:30,350
(The trading only begins after
the weapon dealer sets the war cost.)

1469
00:57:30,350 --> 00:57:31,420
Fifteen or...

1470
00:57:32,650 --> 00:57:33,850
Thirty or fifteen.

1471
00:57:42,990 --> 00:57:44,130
The war cost is...

1472
00:57:46,960 --> 00:57:48,070
I set it at 30 diamonds.

1473
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:51,670
The war cost has been set.

1474
00:57:53,470 --> 00:57:54,610
The weapon cost...

1475
00:57:57,840 --> 00:57:59,980
I'll set it to 30, 20, 10, respectively.

1476
00:58:01,010 --> 00:58:03,210
The weapon cost has been set.

1477
00:58:05,020 --> 00:58:07,950
I increased the cost from 15 to 30. Why?

1478
00:58:08,320 --> 00:58:10,560
Raising the war cost lets me...

1479
00:58:10,790 --> 00:58:12,690
indirectly signal inflation.

1480
00:58:12,690 --> 00:58:15,860
"Team White is pumping out diamonds
like crazy right now."

1481
00:58:15,860 --> 00:58:19,100
"If you don't act,
Team White might overrun you,"

1482
00:58:19,100 --> 00:58:21,370
"so go after them."
I raised the cost to 30...

1483
00:58:21,570 --> 00:58:23,730
to send them that message.

1484
00:58:24,040 --> 00:58:25,700
The second reason
for doubling the war cost...

1485
00:58:25,700 --> 00:58:27,140
was to indicate that initiating a war...

1486
00:58:27,140 --> 00:58:29,510
is going to become
much more difficult later on.

1487
00:58:29,510 --> 00:58:31,510
"If you're going to start a war,
you'd better do it now."

1488
00:58:31,510 --> 00:58:33,850
That was the mind game
I was trying to play with them.

1489
00:58:39,180 --> 00:58:41,820
The trading for Day Three will begin.

1490
00:58:43,020 --> 00:58:45,760
You may declare a war during trading.

1491
00:58:46,720 --> 00:58:50,730
Today's war cost is 30 diamonds.

1492
00:58:50,730 --> 00:58:52,530
Wait, it doubled.

1493
00:58:52,530 --> 00:58:53,830
See? It doubled.

1494
00:58:53,900 --> 00:58:56,100
That's it from the Community Center.

1495
00:58:56,100 --> 00:58:58,240
Thirty diamonds is too steep
for us to pay.

1496
00:58:58,770 --> 00:59:02,110
What will it be tomorrow?
Will it be 45 or 60?

1497
00:59:02,440 --> 00:59:06,110
Maybe it was adjusted to accommodate
the diamonds that were issued.

1498
00:59:06,540 --> 00:59:08,550
- Did they issue 200 of them?
- Maybe they did.

1499
00:59:11,120 --> 00:59:13,050
Team Blue wants to start a war.

1500
00:59:13,420 --> 00:59:14,590
They want fewer mouths to feed.

1501
00:59:15,220 --> 00:59:17,760
Since they produce life,
having more mouths to feed is a burden.

1502
00:59:17,760 --> 00:59:20,090
They're having trouble
getting the questions right as is.

1503
00:59:20,390 --> 00:59:21,960
They're working their butts off
to earn lives,

1504
00:59:21,960 --> 00:59:23,430
and six people are begging for them.

1505
00:59:24,760 --> 00:59:27,370
Why don't we talk to Team Blue?

1506
00:59:28,770 --> 00:59:29,800
Maybe we should stay put.

1507
00:59:30,970 --> 00:59:32,340
We're in no hurry.

1508
00:59:32,870 --> 00:59:34,240
- That's right.
- We're fine...

1509
00:59:34,240 --> 00:59:36,710
not trading for a day.

1510
00:59:37,140 --> 00:59:38,810
Yes. What we really need to do...

1511
00:59:38,810 --> 00:59:40,780
is acquire this specialized skill.

1512
00:59:41,650 --> 00:59:43,310
Should we talk to Team Red first?

1513
00:59:45,020 --> 00:59:47,120
- Where are you going?
- What? To wake up Genie.

1514
00:59:47,120 --> 00:59:48,550
I have something to say.

1515
00:59:48,550 --> 00:59:51,160
- Really? We'll let her sleep some more.
- To you.

1516
00:59:51,560 --> 00:59:52,860
It's time for trading though.

1517
00:59:54,390 --> 00:59:56,960
If we lose the war...

1518
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:59,460
and our holdings get halved,

1519
01:00:00,600 --> 01:00:03,170
will we stick together...

1520
01:00:03,170 --> 01:00:04,970
and drop Genie?

1521
01:00:05,540 --> 01:00:07,310
Or will we not do that?

1522
01:00:09,340 --> 01:00:12,410
I think if it comes down
to the worst case scenario...

1523
01:00:13,340 --> 01:00:16,080
If there's a way,
it's better to stick together.

1524
01:00:17,450 --> 01:00:19,780
But in order to do so,

1525
01:00:22,190 --> 01:00:24,820
she can't be the leader.

1526
01:00:25,790 --> 01:00:27,690
I agree. You and I are on the same page.

1527
01:00:30,290 --> 01:00:31,600
Anyway, when it comes down to it,

1528
01:00:32,330 --> 01:00:34,670
she won't be the first one
you'll sacrifice. Right?

1529
01:00:36,630 --> 01:00:38,970
But if we're not the leader...

1530
01:00:39,300 --> 01:00:42,770
and if she's the leader,
it's something she'd definitely do.

1531
01:00:43,640 --> 01:00:46,280
So we might end up going home together.

1532
01:00:48,050 --> 01:00:50,510
But we do have to talk to Team Red.

1533
01:00:50,510 --> 01:00:52,120
Should we call them first
and then wake her up?

1534
01:00:52,520 --> 01:00:55,120
Then will you call them?

1535
01:00:55,120 --> 01:00:57,460
- I'll go and wake her up.
- Okay.

1536
01:01:02,660 --> 01:01:03,890
They're not calling us.

1537
01:01:04,660 --> 01:01:06,000
(Team Blue requests a meeting
with Team Red at Hub 2.)

1538
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:08,070
Team Blue wants to meet up.

1539
01:01:08,170 --> 01:01:10,070
- Let's accept it.
- Yes. Let's go.

1540
01:01:10,330 --> 01:01:11,640
Let's go to Hub Two.

1541
01:01:12,540 --> 01:01:14,370
I'll go and say "Secret Room."

1542
01:01:14,370 --> 01:01:15,370
Okay.

1543
01:01:25,980 --> 01:01:27,520
Secret room of center.

1544
01:01:29,520 --> 01:01:32,560
(Trading Hours)

1545
01:01:36,390 --> 01:01:38,730
State the exact command, please.

1546
01:01:41,270 --> 01:01:43,670
"Placed within secret room of center."

1547
01:01:46,600 --> 01:01:49,070
State the exact command, please.

1548
01:01:49,710 --> 01:01:52,040
"Tell these words in the center."

1549
01:01:52,180 --> 01:01:54,280
"Placed within secret room of center."

1550
01:01:56,250 --> 01:01:58,550
State the exact command, please.

1551
01:01:59,380 --> 01:02:00,580
Open sesame.

1552
01:02:02,690 --> 01:02:03,950
Open sesame.

1553
01:02:08,890 --> 01:02:10,030
I'll come back.

1554
01:02:11,700 --> 01:02:12,860
(Occupied: Please wait.)

1555
01:02:18,140 --> 01:02:20,570
We do have to say the command in there.

1556
01:02:20,570 --> 01:02:22,610
- Let's walk and talk.
- I don't know if I can go far.

1557
01:02:22,610 --> 01:02:24,280
- I do have to go back.
- Okay.

1558
01:02:24,780 --> 01:02:26,780
To crack the puzzle,

1559
01:02:27,040 --> 01:02:28,780
- you need the code for the second part.
- Okay.

1560
01:02:28,780 --> 01:02:30,610
- But only I know what it is.
- You know what it is?

1561
01:02:30,820 --> 01:02:34,090
I'll make up a decoy quiz.

1562
01:02:34,720 --> 01:02:36,950
I'm going to tell people tomorrow that...

1563
01:02:36,950 --> 01:02:38,590
- it's been in the supermarket all along.
- Okay.

1564
01:02:38,590 --> 01:02:41,160
Show people that you are
desperately trying to crack the code.

1565
01:02:41,160 --> 01:02:42,160
I got it.

1566
01:02:42,160 --> 01:02:43,290
When they crack it,

1567
01:02:43,290 --> 01:02:44,600
- I'll make sure something shows up.
- Okay.

1568
01:02:44,600 --> 01:02:45,830
- That's how it'll look on the surface.
- Okay.

1569
01:02:49,970 --> 01:02:51,770
(Hub 2)

1570
01:02:51,770 --> 01:02:53,070
What's taking them so long?

1571
01:02:53,400 --> 01:02:55,110
Did they not reach an agreement yet?

1572
01:02:58,880 --> 01:03:01,110
"State the exact command, please."

1573
01:03:02,550 --> 01:03:03,980
Right. So we don't have everything.

1574
01:03:04,350 --> 01:03:06,320
- Hello.
- Hello.

1575
01:03:06,320 --> 01:03:07,690
- Hi.
- I'll go over there.

1576
01:03:07,690 --> 01:03:08,690
Great.

1577
01:03:08,990 --> 01:03:11,020
Leader Luna,
could you go over it one more time?

1578
01:03:11,020 --> 01:03:13,690
What do we need to acquire
from today's trading?

1579
01:03:13,690 --> 01:03:15,930
- First, our priority is...
- Lives...

1580
01:03:15,930 --> 01:03:18,600
- getting 3 lives. That's our goal.
- Getting 3 lives.

1581
01:03:18,800 --> 01:03:21,300
I think three is probably
the maximum they'll offer us.

1582
01:03:21,770 --> 01:03:23,100
If they can't give us three,

1583
01:03:23,100 --> 01:03:25,870
the minimum number of lives
we absolutely need is two...

1584
01:03:26,040 --> 01:03:27,540
with the plan that
we must get at least one...

1585
01:03:27,540 --> 01:03:29,040
during the activity tomorrow.

1586
01:03:30,040 --> 01:03:32,010
Then we can buy one more day.

1587
01:03:32,010 --> 01:03:33,640
Then what about the day after tomorrow?

1588
01:03:33,840 --> 01:03:36,710
- We'll have to start a war.
- There will be a war for sure.

1589
01:03:36,710 --> 01:03:37,880
We'll need six.

1590
01:03:37,880 --> 01:03:39,980
- There's no way we can get six.
- No. It's not possible.

1591
01:03:39,980 --> 01:03:41,950
That's why getting three or more
will be nice.

1592
01:03:42,120 --> 01:03:43,890
So it will depend on...

1593
01:03:43,890 --> 01:03:46,660
- how many lives Team Blue got today.
- Yes.

1594
01:03:46,960 --> 01:03:49,730
How many diamonds are we going to spend
for one life?

1595
01:03:50,030 --> 01:03:53,030
We have 85 diamonds left.

1596
01:03:53,560 --> 01:03:56,800
Actually, this might be
the right approach to Team Blue.

1597
01:03:57,130 --> 01:03:58,700
"Name the price. We'll match it."

1598
01:03:58,700 --> 01:04:00,840
"Give us as many lives as you can."

1599
01:04:00,840 --> 01:04:03,210
That might be the right way to go.

1600
01:04:03,210 --> 01:04:06,510
Securing as many lives as we can
might be a good approach.

1601
01:04:06,510 --> 01:04:07,750
Then we have to meet with them first.

1602
01:04:07,750 --> 01:04:09,350
- We must talk to them first.
- After that...

1603
01:04:13,980 --> 01:04:17,690
We'd like to request a meeting
with Team Blue at Hub Five.

1604
01:04:19,660 --> 01:04:21,490
Team Blue is away.

1605
01:04:21,690 --> 01:04:23,390
Are they already talking?

1606
01:04:23,390 --> 01:04:24,700
Should we just go out?

1607
01:04:25,160 --> 01:04:26,730
- Let's call Team Red.
- Team Red.

1608
01:04:27,330 --> 01:04:29,700
- We can call them and head over.
- Yes. If they're also away,

1609
01:04:29,700 --> 01:04:31,400
- the two teams are talking.
- We must be out and about.

1610
01:04:32,170 --> 01:04:35,870
We'd like to request a meeting
with Team Red at Hub Five.

1611
01:04:38,110 --> 01:04:40,080
Team Red is away.

1612
01:04:40,340 --> 01:04:41,550
- Yes. They're meeting up now.
- Yes, they're talking.

1613
01:04:41,550 --> 01:04:42,710
- Yes.
- Right. Let's go out.

1614
01:04:42,710 --> 01:04:44,850
- Let's go out.
- We need to buy lives now.

1615
01:04:44,850 --> 01:04:46,080
I bet Team Blue...

1616
01:04:46,080 --> 01:04:48,020
- is in dire need of credits.
- That's right.

1617
01:04:48,020 --> 01:04:49,850
We couldn't secure the upper hand here.

1618
01:04:49,850 --> 01:04:52,390
- There's nothing we can do now.
- I saw this coming.

1619
01:04:52,390 --> 01:04:54,020
Where do you think they're meeting up?

1620
01:04:54,230 --> 01:04:56,360
Wouldn't they be between the hubs?

1621
01:04:57,560 --> 01:04:59,130
How did it go? You earned...

1622
01:04:59,130 --> 01:05:00,560
- three lives today, right?
- No.

1623
01:05:00,730 --> 01:05:02,070
- Did you earn more?
- No.

1624
01:05:02,070 --> 01:05:03,370
- Two?
- Yes.

1625
01:05:03,370 --> 01:05:04,640
- We weren't efficient.
- I see.

1626
01:05:04,740 --> 01:05:06,570
- We earned five.
- Five?

1627
01:05:06,570 --> 01:05:09,110
- Yes.
- We used up all of our credits today.

1628
01:05:09,110 --> 01:05:10,810
That's why we don't have any credits left.

1629
01:05:10,810 --> 01:05:12,180
- So...
- You have zero left?

1630
01:05:12,180 --> 01:05:13,540
- No. Of course...
- We...

1631
01:05:13,540 --> 01:05:15,050
- We have 1 left for tomorrow.
- We have 1 for tomorrow.

1632
01:05:15,050 --> 01:05:16,980
- We'll need one for tomorrow.
- Yes.

1633
01:05:17,620 --> 01:05:20,380
- So that's all we have now.
- This is everything.

1634
01:05:20,380 --> 01:05:22,190
- We only have nine. That's it.
- Yes.

1635
01:05:22,420 --> 01:05:26,560
We don't have that many left.
So we want to earn more credits tomorrow.

1636
01:05:26,920 --> 01:05:28,930
- I think you should.
- Right. And...

1637
01:05:29,460 --> 01:05:34,230
If you can sell us some of the lives
you have,

1638
01:05:34,400 --> 01:05:37,230
we'll be in a position
to go after the credits tomorrow.

1639
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:40,140
As you mentioned earlier,

1640
01:05:40,140 --> 01:05:43,070
we can side with you if a war breaks out.

1641
01:05:43,740 --> 01:05:45,380
That's what we can offer.

1642
01:05:45,380 --> 01:05:47,310
- Hello.
- It's Team White.

1643
01:05:47,910 --> 01:05:50,350
- Hello.
- You guys are getting along well.

1644
01:05:50,350 --> 01:05:52,850
We kept calling you,
but we didn't hear back.

1645
01:05:52,850 --> 01:05:55,290
- No one was inside.
- We're meeting with them first.

1646
01:05:55,390 --> 01:05:57,920
You'd be uncomfortable
if we were here, right?

1647
01:05:57,920 --> 01:05:59,820
- Could you give us some time, then?
- Sure.

1648
01:05:59,820 --> 01:06:01,190
- Then...
- Okay.

1649
01:06:01,430 --> 01:06:02,660
- We... Sure.
- I have a question.

1650
01:06:02,660 --> 01:06:05,400
Is there anyone trying to solve
the skill development question?

1651
01:06:05,400 --> 01:06:06,400
Right.

1652
01:06:06,400 --> 01:06:09,330
I'm asking because
we're trying really hard to solve it.

1653
01:06:09,770 --> 01:06:10,830
But...

1654
01:06:10,830 --> 01:06:12,770
we're approaching the question
with the premise that...

1655
01:06:12,770 --> 01:06:14,100
it would negatively affect...

1656
01:06:14,100 --> 01:06:15,910
our entire community in exchange for...

1657
01:06:15,910 --> 01:06:17,340
one team to acquire the skill.

1658
01:06:17,340 --> 01:06:19,640
- I think it will help us for now...
- Actually...

1659
01:06:19,640 --> 01:06:22,180
because our overall production efficiency
is very low.

1660
01:06:22,550 --> 01:06:24,110
There's a shortage of resources.

1661
01:06:24,110 --> 01:06:25,780
We need to develop these skills.

1662
01:06:26,150 --> 01:06:27,320
- Right.
- It might boost...

1663
01:06:27,320 --> 01:06:28,520
the volume of life production.

1664
01:06:28,520 --> 01:06:29,520
That could be possible.

1665
01:06:29,520 --> 01:06:31,490
Or the volume of credit production.
We need...

1666
01:06:32,020 --> 01:06:34,660
a way to boost our resource production.

1667
01:06:34,790 --> 01:06:37,730
It's only the third day,
and we're running out of resources.

1668
01:06:37,730 --> 01:06:39,130
- It makes no sense.
- All of us will die.

1669
01:06:39,130 --> 01:06:41,130
We need to solve
the skill development question.

1670
01:06:41,230 --> 01:06:43,200
We should come together...

1671
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:45,940
and try to solve
the skill development questions together.

1672
01:06:45,940 --> 01:06:48,010
We need to solve them as fast as possible.

1673
01:06:48,310 --> 01:06:50,870
- It'll improve the quality of our life.
- Right.

1674
01:06:51,010 --> 01:06:53,980
- You guys are trying to make a deal now.
- Once we finish trading,

1675
01:06:53,980 --> 01:06:56,010
we can do this over dinner.

1676
01:06:56,010 --> 01:06:57,850
- Let's meet up then.
- Okay.

1677
01:06:57,850 --> 01:06:59,020
Then...

1678
01:06:59,480 --> 01:07:01,020
- should we wait in the Town Hall?
- Let's go.

1679
01:07:01,190 --> 01:07:03,590
Let's go to the Town Hall
and force open the fridge.

1680
01:07:03,590 --> 01:07:04,890
That's not a bad idea.

1681
01:07:06,360 --> 01:07:09,160
As we told you earlier,

1682
01:07:09,390 --> 01:07:12,400
we're not going to trade with them today.

1683
01:07:13,100 --> 01:07:16,530
We'll have to give one to Vector.

1684
01:07:16,900 --> 01:07:18,240
- The supermarket must be open.
- Right, it must be open.

1685
01:07:18,240 --> 01:07:20,240
Then we have four left. Right?

1686
01:07:20,340 --> 01:07:22,370
We're interested
in splitting the remaining four with you.

1687
01:07:23,040 --> 01:07:24,840
- So we'd get two each.
- Okay.

1688
01:07:25,010 --> 01:07:29,880
We'll give you as many lives
as we can spare. As for the credits,

1689
01:07:29,880 --> 01:07:31,280
give us as many credits as you can spare.

1690
01:07:31,380 --> 01:07:34,720
We can split the leftovers
and give you four.

1691
01:07:34,920 --> 01:07:38,560
Here's why.
Our job is producing the credits.

1692
01:07:38,920 --> 01:07:40,420
We have to use one each.

1693
01:07:46,300 --> 01:07:47,870
- So you have to use three in total?
- Yes.

1694
01:07:48,200 --> 01:07:49,700
- It's different with us.
- Right.

1695
01:07:49,700 --> 01:07:50,930
(Each team only needs 1 credit
to enter the production site.)

1696
01:07:50,930 --> 01:07:52,270
- Let me explain.
- That's why...

1697
01:07:52,270 --> 01:07:54,470
For each correct answer,
we get three credits.

1698
01:07:55,940 --> 01:07:58,140
- That's why we need to use three.
- That's why it's different.

1699
01:07:58,140 --> 01:08:00,440
- Yes.
- Your team is...

1700
01:08:00,440 --> 01:08:01,450
- highly efficient.
- Right.

1701
01:08:01,450 --> 01:08:03,080
That's why we can only give you four.

1702
01:08:03,080 --> 01:08:05,880
We need to use three credits
to enter the site.

1703
01:08:05,880 --> 01:08:07,080
We need another one for the questions.

1704
01:08:07,080 --> 01:08:09,290
- If we want a hint...
- We need at least five.

1705
01:08:09,290 --> 01:08:10,390
- Right.
- We need at least this many credits.

1706
01:08:10,890 --> 01:08:12,890
- This is all we have.
- I see.

1707
01:08:13,660 --> 01:08:17,730
- It looks like we can give you two lives.
- Yes.

1708
01:08:18,100 --> 01:08:20,160
For your information,

1709
01:08:20,160 --> 01:08:23,370
we'll tell Team White that
we only acquired three lives,

1710
01:08:23,370 --> 01:08:26,300
but we had to use up all of our credits
to do that.

1711
01:08:26,300 --> 01:08:27,840
So we desperately need credits.

1712
01:08:28,070 --> 01:08:29,970
That's why we have to give you two.

1713
01:08:30,010 --> 01:08:32,740
And we have to give one to Vector
which leaves us with nothing.

1714
01:08:33,140 --> 01:08:36,150
That's what we must tell them to justify
why we're not giving any to them.

1715
01:08:36,150 --> 01:08:38,580
We don't have any credit left
for Team White.

1716
01:08:38,720 --> 01:08:40,480
Then they can trade neither with us...

1717
01:08:40,480 --> 01:08:41,790
- nor with them.
- Right.

1718
01:08:41,790 --> 01:08:44,350
What if they start a war?
Are we going to be okay?

1719
01:08:44,990 --> 01:08:47,690
Team Blue has to buy credits.

1720
01:08:47,690 --> 01:08:49,260
- They must.
- They don't have any left.

1721
01:08:49,260 --> 01:08:51,660
Then they won't be able to enter
the production site.

1722
01:08:51,800 --> 01:08:53,930
I'm getting a feeling that
they might not trade with us today.

1723
01:08:53,930 --> 01:08:55,700
Then they might collude.

1724
01:08:55,870 --> 01:08:57,470
- They might think that...
- Right.

1725
01:08:57,470 --> 01:08:59,170
by not trading with us,
some of us will be eliminated.

1726
01:08:59,270 --> 01:09:00,440
I bet that's what they're thinking.

1727
01:09:00,440 --> 01:09:02,040
- Yes. That's why they met up.
- That's it.

1728
01:09:02,140 --> 01:09:04,810
Then solving
the skill development question...

1729
01:09:04,810 --> 01:09:06,210
- as soon as possible...
- Yes.

1730
01:09:06,210 --> 01:09:08,780
Should we tell you what the skill is
before we end up on bad terms?

1731
01:09:08,780 --> 01:09:12,020
But if they want to trade with us
while we're talking to them,

1732
01:09:12,020 --> 01:09:13,620
we have no excuse not to.

1733
01:09:13,820 --> 01:09:15,820
What can we trade with?
We didn't earn enough.

1734
01:09:15,820 --> 01:09:18,220
That's true. But when we talked to them...

1735
01:09:18,220 --> 01:09:20,560
in the beginning, we promised that
they'd have the priority to buy from us.

1736
01:09:20,560 --> 01:09:21,690
We did promise that.

1737
01:09:22,130 --> 01:09:24,290
(During the trading session of Day 2)

1738
01:09:24,900 --> 01:09:28,530
(Team Blue offered them priority.)

1739
01:09:29,330 --> 01:09:32,000
(Team White and Team Blue
formed an alliance.)

1740
01:09:32,470 --> 01:09:35,470
(In exchange for priority,
Team Blue secured a wartime alliance.)

1741
01:09:35,970 --> 01:09:38,680
After seeing us here,
they won't be happy that...

1742
01:09:38,680 --> 01:09:40,710
we talked to them first.

1743
01:09:40,840 --> 01:09:42,950
What could we say to them when we...

1744
01:09:42,950 --> 01:09:45,150
If they're not happy with it,
they'll start a war tomorrow.

1745
01:09:45,150 --> 01:09:46,750
- I'm not sure...
- But the credits...

1746
01:09:46,750 --> 01:09:47,990
if it will be today or tomorrow.

1747
01:09:47,990 --> 01:09:50,890
If war breaks out,
we'll put our lives on the line and fight.

1748
01:09:51,160 --> 01:09:52,690
- Yes.
- We'll give it our all.

1749
01:09:52,690 --> 01:09:55,190
- That's better for us too.
- And...

1750
01:09:55,190 --> 01:09:57,260
- It'd be better if it was today.
- Yes.

1751
01:09:57,260 --> 01:09:58,830
- That's true.
- It costs 30 diamonds to start the war.

1752
01:09:58,830 --> 01:10:00,030
- Right.
- If it costs 60 tomorrow,

1753
01:10:00,030 --> 01:10:01,500
- we won't be able to afford it.
- Right.

1754
01:10:01,500 --> 01:10:03,570
- If there's a war...
- Then it will be them starting it.

1755
01:10:04,370 --> 01:10:07,000
That's why the best thing we can do now...

1756
01:10:07,000 --> 01:10:08,410
is solving the question.

1757
01:10:08,410 --> 01:10:09,610
- Right.
- We should talk to them...

1758
01:10:09,610 --> 01:10:10,610
- after we solve it.
- So...

1759
01:10:10,610 --> 01:10:12,580
if you guys can acquire
a lot of lives tomorrow,

1760
01:10:12,710 --> 01:10:14,680
things might change for them.

1761
01:10:14,680 --> 01:10:15,750
- Yes.
- Right.

1762
01:10:18,020 --> 01:10:19,080
What's going on?

1763
01:10:19,880 --> 01:10:20,950
They got rid of everything.

1764
01:10:20,950 --> 01:10:22,090
- They just pulled everything out?
- They did?

1765
01:10:23,920 --> 01:10:26,160
- That's cruel.
- They got rid of everything.

1766
01:10:26,460 --> 01:10:27,930
In case things get stolen?

1767
01:10:27,930 --> 01:10:29,090
(The supermarket disappeared
in an instant.)

1768
01:10:29,090 --> 01:10:30,630
The fridges were removed?

1769
01:10:30,860 --> 01:10:32,230
- They got rid of everything.
- That's cruel.

1770
01:10:32,230 --> 01:10:34,630
We wish to talk with you, Vector.

1771
01:10:35,070 --> 01:10:36,230
Sure.

1772
01:10:36,230 --> 01:10:37,900
(Away)

1773
01:10:38,040 --> 01:10:41,070
Isn't there something written
on your wall?

1774
01:10:41,070 --> 01:10:42,140
There really isn't anything.

1775
01:10:42,240 --> 01:10:45,210
- You said there was something yesterday.
- You said there was something.

1776
01:10:45,210 --> 01:10:46,540
I said there could be something.

1777
01:10:46,540 --> 01:10:47,880
But I couldn't see it as I was busy.

1778
01:10:47,880 --> 01:10:49,850
- You said there was something.
- You said there was something.

1779
01:10:50,950 --> 01:10:52,650
There really isn't anything. First of all,

1780
01:10:52,650 --> 01:10:53,980
my dorm has a different structure.

1781
01:10:55,690 --> 01:10:56,890
I'm sure there isn't anything.

1782
01:10:56,920 --> 01:10:58,260
The walls are small.

1783
01:11:00,320 --> 01:11:04,160
The role of Black really got me thinking.

1784
01:11:04,260 --> 01:11:06,400
You're not in a natural market.

1785
01:11:06,560 --> 01:11:08,570
You're in a market
without any competition.

1786
01:11:08,800 --> 01:11:11,600
I believe it's a powerful market.

1787
01:11:11,640 --> 01:11:14,000
You can think of me as a neutral country.

1788
01:11:14,000 --> 01:11:16,110
A neutral country
will not suffer from any harm.

1789
01:11:16,770 --> 01:11:18,410
It will just generate revenue.

1790
01:11:18,480 --> 01:11:21,580
However, for a neutral country
to maximize its revenue,

1791
01:11:21,650 --> 01:11:22,910
peace must be maintained.

1792
01:11:24,280 --> 01:11:25,750
It depends on what gets sold.

1793
01:11:25,750 --> 01:11:28,650
The US made a lot of revenue
during World War II.

1794
01:11:29,650 --> 01:11:31,820
This happened while maintaining
a neutral stance...

1795
01:11:31,820 --> 01:11:33,190
before getting involved in the war.

1796
01:11:39,900 --> 01:11:41,300
Does Black sell the weapons as well?

1797
01:11:44,130 --> 01:11:45,770
- No. Not at all.
- There was nothing about that?

1798
01:11:45,770 --> 01:11:47,040
The weapons aren't here.

1799
01:11:49,310 --> 01:11:51,010
We can't be sure from here.

1800
01:11:51,010 --> 01:11:52,110
We never went in.

1801
01:11:52,440 --> 01:11:55,250
I'm a market and neutral country.

1802
01:11:55,550 --> 01:11:58,650
I'm doing my best
to keep the balance of the market.

1803
01:11:58,650 --> 01:12:01,620
That is never an easy thing to do.

1804
01:12:03,850 --> 01:12:06,660
One hour into the trading session.

1805
01:12:06,660 --> 01:12:07,860
There are only two hours left.

1806
01:12:07,960 --> 01:12:09,330
There are two hours left now.

1807
01:12:09,330 --> 01:12:12,030
If we are going to continue
to talk about this,

1808
01:12:12,030 --> 01:12:14,130
we should come prepared
for the skill development questions...

1809
01:12:14,130 --> 01:12:15,200
and gather together...

1810
01:12:15,200 --> 01:12:17,170
to get this solved quickly.

1811
01:12:17,200 --> 01:12:19,140
Should we go after making our trade?

1812
01:12:19,140 --> 01:12:20,170
I think our trade should come first.

1813
01:12:20,170 --> 01:12:21,540
- Should we trade first?
- Yes. Let's trade first.

1814
01:12:21,540 --> 01:12:23,240
- Should we trade first?
- Yes.

1815
01:12:23,240 --> 01:12:24,470
- Let's trade first.
- Let's trade first.

1816
01:12:24,470 --> 01:12:25,640
I'll bring it.

1817
01:12:25,710 --> 01:12:26,880
It came to me as a big surprise.

1818
01:12:26,880 --> 01:12:29,310
Team Blue seemed to be quite anxious.

1819
01:12:29,480 --> 01:12:30,880
They wanted four credits.

1820
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:32,920
On top of that,
one credit was used for commission.

1821
01:12:32,920 --> 01:12:35,320
So 1 will be submitted for commission
and 3 will be put up for the trade.

1822
01:12:35,320 --> 01:12:36,420
- Right.
- Right.

1823
01:12:36,420 --> 01:12:37,990
(Trade: 2 lives for 4 credits)

1824
01:12:38,220 --> 01:12:40,720
The Trading Station has been activated.

1825
01:12:42,130 --> 01:12:43,190
That way.

1826
01:12:44,860 --> 01:12:47,360
(Team Blue's Resources:
76 diamonds, 17 lives, 2 credits)

1827
01:12:47,360 --> 01:12:49,900
(Team Red's Resources:
55 diamonds, 8 lives, 9 credits)

1828
01:12:49,900 --> 01:12:51,270
They received three credits...

1829
01:12:51,270 --> 01:12:52,940
and gave us two lives.

1830
01:12:52,940 --> 01:12:56,070
Except for the first day
when we didn't have any information,

1831
01:12:56,070 --> 01:12:57,370
we never made a trade like this.

1832
01:12:57,370 --> 01:13:00,680
We didn't expect to make a trade
based on this ratio.

1833
01:13:00,940 --> 01:13:02,350
We thought that we had to pay...

1834
01:13:02,350 --> 01:13:06,180
at least 4 or 5 credits to buy a life.

1835
01:13:06,180 --> 01:13:08,450
The fact that they agreed
to make this trade...

1836
01:13:08,450 --> 01:13:11,520
made me think that they were
feeling the pressure of war.

1837
01:13:11,590 --> 01:13:13,720
Under the condition
of becoming their ally,

1838
01:13:13,720 --> 01:13:16,360
we were able to make a good trade.

1839
01:13:16,360 --> 01:13:17,690
That was a relief for us.

1840
01:13:18,600 --> 01:13:20,130
- Thank you.
- Gosh.

1841
01:13:20,130 --> 01:13:21,230
(Teams Blue and Red are done trading.)

1842
01:13:27,900 --> 01:13:29,210
- Did you make the trade?
- Yes.

1843
01:13:30,040 --> 01:13:31,380
Could I get the card key?

1844
01:13:31,380 --> 01:13:32,910
The card key?
Are you going to stop by the dorm?

1845
01:13:33,240 --> 01:13:35,250
I want to look up something.

1846
01:13:35,610 --> 01:13:37,080
Look up what?

1847
01:13:37,150 --> 01:13:39,880
There's a rule that I'm curious about.

1848
01:13:41,490 --> 01:13:45,060
(Pitou heads to the dorm
before meeting Team White.)

1849
01:13:46,960 --> 01:13:48,760
We're sorry. We were in a conversation.

1850
01:13:48,760 --> 01:13:50,390
We brought the skill development question.

1851
01:13:51,660 --> 01:13:53,000
They're here.

1852
01:13:53,400 --> 01:13:55,000
Did you complete the trade?

1853
01:13:55,230 --> 01:13:56,800
- Us?
- Do you need to talk more?

1854
01:13:56,800 --> 01:13:57,970
We made our trade.

1855
01:13:58,070 --> 01:13:59,740
- You made a trade? Really?
- You made a trade?

1856
01:14:00,400 --> 01:14:03,010
Really? They made a trade.

1857
01:14:03,210 --> 01:14:04,340
This is bad.

1858
01:14:05,510 --> 01:14:07,140
We expected it to happen,

1859
01:14:07,140 --> 01:14:10,080
but Team Blue already made contact
with Team Red.

1860
01:14:10,310 --> 01:14:13,750
We were promised
a trade priority yesterday,

1861
01:14:14,080 --> 01:14:16,920
but it's all meaningless now.

1862
01:14:16,920 --> 01:14:18,660
It was just a verbal promise.

1863
01:14:18,660 --> 01:14:22,590
I prepared for the trade with a mindset...

1864
01:14:22,590 --> 01:14:26,660
of trying to get as many lives
as possible.

1865
01:14:27,260 --> 01:14:28,930
They were like weathercocks.

1866
01:14:28,930 --> 01:14:31,840
We formed an alliance yesterday,

1867
01:14:31,870 --> 01:14:34,840
but they changed paths the very next day.

1868
01:14:34,870 --> 01:14:37,810
I thought,
"These people have short-term minds."

1869
01:14:37,840 --> 01:14:40,080
"We aren't the ones who must
make them trust us."

1870
01:14:40,080 --> 01:14:43,850
"They are the ones we won't be
able to trust in the future."

1871
01:14:43,950 --> 01:14:45,920
- Let's start our conversation.
- Right.

1872
01:14:45,920 --> 01:14:47,950
- Will you make a trade?
- Yes. We'll trade first.

1873
01:14:47,950 --> 01:14:50,150
- Go ahead.
- Make your trade first.

1874
01:14:50,190 --> 01:14:53,560
- We're feeling really anxious right now.
- Right.

1875
01:14:53,820 --> 01:14:55,630
Let's begin.

1876
01:14:55,630 --> 01:14:57,360
Were you able to earn 1 or 2 today?

1877
01:14:57,560 --> 01:14:59,300
- Well,
- We did our best.

1878
01:14:59,300 --> 01:15:01,300
- we did our best.
- The questions were so hard.

1879
01:15:01,570 --> 01:15:03,700
We used all of our credits.

1880
01:15:03,830 --> 01:15:06,000
We used all of them except for the one
that will be used tomorrow.

1881
01:15:06,000 --> 01:15:07,140
So you have one left.

1882
01:15:07,140 --> 01:15:09,740
Are you not able to make a trade
with your own credit?

1883
01:15:09,740 --> 01:15:11,340
Do you not have any leftovers?

1884
01:15:11,640 --> 01:15:13,410
No. Well,

1885
01:15:13,510 --> 01:15:15,010
we have enough credits to make trades.

1886
01:15:15,010 --> 01:15:16,480
We have exactly...

1887
01:15:16,480 --> 01:15:18,220
- two credits left.
- Right.

1888
01:15:18,250 --> 01:15:20,420
We have exactly two credits left.

1889
01:15:20,520 --> 01:15:22,320
With our credits,

1890
01:15:22,990 --> 01:15:24,050
we really...

1891
01:15:25,090 --> 01:15:26,720
Well, as a result,

1892
01:15:26,720 --> 01:15:28,690
we were able to earn only three lives.

1893
01:15:29,230 --> 01:15:30,360
- Three?
- Yes.

1894
01:15:30,360 --> 01:15:32,160
That was how things ended for us.

1895
01:15:32,160 --> 01:15:34,870
This was the reason we moved quickly
to talk with the team with credits.

1896
01:15:34,900 --> 01:15:36,830
We were in need of credits,

1897
01:15:36,900 --> 01:15:38,870
and they also asked...

1898
01:15:38,870 --> 01:15:41,910
- for lives from us.
- Right.

1899
01:15:42,010 --> 01:15:44,040
- So...
- How many did you offer them?

1900
01:15:44,070 --> 01:15:45,580
We offered two.

1901
01:15:45,710 --> 01:15:48,510
And we have to give one
to Vector later as well.

1902
01:15:48,510 --> 01:15:49,710
So, actually,

1903
01:15:49,710 --> 01:15:50,950
we spent all of them.

1904
01:15:51,080 --> 01:15:52,950
- We spent the ones we earned today.
- Right.

1905
01:15:57,390 --> 01:16:00,090
So, if you are short on lives
because of that,

1906
01:16:00,090 --> 01:16:02,090
do you not have any lives
that can be offered to us?

1907
01:16:03,890 --> 01:16:05,400
To be honest, as of right now...

1908
01:16:05,760 --> 01:16:06,860
None?

1909
01:16:06,860 --> 01:16:08,230
That can't be true.

1910
01:16:08,270 --> 01:16:10,730
This makes things really tough.

1911
01:16:11,370 --> 01:16:14,400
You said that you spent all of them.

1912
01:16:14,470 --> 01:16:16,570
That's excluding the ones
you originally had.

1913
01:16:16,570 --> 01:16:19,180
You were talking about the ones
you earned today, right?

1914
01:16:19,880 --> 01:16:21,750
I understand the anxiety you could feel...

1915
01:16:21,750 --> 01:16:24,310
from the continuous loss of lives,

1916
01:16:24,480 --> 01:16:25,780
but we believe it won't be as serious...

1917
01:16:25,780 --> 01:16:29,550
as us who might end up
being short on lives tomorrow.

1918
01:16:29,620 --> 01:16:31,220
This is our plea.

1919
01:16:31,220 --> 01:16:34,420
We're not asking you
to sacrifice the lives...

1920
01:16:34,420 --> 01:16:36,890
you have saved up for tomorrow
or the day after.

1921
01:16:36,890 --> 01:16:38,600
We all started by knowing...

1922
01:16:38,600 --> 01:16:40,730
the total amount of lives.

1923
01:16:40,730 --> 01:16:42,800
We know how many lives were spent.

1924
01:16:42,870 --> 01:16:45,670
We have a brief prediction
of how many were produced as well.

1925
01:16:46,300 --> 01:16:49,840
We're all keeping count
of each other's resources.

1926
01:16:50,140 --> 01:16:52,180
Based on that,

1927
01:16:52,280 --> 01:16:55,110
we believe you will be safe
for the next few days.

1928
01:16:55,110 --> 01:16:56,180
It's a lot worse than you think.

1929
01:16:56,180 --> 01:16:58,520
If we give up a bit more
from what we have...

1930
01:16:59,120 --> 01:17:00,350
and give one to Black,

1931
01:17:00,350 --> 01:17:02,820
we'll have a similar amount to Team Red.

1932
01:17:02,890 --> 01:17:03,990
(Team Blue Lives: 17)

1933
01:17:03,990 --> 01:17:05,190
(Team Red Lives: 8)

1934
01:17:05,190 --> 01:17:06,320
I see.

1935
01:17:06,320 --> 01:17:08,330
We don't have that many lives to spare.

1936
01:17:08,830 --> 01:17:11,160
We aren't that far off
with the number of lives already.

1937
01:17:12,500 --> 01:17:14,100
- We must get at least one.
- Right.

1938
01:17:14,660 --> 01:17:16,100
- That can't happen.
- Please spare us just a little.

1939
01:17:17,130 --> 01:17:18,770
Look at our glowing eyes.

1940
01:17:19,170 --> 01:17:20,870
A trade must happen.

1941
01:17:21,770 --> 01:17:24,140
But things are...

1942
01:17:31,850 --> 01:17:33,320
Pitou...

1943
01:17:33,320 --> 01:17:34,520
Why isn't she coming?

1944
01:17:35,450 --> 01:17:37,890
(Leader Pitou is holding out in the dorm.)

1945
01:17:38,390 --> 01:17:42,860
It feels like my blood is drying up
day after day.

1946
01:17:42,930 --> 01:17:46,900
We are short on lives right now,

1947
01:17:46,900 --> 01:17:48,470
and we don't have enough for everyone.

1948
01:17:48,470 --> 01:17:50,330
The people here felt so warm,

1949
01:17:50,400 --> 01:17:52,240
and that kept bothering me...

1950
01:17:52,240 --> 01:17:55,070
as someone who wants a war to break out.

1951
01:17:55,170 --> 01:17:57,010
As a leader,

1952
01:17:57,010 --> 01:17:58,340
I felt so incompetent.

1953
01:17:58,340 --> 01:18:00,740
That was how I felt about this situation.

1954
01:18:00,910 --> 01:18:02,850
I felt a sense of fear today.

1955
01:18:05,750 --> 01:18:09,650
The fourth code on the wall
hasn't been figured out yet.

1956
01:18:09,650 --> 01:18:10,820
There were four dorms.

1957
01:18:10,820 --> 01:18:12,590
Each dorm seemed to have a code.

1958
01:18:12,590 --> 01:18:14,690
Black didn't reveal that code.

1959
01:18:14,690 --> 01:18:16,630
I still can't believe what he said.

1960
01:18:16,690 --> 01:18:18,830
Vector went against his own words
the most.

1961
01:18:18,830 --> 01:18:21,100
He rambled too often
during our conversations.

1962
01:18:21,100 --> 01:18:23,370
He said things that didn't sound right
too often.

1963
01:18:24,530 --> 01:18:25,940
Are you heading over
to solve your question?

1964
01:18:26,400 --> 01:18:27,500
No.

1965
01:18:28,040 --> 01:18:29,370
I'm here to talk with you.

1966
01:18:29,370 --> 01:18:30,540
- Me?
- Yes.

1967
01:18:31,010 --> 01:18:32,480
I wonder what you want to talk about.

1968
01:18:33,080 --> 01:18:34,440
What's your mission?

1969
01:18:34,680 --> 01:18:35,880
- My mission?
- Yes.

1970
01:18:36,380 --> 01:18:37,950
- It's to solve this question.
- Really?

1971
01:18:38,050 --> 01:18:39,380
- That's it?
- Yes.

1972
01:18:39,380 --> 01:18:40,780
You don't have any hidden mission?

1973
01:18:40,780 --> 01:18:42,290
- I really don't.
- Really?

1974
01:18:44,890 --> 01:18:46,020
Have you tried cracking the code?

1975
01:18:46,890 --> 01:18:48,020
Well...

1976
01:18:48,020 --> 01:18:51,530
I would've tried if there was something
in my room.

1977
01:18:51,530 --> 01:18:52,930
- There wasn't anything?
- I assure you. There wasn't anything.

1978
01:18:52,930 --> 01:18:54,030
Okay. Well,

1979
01:18:54,030 --> 01:18:55,730
- we tried to crack the code.
- Right.

1980
01:18:55,730 --> 01:18:57,070
But we can't do anything
without the missing code.

1981
01:18:57,870 --> 01:18:59,370
It's essential.

1982
01:18:59,940 --> 01:19:00,970
Well,

1983
01:19:00,970 --> 01:19:02,570
- when the market opens,
- Right.

1984
01:19:02,570 --> 01:19:03,910
something might pop up.

1985
01:19:03,910 --> 01:19:07,280
- There could be a code that I missed.
- Right.

1986
01:19:08,280 --> 01:19:09,610
When it opens tomorrow,

1987
01:19:09,710 --> 01:19:11,110
I'll try to find it
and tell you what it is.

1988
01:19:11,110 --> 01:19:12,120
Right.

1989
01:19:12,280 --> 01:19:13,520
We have to solve this together.

1990
01:19:14,020 --> 01:19:16,990
My position and sense of trust...

1991
01:19:17,220 --> 01:19:18,760
have hit rock bottom.

1992
01:19:18,760 --> 01:19:21,460
As the information I had was precious,

1993
01:19:21,460 --> 01:19:24,030
everyone was trying to
get on my good side.

1994
01:19:24,090 --> 01:19:25,460
But in one moment,

1995
01:19:25,560 --> 01:19:28,930
the trust people had in me was shattered
because of Team Red's Maillard.

1996
01:19:29,000 --> 01:19:31,900
The missing code...

1997
01:19:31,900 --> 01:19:33,900
kept making people question me.

1998
01:19:33,970 --> 01:19:36,240
The good image I built...

1999
01:19:36,240 --> 01:19:37,640
was brought down in a flash.

2000
01:19:37,640 --> 01:19:39,440
I was in great despair...

2001
01:19:39,440 --> 01:19:40,840
as if I failed with an investment I made.

2002
01:19:41,610 --> 01:19:42,810
It was so...

2003
01:19:42,810 --> 01:19:45,280
(Vector, Businessman)

2004
01:19:45,280 --> 01:19:47,750
I didn't know how to deal
with this situation.

2005
01:19:48,120 --> 01:19:50,590
"I have no idea."
If I keep going with this stance,

2006
01:19:50,590 --> 01:19:52,320
people will question me even more.

2007
01:19:52,320 --> 01:19:55,960
That's why I'm planning to come up
with a fake question all night long.

2008
01:19:56,030 --> 01:19:58,800
I'm going to confuse them.

2009
01:19:59,500 --> 01:20:01,700
But as of right now,

2010
01:20:01,870 --> 01:20:06,740
Team Blue is ready to go to war.

2011
01:20:10,410 --> 01:20:11,880
Will Team Blue buy the weapons as well?

2012
01:20:11,980 --> 01:20:13,840
We didn't talk about that. Wait.

2013
01:20:14,710 --> 01:20:16,650
She appeared out of nowhere
like a female lead.

2014
01:20:16,650 --> 01:20:18,110
Why are you all here?

2015
01:20:18,110 --> 01:20:21,480
- Team Blue and Team White are talking.
- Right.

2016
01:20:21,820 --> 01:20:23,090
Are you not going to join them?

2017
01:20:23,090 --> 01:20:24,190
I don't want to go.

2018
01:20:24,190 --> 01:20:25,190
- Are you scared?
- Yes.

2019
01:20:25,190 --> 01:20:26,760
- Why is that?
- Things are serious over there.

2020
01:20:26,760 --> 01:20:30,360
My idea was to avoid them.

2021
01:20:30,360 --> 01:20:31,800
You should take responsibility
as the leader.

2022
01:20:32,400 --> 01:20:34,730
I'm going to give up my position
right away tomorrow.

2023
01:20:36,630 --> 01:20:37,830
You should take responsibility
as the leader.

2024
01:20:38,640 --> 01:20:43,110
We were going to ask,
"Will we talk about skill development?"

2025
01:20:43,110 --> 01:20:45,010
But they said,
"We will talk about our trade first."

2026
01:20:45,010 --> 01:20:47,180
- Right. I knew it.
- That was why we stepped out.

2027
01:20:47,180 --> 01:20:49,180
I was against it from the start.

2028
01:20:49,350 --> 01:20:51,580
It's obvious that Team White...

2029
01:20:51,580 --> 01:20:53,120
would want to make a trade first.

2030
01:20:53,120 --> 01:20:55,850
- Right.
- But we have nothing to offer.

2031
01:20:55,850 --> 01:20:58,560
They would definitely not want to
talk about skill development.

2032
01:20:59,020 --> 01:21:00,490
I want to avoid them as much as possible.

2033
01:21:01,490 --> 01:21:04,160
- Should we offer more?
- No. We should decide on a limit.

2034
01:21:04,560 --> 01:21:08,060
Two will be guaranteed from them.

2035
01:21:08,730 --> 01:21:11,200
- And...
- Then, can we have a minute?

2036
01:21:11,200 --> 01:21:12,200
- Sure.
- You should talk.

2037
01:21:12,200 --> 01:21:13,870
- Can we have a minute to talk?
- Sure.

2038
01:21:15,170 --> 01:21:17,310
- Let's go outside.
- Right.

2039
01:21:19,680 --> 01:21:21,880
During the Leader Negotiation,
there was...

2040
01:21:21,880 --> 01:21:23,680
- a new thing called the transfer.
- Right.

2041
01:21:23,680 --> 01:21:26,080
Instead of just the diamonds,

2042
01:21:26,080 --> 01:21:27,880
we can trade with credits.

2043
01:21:28,420 --> 01:21:31,090
If they need credits,
we can give them some.

2044
01:21:31,090 --> 01:21:32,220
They will be transferred to them?

2045
01:21:32,220 --> 01:21:34,520
- We'll offer them credits as well?
- Right.

2046
01:21:34,960 --> 01:21:37,190
We have to talk about this right now.

2047
01:21:37,190 --> 01:21:39,400
- Right.
- Tell them we'll offer them credits.

2048
01:21:41,970 --> 01:21:43,270
Team Blue!

2049
01:21:43,270 --> 01:21:46,140
This may sound too desperate,
but listen to what I have to say.

2050
01:21:46,140 --> 01:21:47,770
With our current trade,

2051
01:21:47,770 --> 01:21:49,910
- we can offer you diamonds.
- Right.

2052
01:21:49,910 --> 01:21:52,210
But there's something called
the transfer now.

2053
01:21:52,210 --> 01:21:54,180
Credits are important for you, right?

2054
01:21:54,180 --> 01:21:55,180
- Right.
- So,

2055
01:21:55,180 --> 01:21:57,650
we'll make a trade
with lives and diamonds now,

2056
01:21:57,650 --> 01:22:00,780
but we can also transfer credits to you
at night.

2057
01:22:00,980 --> 01:22:03,720
You should consider that
when deciding on...

2058
01:22:03,720 --> 01:22:04,990
what to do with this current trade.

2059
01:22:04,990 --> 01:22:06,560
Right. I understand what you're saying.

2060
01:22:06,560 --> 01:22:07,920
- Right.
- I got it.

2061
01:22:07,920 --> 01:22:09,730
(A transfer of credits was also offered
as part of the trade for lives.)

2062
01:22:11,390 --> 01:22:13,900
- Team Red!
- Right.

2063
01:22:14,100 --> 01:22:16,270
- Stay seated.
- We need to discuss things.

2064
01:22:16,270 --> 01:22:18,130
- Right.
- Team White...

2065
01:22:18,130 --> 01:22:20,800
is desperate to get
at least one life from us.

2066
01:22:20,800 --> 01:22:22,570
- Right.
- They want at least one.

2067
01:22:22,570 --> 01:22:25,880
We must decide on
which path we want to take.

2068
01:22:25,880 --> 01:22:28,650
If we're expecting war to happen
today or tomorrow,

2069
01:22:28,650 --> 01:22:31,410
there's no reason to give them
any lives...

2070
01:22:31,410 --> 01:22:33,780
- as it would be a loss.
- Right.

2071
01:22:33,780 --> 01:22:35,320
If that's not the case,

2072
01:22:35,320 --> 01:22:38,120
we should try our best...

2073
01:22:38,120 --> 01:22:39,760
to maintain a friendly relationship...

2074
01:22:39,760 --> 01:22:41,120
and solve the skill development question
with them...

2075
01:22:41,120 --> 01:22:43,530
and see things out until tomorrow.

2076
01:22:43,530 --> 01:22:44,530
Additionally,

2077
01:22:44,690 --> 01:22:48,100
it would be great if your team
can help Vector...

2078
01:22:48,100 --> 01:22:50,800
open the supermarket again
through the Leader Negotiation.

2079
01:22:50,800 --> 01:22:52,670
If this happens,

2080
01:22:52,670 --> 01:22:54,370
we will agree to make a deal with them...

2081
01:22:54,370 --> 01:22:56,110
without causing any trouble.

2082
01:22:56,110 --> 01:22:58,040
- We want to hear your opinion on this.
- What do you think?

2083
01:23:01,210 --> 01:23:03,980
It feels like we're going to get
one life, right?

2084
01:23:03,980 --> 01:23:06,220
- It feels like one life at most.
- One at most?

2085
01:23:06,220 --> 01:23:08,180
We need to secure at least one.

2086
01:23:08,180 --> 01:23:10,220
Right. Are those two teams talking?

2087
01:23:10,220 --> 01:23:11,550
- Yes. All of them are gathered.
- Right.

2088
01:23:11,550 --> 01:23:13,120
Right. They're talking with Team Red.

2089
01:23:14,160 --> 01:23:15,560
Should we move over to them?

2090
01:23:15,560 --> 01:23:18,030
- They already made a trade.
- Right.

2091
01:23:18,390 --> 01:23:19,860
Let's talk with them.

2092
01:23:19,860 --> 01:23:21,000
Don't you have two digits of them?

2093
01:23:21,000 --> 01:23:22,070
No.

2094
01:23:22,130 --> 01:23:23,700
You've got it all wrong.

2095
01:23:23,700 --> 01:23:25,540
- You have two digits of them.
- Not at all!

2096
01:23:25,540 --> 01:23:27,000
- What's wrong?
- There's a team with two digits of them?

2097
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:28,710
But the total amount...

2098
01:23:28,710 --> 01:23:30,040
You must count again.

2099
01:23:30,040 --> 01:23:31,640
We don't have that many.

2100
01:23:32,480 --> 01:23:34,740
You came in the middle
of our conversation.

2101
01:23:34,740 --> 01:23:36,310
- We haven't made a decision.
- Right.

2102
01:23:36,310 --> 01:23:38,650
But is this something that must be
discussed with Team Red?

2103
01:23:38,650 --> 01:23:40,350
- Yes.
- Really?

2104
01:23:40,750 --> 01:23:41,820
- Why is that?
- Why is that?

2105
01:23:41,820 --> 01:23:43,590
We must give up on a life...

2106
01:23:43,590 --> 01:23:45,990
for it to be offered to you.

2107
01:23:45,990 --> 01:23:47,190
No.

2108
01:23:47,190 --> 01:23:48,930
We're not asking for Team Blue...

2109
01:23:48,930 --> 01:23:52,160
to share the lives
that will be offered to you.

2110
01:23:52,430 --> 01:23:54,360
We're asking them to offer us...

2111
01:23:54,860 --> 01:23:57,900
the additional lives that they have.

2112
01:23:59,370 --> 01:24:01,870
They're not the lives
that were earned today.

2113
01:24:01,870 --> 01:24:03,710
So you're asking us to offer you...

2114
01:24:03,710 --> 01:24:05,040
- the lives we originally had.
- Right.

2115
01:24:05,040 --> 01:24:08,080
There's something I want to ask.

2116
01:24:08,080 --> 01:24:09,110
- It's a straightforward question.
- Right.

2117
01:24:09,110 --> 01:24:12,080
- Let's say we give you one life today.
- Right.

2118
01:24:12,080 --> 01:24:13,180
Then,

2119
01:24:15,550 --> 01:24:18,120
can we be certain that
a war won't break out tomorrow?

2120
01:24:26,300 --> 01:24:27,760
- Our team will start a war?
- Our team will start a war?

2121
01:24:27,760 --> 01:24:30,100
Since we'll be short on lives
even after receiving one life?

2122
01:24:30,100 --> 01:24:32,070
I believe 1 or 2 lives
won't make a difference.

2123
01:24:32,070 --> 01:24:34,640
- We made our own calculations.
- Right.

2124
01:24:34,640 --> 01:24:36,910
- You're right.
- You will have enough lives for today.

2125
01:24:36,910 --> 01:24:38,440
- Right. I get what you're saying.
- If we give you a life today...

2126
01:24:38,440 --> 01:24:39,740
and war breaks out tomorrow,

2127
01:24:39,740 --> 01:24:40,780
that would be one of our lives wasted.

2128
01:24:40,780 --> 01:24:43,050
- It's hard for us to take that risk.
- Right.

2129
01:24:43,050 --> 01:24:44,710
We're telling you that we won't go to war.

2130
01:24:44,710 --> 01:24:47,780
We will assure you that
we won't go to war.

2131
01:24:47,780 --> 01:24:50,920
Verbally expressing this
is the only thing we can do.

2132
01:24:50,920 --> 01:24:52,890
We can also offer a verbal contract.

2133
01:24:52,890 --> 01:24:54,620
- Right.
- After going through skill development...

2134
01:24:54,620 --> 01:24:56,090
and being assured by the progress made,

2135
01:24:56,090 --> 01:24:57,330
we can find a method...

2136
01:24:57,330 --> 01:24:59,100
- through a transfer.
- Right.

2137
01:24:59,100 --> 01:25:00,200
For example...

2138
01:25:00,200 --> 01:25:03,970
We will explain our reasoning
to help you trust us.

2139
01:25:03,970 --> 01:25:07,170
If we start a war
after losing one of our members,

2140
01:25:07,170 --> 01:25:08,640
would that benefit us?

2141
01:25:08,640 --> 01:25:09,940
- We're constantly thinking about that.
- Well,

2142
01:25:09,940 --> 01:25:11,670
- that will bring down the prize money.
- For that reason,

2143
01:25:11,670 --> 01:25:13,240
we kept mentioning this since yesterday...

2144
01:25:13,240 --> 01:25:15,650
that we didn't change the value
of the diamonds.

2145
01:25:15,650 --> 01:25:18,650
The fee for going to war
is worth 30 diamonds today.

2146
01:25:18,650 --> 01:25:20,450
- That will cut down our prize money.
- Right.

2147
01:25:20,450 --> 01:25:22,320
Would we want to go through that
to go to war?

2148
01:25:22,320 --> 01:25:23,390
That's a no.

2149
01:25:23,420 --> 01:25:24,690
You can trust us on this.

2150
01:25:24,690 --> 01:25:26,260
- War is not an option for us.
- You can sense it from our attitude.

2151
01:25:26,260 --> 01:25:27,990
We kept explaining things like this.

2152
01:25:27,990 --> 01:25:29,530
We helped out with the questions.

2153
01:25:29,530 --> 01:25:31,330
We kept being open about these things.

2154
01:25:31,330 --> 01:25:32,760
On top of that,
we kept providing you with money...

2155
01:25:32,760 --> 01:25:34,930
while making sacrifices.

2156
01:25:34,930 --> 01:25:36,070
If we were planning to go to war,

2157
01:25:36,070 --> 01:25:37,930
we would've issued a bunch of diamonds.

2158
01:25:37,930 --> 01:25:40,500
- We're capable of reducing numbers.
- We're like the US with our numbers.

2159
01:25:40,500 --> 01:25:43,440
Right. You don't have to worry about
going to war.

2160
01:25:43,440 --> 01:25:45,010
- And to add to that,
- Yes?

2161
01:25:45,010 --> 01:25:47,610
we weren't considering war as an option.

2162
01:25:47,610 --> 01:25:48,880
We expected...

2163
01:25:48,880 --> 01:25:51,010
this team or this team
to make a deal with us.

2164
01:25:51,010 --> 01:25:52,350
- War is not an option for us.
- Right.

2165
01:25:52,350 --> 01:25:53,820
We came down...

2166
01:25:53,820 --> 01:25:55,790
feeling concerned about...

2167
01:25:55,790 --> 01:25:57,150
Team Blue and Team Red
agreeing to start a war.

2168
01:25:57,150 --> 01:25:59,460
With all of that in mind,
you don't have to worry about war.

2169
01:25:59,460 --> 01:26:02,290
But by my calculations,
the only way war is prevented...

2170
01:26:02,630 --> 01:26:04,460
is by having fewer members.

2171
01:26:06,900 --> 01:26:10,500
The precondition of not going to war...

2172
01:26:10,900 --> 01:26:13,440
is established by Team White
acknowledging a loss in number...

2173
01:26:14,140 --> 01:26:17,470
without taking further action
against the other teams.

2174
01:26:17,470 --> 01:26:19,410
It's hard for us to offer our lives
if that doesn't happen.

2175
01:26:19,410 --> 01:26:21,480
We won't start a war
if you offer us your lives.

2176
01:26:21,480 --> 01:26:23,950
We will be sacrificed
if things don't work out for us.

2177
01:26:23,950 --> 01:26:27,180
It's hard to predict what will happen.

2178
01:26:27,620 --> 01:26:29,250
We should talk about this...

2179
01:26:29,250 --> 01:26:30,890
- between ourselves first.
- Right. We'll talk.

2180
01:26:30,890 --> 01:26:33,890
You don't have to worry about that at all.

2181
01:26:34,020 --> 01:26:35,490
- We'll talk about it first.
- Right.

2182
01:26:40,930 --> 01:26:44,530
Team Red has nine lives,
and so does Team White.

2183
01:26:44,770 --> 01:26:46,940
Team White will purchase more today...

2184
01:26:46,940 --> 01:26:48,740
and they have enough for three
to survive tomorrow.

2185
01:26:49,940 --> 01:26:52,440
That is why they want at least one
from us.

2186
01:26:52,440 --> 01:26:54,280
They're confident that they will produce
two more tomorrow.

2187
01:26:54,410 --> 01:26:56,950
Let's just give one to Team White,

2188
01:26:57,450 --> 01:26:59,250
and we'll all starve together again.

2189
01:27:00,220 --> 01:27:01,280
No.

2190
01:27:02,350 --> 01:27:03,350
That's a no.

2191
01:27:03,990 --> 01:27:05,390
That can't happen.

2192
01:27:05,390 --> 01:27:06,790
That's not even an option.

2193
01:27:07,560 --> 01:27:09,690
- No.
- We should tell them this.

2194
01:27:09,690 --> 01:27:13,700
We will say we won't be able to
open the supermarket if we give them one.

2195
01:27:14,030 --> 01:27:15,970
It feels like we're getting persuaded...

2196
01:27:16,370 --> 01:27:17,970
the more we talk to them.

2197
01:27:18,230 --> 01:27:19,640
I got carried away as well.

2198
01:27:19,640 --> 01:27:20,900
- Right.
- I couldn't help it.

2199
01:27:20,900 --> 01:27:22,240
It was better not to hear from them.

2200
01:27:22,240 --> 01:27:23,370
I got carried away.

2201
01:27:23,610 --> 01:27:26,380
We were being persuaded
by their reasoning.

2202
01:27:26,380 --> 01:27:28,140
I told them to go
so we won't get persuaded.

2203
01:27:28,610 --> 01:27:30,250
- You didn't want to get persuaded?
- Right.

2204
01:27:30,350 --> 01:27:31,950
But that made no sense.

2205
01:27:31,950 --> 01:27:33,220
How can a team be like that?

2206
01:27:33,220 --> 01:27:35,820
Can we allow one of our members
to get eliminated?

2207
01:27:37,390 --> 01:27:38,390
That won't be easy.

2208
01:27:38,390 --> 01:27:40,260
That can't be easy. It makes no sense.

2209
01:27:41,120 --> 01:27:43,390
It's easy for one's heart to get shaken.

2210
01:27:43,390 --> 01:27:46,260
Even after feeling completely determined,

2211
01:27:46,260 --> 01:27:49,400
hearing from Team White...

2212
01:27:49,400 --> 01:27:53,100
made me feel like
we should give them a life.

2213
01:27:53,100 --> 01:27:56,240
My heart started to soften up.

2214
01:27:56,740 --> 01:27:58,270
It's not out of preference.

2215
01:27:58,270 --> 01:28:01,640
Having to step up to strike someone...

2216
01:28:01,640 --> 01:28:04,080
wasn't something pleasant to do.

2217
01:28:04,310 --> 01:28:07,080
Also, they came up to us...

2218
01:28:07,080 --> 01:28:10,020
saying things like,
"Let's do our best for this."

2219
01:28:10,020 --> 01:28:12,260
They were pleading with us
with glowing eyes,

2220
01:28:12,260 --> 01:28:14,090
and it was hard to go against them.

2221
01:28:14,960 --> 01:28:17,530
I wasn't some psychopath.

2222
01:28:17,530 --> 01:28:19,430
It made me let out a sigh like this.

2223
01:28:19,600 --> 01:28:22,270
I feel confused. My heart feels torn.

2224
01:28:22,770 --> 01:28:25,530
Pitou and Genie said things like this.

2225
01:28:25,640 --> 01:28:27,470
"We shouldn't have listened to them."

2226
01:28:27,470 --> 01:28:30,610
"It's hard to go to war
after hearing from them."

2227
01:28:30,640 --> 01:28:31,870
And this was what I thought inside,

2228
01:28:32,340 --> 01:28:34,440
"This was what I wanted."

2229
01:28:35,280 --> 01:28:37,550
"We were able to talk with Team White."

2230
01:28:37,550 --> 01:28:40,480
"We had these conversations
with each other..."

2231
01:28:40,480 --> 01:28:42,550
"and kept spending time with each other."

2232
01:28:42,550 --> 01:28:45,390
I won't be able to stop us
from going to war forever,

2233
01:28:45,390 --> 01:28:48,060
but a method of delaying war...

2234
01:28:48,060 --> 01:28:52,030
is to leave a sense of pleasant discomfort
in our hearts.

2235
01:28:53,130 --> 01:28:54,960
In your opinion,

2236
01:28:55,160 --> 01:28:57,070
is it tough for Team Blue...

2237
01:28:57,070 --> 01:28:58,470
to offer one of the lives they have?

2238
01:28:58,470 --> 01:29:00,000
Is it hard to make that decision?

2239
01:29:00,000 --> 01:29:02,310
Well, I don't understand it, to be honest.

2240
01:29:02,840 --> 01:29:04,040
- Right?
- Yes.

2241
01:29:04,040 --> 01:29:07,010
- I believe they can offer us one.
- Right.

2242
01:29:07,010 --> 01:29:08,080
That was why I brought that up.

2243
01:29:08,240 --> 01:29:11,810
They probably want to
reduce Team White's number.

2244
01:29:11,810 --> 01:29:14,180
- Right. I think that's what it is.
- Right.

2245
01:29:14,180 --> 01:29:16,590
- That's what it is.
- "Are you going to keep everyone alive?"

2246
01:29:16,590 --> 01:29:18,390
All questions were based on that.

2247
01:29:18,390 --> 01:29:19,490
Right.

2248
01:29:20,060 --> 01:29:22,360
They want us to make a promise
on top of that.

2249
01:29:22,360 --> 01:29:24,690
- Right.
- They don't want war...

2250
01:29:24,690 --> 01:29:25,930
and they don't want to waste their lives.

2251
01:29:25,930 --> 01:29:28,760
When we respond to their claims,

2252
01:29:28,760 --> 01:29:30,600
- we have to promise them.
- We shouldn't make promises.

2253
01:29:30,600 --> 01:29:31,600
We have to promise them.

2254
01:29:31,600 --> 01:29:32,600
- We have to promise them.
- Why?

2255
01:29:32,600 --> 01:29:33,740
We have to promise them.

2256
01:29:34,740 --> 01:29:36,310
That way, we'll feel friendly to them.

2257
01:29:36,310 --> 01:29:38,070
- At that moment?
- Right.

2258
01:29:38,370 --> 01:29:39,410
Are you planning to go to war?

2259
01:29:39,580 --> 01:29:41,740
- No.
- No. We aren't considering that at all.

2260
01:29:41,740 --> 01:29:43,780
It's not an option for us.

2261
01:29:44,350 --> 01:29:48,050
We will be able to make a deal
if we promise not to go to war today.

2262
01:29:50,190 --> 01:29:52,920
- Will we not go to war a few days later?
- But...

2263
01:29:52,920 --> 01:29:57,060
But it's not good for us if they believe,

2264
01:29:57,060 --> 01:29:59,900
"They will start a war
if things don't turn out good."

2265
01:30:00,130 --> 01:30:03,270
They must feel assured
that war won't break out...

2266
01:30:03,270 --> 01:30:05,430
for us to make trades for lives.

2267
01:30:05,430 --> 01:30:07,600
That promise must be made.

2268
01:30:07,600 --> 01:30:08,940
Listen to this.

2269
01:30:08,940 --> 01:30:11,040
If I were a Team Blue member,

2270
01:30:11,040 --> 01:30:12,240
I would not make a deal with Team White.

2271
01:30:12,610 --> 01:30:14,480
I won't. What's the point?

2272
01:30:14,480 --> 01:30:16,210
Why is money needed right now?

2273
01:30:16,210 --> 01:30:18,110
We brought them this far...

2274
01:30:18,110 --> 01:30:19,720
to feel persuaded about giving us a life.

2275
01:30:19,720 --> 01:30:21,720
We can't let them take the lead.

2276
01:30:22,250 --> 01:30:25,150
"We won't make a deal with them
if they are going to start a war."

2277
01:30:25,150 --> 01:30:26,160
This isn't what they're thinking.

2278
01:30:26,160 --> 01:30:28,660
The ones who didn't have to do anything
came this close to us.

2279
01:30:28,660 --> 01:30:30,060
But the reason they came is...

2280
01:30:30,060 --> 01:30:32,330
- They're not that calculating.
- Right.

2281
01:30:32,330 --> 01:30:34,760
- I think emotions brought us this far.
- Right.

2282
01:30:34,760 --> 01:30:36,570
This is how united we are.

2283
01:30:36,570 --> 01:30:38,100
So even as soon as tomorrow...

2284
01:30:38,100 --> 01:30:40,900
If we're in danger,
we may have to go to war,

2285
01:30:40,900 --> 01:30:42,340
even though we really do not want to.

2286
01:30:42,340 --> 01:30:45,340
- Saying that sounds like a threat...
- It is a threat.

2287
01:30:45,340 --> 01:30:47,010
Here is why I think that is dangerous.

2288
01:30:47,010 --> 01:30:48,480
If we make it look like we will go to war,

2289
01:30:48,480 --> 01:30:51,080
war really becomes our only option.

2290
01:30:51,680 --> 01:30:54,220
A real war, because then,
they will not trade with us.

2291
01:30:54,220 --> 01:30:57,690
That crosses the red line
we discussed earlier.

2292
01:30:58,450 --> 01:31:01,360
- No, the main point here is this.
- Right.

2293
01:31:01,360 --> 01:31:02,790
Right now, we're being taken advantage of.

2294
01:31:02,930 --> 01:31:04,130
We've been taken advantage of all along.

2295
01:31:04,130 --> 01:31:05,800
No. Look.

2296
01:31:05,800 --> 01:31:08,100
Yesterday, Team Blue came to us.

2297
01:31:08,500 --> 01:31:11,800
(Team Blue initiated the Day 2 trade.)

2298
01:31:12,130 --> 01:31:16,640
(They first offered a diamond trade
and alliance.)

2299
01:31:17,110 --> 01:31:18,840
Look at how today's trades are unfolding.

2300
01:31:18,840 --> 01:31:20,840
Look at how the first trade starts.

2301
01:31:20,840 --> 01:31:22,110
You can see who is being exploited today.

2302
01:31:22,810 --> 01:31:24,510
Money does not matter at all today.

2303
01:31:24,850 --> 01:31:26,550
Those two are trading with each other.

2304
01:31:28,380 --> 01:31:32,390
(Team Blue traded with Team Red first.)

2305
01:31:32,860 --> 01:31:36,360
In that situation,
we need to show our presence.

2306
01:31:36,360 --> 01:31:39,830
But using war to show it is much riskier.

2307
01:31:39,830 --> 01:31:41,700
Because our presence is already known.

2308
01:31:42,160 --> 01:31:43,900
I had a really bad thought.

2309
01:31:43,900 --> 01:31:46,000
If our production is low tomorrow,

2310
01:31:46,000 --> 01:31:48,640
maybe we should go to war. Is that awful?

2311
01:31:48,640 --> 01:31:51,010
- No. I think so too.
- If production is low tomorrow,

2312
01:31:51,010 --> 01:31:52,170
one of us will have to die.

2313
01:31:52,170 --> 01:31:53,840
It may be more than one
if we get nothing here.

2314
01:31:53,840 --> 01:31:54,840
And it is not just us.

2315
01:31:54,840 --> 01:31:56,650
If their production is low,
they'll start a war tomorrow.

2316
01:31:56,650 --> 01:31:57,880
- Right. That is what I mean.
- Right.

2317
01:31:59,080 --> 01:32:03,050
Anyway, we left that issue
unresolved earlier.

2318
01:32:03,050 --> 01:32:08,390
Overall, we're staying peaceful
through today, right?

2319
01:32:08,390 --> 01:32:10,730
When it was just the six of us, honestly,

2320
01:32:10,730 --> 01:32:13,200
I thought we could even start a war today.

2321
01:32:13,200 --> 01:32:14,300
But then I saw their faces.

2322
01:32:14,860 --> 01:32:17,200
If we had not heard them out,

2323
01:32:17,200 --> 01:32:19,540
we would have thought it had to be
today or tomorrow.

2324
01:32:19,540 --> 01:32:21,000
- But after hearing them...
- They're all so kind.

2325
01:32:21,000 --> 01:32:22,740
Then I suddenly thought they might
really be like that,

2326
01:32:22,740 --> 01:32:23,940
and that scared me.

2327
01:32:23,940 --> 01:32:27,680
But we definitely need
to cut their numbers, right?

2328
01:32:27,680 --> 01:32:29,410
- Absolutely.
- We really need to.

2329
01:32:29,410 --> 01:32:30,880
It is an absolutely necessary process.

2330
01:32:30,880 --> 01:32:32,780
We cut their numbers,

2331
01:32:32,780 --> 01:32:36,090
but as long as we let the team survive,

2332
01:32:36,090 --> 01:32:38,720
I think the survivors there
will have no complaints.

2333
01:32:38,720 --> 01:32:40,360
- That is what I think.
- Yes.

2334
01:32:41,220 --> 01:32:42,220
Why don't we...

2335
01:32:43,860 --> 01:32:44,930
just not give them one?

2336
01:32:50,670 --> 01:32:51,900
I cannot bring myself to cut one.

2337
01:32:52,270 --> 01:32:53,700
- Neither can I.
- But then, clearly,

2338
01:32:53,700 --> 01:32:54,940
tomorrow, one of us either dies,

2339
01:32:54,940 --> 01:32:56,110
- or it is war.
- Right.

2340
01:32:56,110 --> 01:32:57,370
They would pay the war fee too,

2341
01:32:57,370 --> 01:32:59,040
- and things would move quickly for us.
- That is true.

2342
01:32:59,040 --> 01:33:00,110
- Let us not waste it.
- Agreed.

2343
01:33:00,110 --> 01:33:03,210
We can also defend it
by saying we're too scared.

2344
01:33:03,210 --> 01:33:04,210
We cannot give one.

2345
01:33:04,210 --> 01:33:05,580
Let us tell them that.

2346
01:33:05,580 --> 01:33:06,880
- That is true.
- Good.

2347
01:33:06,880 --> 01:33:07,880
Good luck.

2348
01:33:08,050 --> 01:33:10,590
Was I too harsh earlier?

2349
01:33:10,590 --> 01:33:12,620
No.

2350
01:33:15,590 --> 01:33:17,430
We cannot do that
after declaring war, right?

2351
01:33:19,060 --> 01:33:20,460
How did it go?

2352
01:33:20,730 --> 01:33:24,570
We kept thinking it through to the end.

2353
01:33:24,570 --> 01:33:25,970
For us, tomorrow,

2354
01:33:25,970 --> 01:33:30,210
the biggest issue is food.

2355
01:33:30,210 --> 01:33:32,170
- Opening the snack bar?
- Yes. To open it...

2356
01:33:32,170 --> 01:33:34,680
- If we are to give you a life,
- Yes.

2357
01:33:34,680 --> 01:33:36,810
we are not really in a position
to do that.

2358
01:33:40,250 --> 01:33:43,650
But then, about what we asked earlier...

2359
01:33:43,650 --> 01:33:47,120
The trade for the three
you earned is already done.

2360
01:33:47,120 --> 01:33:50,660
Are you saying you will not use
any lives beyond those now?

2361
01:33:50,660 --> 01:33:52,030
If so,

2362
01:33:52,030 --> 01:33:55,660
that puts us in a very dangerous position.

2363
01:33:55,660 --> 01:33:57,630
How dangerous does it make things for you?

2364
01:33:57,630 --> 01:34:00,140
It means our anxiety rises.

2365
01:34:00,140 --> 01:34:01,640
Either way, for us,
this is about survival.

2366
01:34:01,640 --> 01:34:04,540
While for you, this is only uncertainty.

2367
01:34:04,540 --> 01:34:06,180
What we can offer you is...

2368
01:34:06,180 --> 01:34:08,110
You need credits anyway.

2369
01:34:08,110 --> 01:34:09,210
There is also the option of aid.

2370
01:34:09,210 --> 01:34:11,280
- Please consider using that option.
- Then...

2371
01:34:11,280 --> 01:34:13,050
Another thing we were thinking is...

2372
01:34:13,050 --> 01:34:14,780
Every time we make a trade,

2373
01:34:14,780 --> 01:34:18,090
we have to waste a credit
on the public pool.

2374
01:34:18,090 --> 01:34:19,460
It just disappears.

2375
01:34:20,120 --> 01:34:21,490
And for that process,

2376
01:34:21,490 --> 01:34:24,490
using up one of our credits there...

2377
01:34:24,490 --> 01:34:26,330
also feels like a bit of a waste.

2378
01:34:26,330 --> 01:34:28,160
You spend one trading lives today,

2379
01:34:28,160 --> 01:34:30,170
- and you must spend one again tomorrow.
- Yes, so...

2380
01:34:30,170 --> 01:34:32,870
We have to produce lives again
tomorrow anyway.

2381
01:34:32,870 --> 01:34:34,470
Tomorrow, we really do have to trade.

2382
01:34:34,470 --> 01:34:36,640
Tomorrow, we truly will have to trade.

2383
01:34:36,640 --> 01:34:38,740
Then we would have to do it again.

2384
01:34:38,740 --> 01:34:42,210
Honestly, continually spending credits
that way...

2385
01:34:42,210 --> 01:34:43,650
is starting to make me question it.

2386
01:34:43,650 --> 01:34:44,680
I completely understand.

2387
01:34:44,680 --> 01:34:48,220
Then what we can expect,
purely based on trust,

2388
01:34:48,220 --> 01:34:51,320
is a guarantee of lives tomorrow.

2389
01:34:51,320 --> 01:34:53,690
We would give you priority,
no matter what.

2390
01:34:53,690 --> 01:34:56,830
- That is what we would do.
- Even if tomorrow is like today,

2391
01:34:56,830 --> 01:35:00,160
we need a firm guarantee
that you will honor that.

2392
01:35:02,400 --> 01:35:04,270
Say we produce three tomorrow.

2393
01:35:04,500 --> 01:35:06,540
We need our survival
to be fully guaranteed,

2394
01:35:06,540 --> 01:35:08,040
- no matter what that number is.
- No matter how many we get.

2395
01:35:08,900 --> 01:35:10,670
We would not use any credits today,

2396
01:35:10,670 --> 01:35:13,080
so in return for not trading today,

2397
01:35:13,080 --> 01:35:15,580
we need to know exactly
what we are guaranteed.

2398
01:35:15,940 --> 01:35:17,450
You must guarantee at least a set number.

2399
01:35:17,450 --> 01:35:19,850
We need our lives to be guaranteed.

2400
01:35:21,720 --> 01:35:23,990
Team White's current approach...

2401
01:35:24,390 --> 01:35:26,520
is actually working against them.

2402
01:35:26,520 --> 01:35:27,660
Against themselves.

2403
01:35:27,660 --> 01:35:28,860
- Because right now...
- I do not know why they do that.

2404
01:35:28,860 --> 01:35:31,060
They have military power
but do not want to use it.

2405
01:35:31,060 --> 01:35:32,630
They are like deer.

2406
01:35:32,630 --> 01:35:35,060
They may genuinely be kind people,

2407
01:35:35,060 --> 01:35:36,570
but Maillard is extremely frustrated.

2408
01:35:36,570 --> 01:35:38,200
Why have weapons if you cannot use them?

2409
01:35:38,200 --> 01:35:40,400
If it were me, I would issue 800 today,

2410
01:35:40,400 --> 01:35:43,710
arm everyone with weapons, and advance!

2411
01:35:44,010 --> 01:35:45,910
Advance again tomorrow!

2412
01:35:46,380 --> 01:35:47,380
All-out attack.

2413
01:35:48,540 --> 01:35:52,080
What is Team White doing?

2414
01:35:52,450 --> 01:35:56,620
I do not know if they think
this can really continue. I...

2415
01:35:56,950 --> 01:35:59,120
Judging by how few lives
they are producing,

2416
01:35:59,120 --> 01:36:01,620
they should start saying goodbye
to their teammates soon.

2417
01:36:01,720 --> 01:36:04,130
We also need to cut their numbers.

2418
01:36:04,130 --> 01:36:06,260
We need to kill Team White. Quickly.

2419
01:36:07,200 --> 01:36:10,130
If we produce three again, like today,

2420
01:36:10,600 --> 01:36:13,740
then we can still provide two lives.

2421
01:36:13,740 --> 01:36:16,000
If we do not trade today,

2422
01:36:16,000 --> 01:36:18,810
that makes four guaranteed lives tomorrow.

2423
01:36:18,810 --> 01:36:20,580
- By that math.
- But you will earn more tomorrow.

2424
01:36:20,580 --> 01:36:23,010
That assumes we actually produce more.

2425
01:36:23,010 --> 01:36:25,280
If we do not, and we skip today's trade,

2426
01:36:25,280 --> 01:36:27,450
we will even transfer the credits to you.

2427
01:36:27,450 --> 01:36:28,780
In return for that,

2428
01:36:28,780 --> 01:36:31,320
we must secure a trade
for four lives tomorrow.

2429
01:36:31,320 --> 01:36:33,690
That is why we said the minimum is four.

2430
01:36:34,490 --> 01:36:36,130
How are we supposed to produce
at least four lives?

2431
01:36:36,130 --> 01:36:37,130
No.

2432
01:36:37,330 --> 01:36:39,960
You keep basing this on what you produce,

2433
01:36:39,960 --> 01:36:42,700
without addressing our uncertainty.

2434
01:36:42,700 --> 01:36:46,200
With that risk,
you need to guarantee four.

2435
01:36:46,200 --> 01:36:47,800
- Right now...
- We would be taking all the risk.

2436
01:36:47,800 --> 01:36:50,940
If production cannot guarantee
that tomorrow,

2437
01:36:50,940 --> 01:36:54,580
I am asking you to set
that uncertainty aside.

2438
01:36:54,580 --> 01:36:57,180
Not, "If we produce three,
we can only give you three."

2439
01:36:57,180 --> 01:36:58,680
It should be,
"Even if we produce only three."

2440
01:36:58,680 --> 01:37:00,720
Then what exactly do we gain from this?

2441
01:37:02,820 --> 01:37:04,820
In a way, we would be
giving up our lives...

2442
01:37:04,820 --> 01:37:07,990
to keep someone else alive
for one more day.

2443
01:37:07,990 --> 01:37:10,130
But we are not...

2444
01:37:10,130 --> 01:37:13,030
a team of people who need that, are we?

2445
01:37:13,500 --> 01:37:15,330
Of course staying alive matters right now.

2446
01:37:15,330 --> 01:37:18,530
But near the end,
only the one with a life will survive.

2447
01:37:18,530 --> 01:37:21,740
That very person could make your prize
worth just one cent.

2448
01:37:26,910 --> 01:37:28,740
Survival alone is not the goal...

2449
01:37:29,210 --> 01:37:30,350
when it comes to this system.

2450
01:37:30,950 --> 01:37:33,020
- You cannot kill our entire team.
- Right.

2451
01:37:33,680 --> 01:37:34,820
In that situation,

2452
01:37:34,820 --> 01:37:38,290
we are not playing solely
for survival right now.

2453
01:37:47,300 --> 01:37:50,370
You might think that kind
of threatening strategy...

2454
01:37:50,370 --> 01:37:52,770
does not help.

2455
01:37:52,770 --> 01:37:55,140
But our conclusion was peace in the end.

2456
01:37:55,140 --> 01:37:56,740
Then what stays in their minds is,

2457
01:37:56,740 --> 01:37:59,340
"They could have threatened us,
but they chose peace."

2458
01:37:59,340 --> 01:38:01,880
That is how they will frame it
in their minds.

2459
01:38:01,880 --> 01:38:04,550
But if we offer peace without any threat,

2460
01:38:04,550 --> 01:38:06,280
they get peace without paying any price.

2461
01:38:06,280 --> 01:38:07,750
They will think it is a given.

2462
01:38:07,750 --> 01:38:12,020
Still, we chose peace
in such a dangerous situation...

2463
01:38:12,020 --> 01:38:15,060
I wanted them to feel
that we might do it someday,

2464
01:38:15,060 --> 01:38:17,830
so I thought we had to plant
that thought in their minds.

2465
01:38:17,830 --> 01:38:19,700
Because we still have the upper hand.

2466
01:38:19,700 --> 01:38:20,760
In numbers too.

2467
01:38:20,760 --> 01:38:23,030
I do not want war either,

2468
01:38:23,030 --> 01:38:26,300
but I chose to play the bad cop...

2469
01:38:26,300 --> 01:38:28,800
because we needed
to unsettle them a little.

2470
01:38:29,140 --> 01:38:31,370
I was really just insisting
without grounds.

2471
01:38:31,370 --> 01:38:32,410
There was no logic to it.

2472
01:38:32,410 --> 01:38:33,710
Why should they keep us alive?

2473
01:38:33,710 --> 01:38:35,480
We already have so many mouths to feed.

2474
01:38:35,480 --> 01:38:38,810
But if I stayed firm there...

2475
01:38:38,810 --> 01:38:41,520
and said, "This makes no sense,"

2476
01:38:41,520 --> 01:38:44,920
they would get confused
before thinking it through.

2477
01:38:44,920 --> 01:38:47,460
I was basically insisting
and throwing a tantrum.

2478
01:38:48,220 --> 01:38:50,430
I acted as though it could never happen.

2479
01:38:50,430 --> 01:38:52,290
I thought that was the only way
to get one life.

2480
01:38:53,930 --> 01:38:56,800
We cannot keep talking
about what we gain...

2481
01:38:56,800 --> 01:38:59,670
because what we actually have is a threat.

2482
01:39:01,170 --> 01:39:03,110
That is why we are not using it.

2483
01:39:03,110 --> 01:39:07,140
We are asking you to create conditions
so we do not have to.

2484
01:39:07,140 --> 01:39:10,750
We want to keep the currency
from becoming worthless later.

2485
01:39:10,750 --> 01:39:12,410
At least one person will survive anyway.

2486
01:39:13,820 --> 01:39:15,650
It is not a threat.
That person will do it...

2487
01:39:15,650 --> 01:39:17,250
because that is the rational choice.

2488
01:39:17,750 --> 01:39:21,260
If you assume
you will make that choice eventually...

2489
01:39:21,260 --> 01:39:23,660
That is why you cannot let us
get down to one person.

2490
01:39:23,660 --> 01:39:26,190
Right now, cutting our numbers
could seem like this.

2491
01:39:26,190 --> 01:39:28,700
"They have six people, a large crowd,"

2492
01:39:28,700 --> 01:39:30,670
"and many mouths to feed,
so reducing them seems good."

2493
01:39:30,670 --> 01:39:31,700
But the moment our numbers fall,

2494
01:39:31,700 --> 01:39:34,440
our options become much more likely
to turn aggressive.

2495
01:39:36,040 --> 01:39:38,140
The fact that they can...

2496
01:39:38,140 --> 01:39:41,180
issue diamonds completely at will...

2497
01:39:41,180 --> 01:39:44,550
is starting to make me
more and more uneasy.

2498
01:39:44,550 --> 01:39:46,920
If we put too much pressure on Team White,

2499
01:39:46,920 --> 01:39:49,180
they may become completely vindictive.

2500
01:39:49,180 --> 01:39:52,720
"Even if you survive,
we will make sure you leave with nothing."

2501
01:39:52,720 --> 01:39:54,390
If that is the grudge they hold,

2502
01:39:54,390 --> 01:39:56,220
they may decide to take everyone down
with them,

2503
01:39:56,220 --> 01:39:57,560
go to war,

2504
01:39:57,560 --> 01:39:59,830
and if only one or two of them are left,

2505
01:39:59,830 --> 01:40:01,530
they can issue diamonds freely,

2506
01:40:01,530 --> 01:40:02,730
keep all of them for themselves,

2507
01:40:02,730 --> 01:40:05,670
make everything we hold worth zero,

2508
01:40:05,670 --> 01:40:07,970
and walk away with everything themselves.

2509
01:40:07,970 --> 01:40:10,310
That is what is starting to worry me.

2510
01:40:10,540 --> 01:40:14,210
How do we siphon those diamonds away,

2511
01:40:14,210 --> 01:40:17,210
and what will they be worth even if we do?

2512
01:40:17,210 --> 01:40:21,420
That is why I am paying close attention
to the diamonds now.

2513
01:40:22,250 --> 01:40:26,150
That is why we are asking for
at least a guarantee.

2514
01:40:27,320 --> 01:40:31,490
But Vector's setup
also makes us the ones responsible.

2515
01:40:31,730 --> 01:40:33,060
People keep asking us for credits too.

2516
01:40:33,060 --> 01:40:35,430
We may have the power over life,

2517
01:40:35,430 --> 01:40:39,030
but every time we earn something,
it gets taken away from us.

2518
01:40:39,270 --> 01:40:40,400
It is not easy.

2519
01:40:40,940 --> 01:40:42,940
Then let us settle on three.

2520
01:40:42,940 --> 01:40:45,010
- For now...
- Let us agree on three.

2521
01:40:45,010 --> 01:40:46,710
Let us settle on that, and for now...

2522
01:40:46,710 --> 01:40:48,040
- do our best.
- Let us do our best.

2523
01:40:48,040 --> 01:40:49,910
And let us really base this on trust.

2524
01:40:49,910 --> 01:40:52,210
If your production gets more efficient...

2525
01:40:52,450 --> 01:40:54,220
- and you get more lives,
- Of course.

2526
01:40:54,220 --> 01:40:55,520
- please let us know.
- Of course.

2527
01:40:55,520 --> 01:40:57,850
- I hope we can trade more generously.
- Good.

2528
01:40:57,850 --> 01:40:59,050
- Then let us settle on three for now.
- Yes.

2529
01:40:59,050 --> 01:41:00,720
Because in the end, we also...

2530
01:41:00,720 --> 01:41:02,090
- want to survive until the end...
- Yes.

2531
01:41:02,090 --> 01:41:03,930
- and take home some prize money.
- Of course.

2532
01:41:03,930 --> 01:41:05,890
- So of course, we need a fair trade.
- Okay.

2533
01:41:05,890 --> 01:41:06,930
Three lives...

2534
01:41:06,930 --> 01:41:09,030
and up to four if you earn more.

2535
01:41:09,030 --> 01:41:10,070
Yes, that sounds good.

2536
01:41:10,070 --> 01:41:11,930
Okay. Yes.

2537
01:41:12,030 --> 01:41:13,370
Then we can work on skill development.

2538
01:41:13,370 --> 01:41:15,070
- Good.
- Let us work on skill development.

2539
01:41:15,070 --> 01:41:16,540
- Sounds good.
- When Team Red comes,

2540
01:41:16,540 --> 01:41:17,610
- shall we start right away?
- Team Red went over there.

2541
01:41:17,610 --> 01:41:18,970
- Where did they go?
- Where did they go?

2542
01:41:22,410 --> 01:41:25,950
But I am still worried about the reserves.

2543
01:41:26,250 --> 01:41:27,820
I guess there are not many in reserve.

2544
01:41:28,280 --> 01:41:30,390
But skill development could unlock
more reserves.

2545
01:41:30,720 --> 01:41:32,490
- We need to solve it quickly.
- Exactly.

2546
01:41:33,090 --> 01:41:34,860
I will go try to solve the question.

2547
01:41:34,860 --> 01:41:36,590
Again? Unlimited attempts.

2548
01:41:40,160 --> 01:41:42,330
I actually stayed up all night last night.

2549
01:41:42,730 --> 01:41:46,570
I spent all night writing down
every economic term I knew...

2550
01:41:46,570 --> 01:41:49,570
and every social phenomenon I knew.

2551
01:41:49,740 --> 01:41:50,910
I am determined to get it right.

2552
01:41:51,010 --> 01:41:52,110
Red.

2553
01:41:52,110 --> 01:41:54,080
(He relentlessly tried
to solve the skill development question.)

2554
01:41:58,850 --> 01:42:00,280
Please!

2555
01:42:01,950 --> 01:42:03,350
- Please!
- We are checking your answer.

2556
01:42:03,590 --> 01:42:05,320
Please wait a moment.

2557
01:42:06,490 --> 01:42:07,790
I could really die.

2558
01:42:08,090 --> 01:42:09,120
That is incorrect.

2559
01:42:09,620 --> 01:42:11,990
Please pick up a new answer sheet.

2560
01:42:14,330 --> 01:42:15,630
That was not it?

2561
01:42:17,470 --> 01:42:20,340
Why don't we discuss skill development?

2562
01:42:20,340 --> 01:42:22,040
- Skill development?
- We are done for today.

2563
01:42:22,040 --> 01:42:23,670
- Right.
- If we do it, let us do it together.

2564
01:42:23,670 --> 01:42:25,040
- Okay.
- Okay.

2565
01:42:25,040 --> 01:42:26,140
Did you decide not to do it?

2566
01:42:26,140 --> 01:42:27,880
- Yes.
- Let us use collective intelligence.

2567
01:42:28,310 --> 01:42:30,180
We decided we would rather
all stay alive together.

2568
01:42:30,180 --> 01:42:31,610
But what I am wondering about Black is...

2569
01:42:31,610 --> 01:42:33,820
Is it not a bad idea to solve it together?

2570
01:42:33,820 --> 01:42:35,950
I mean, skill development with Black...

2571
01:42:35,950 --> 01:42:37,150
Sorry, but is that not a bad idea?

2572
01:42:37,150 --> 01:42:39,390
Because if Black solves it,
Black gets the advantage.

2573
01:42:39,390 --> 01:42:41,260
- So that is why, with Black...
- But...

2574
01:42:41,260 --> 01:42:42,560
I was only working on ours.

2575
01:42:42,690 --> 01:42:44,160
- I...
- Black can work on the rest.

2576
01:42:44,160 --> 01:42:46,060
- True, we cannot stop Black anyway.
- Right.

2577
01:42:46,360 --> 01:42:47,660
Anyway...

2578
01:42:47,900 --> 01:42:49,060
I am going to get it right.

2579
01:42:49,060 --> 01:42:52,500
If I do not get it right,
I have no way to survive here.

2580
01:42:52,530 --> 01:42:55,170
I absolutely had to solve
all of these questions.

2581
01:42:59,310 --> 01:43:01,840
- That will not work.
- That day, we...

2582
01:43:01,840 --> 01:43:03,210
did over 100...

2583
01:43:03,210 --> 01:43:04,310
Over 100?

2584
01:43:04,310 --> 01:43:06,150
(That winter day, beautiful)

2585
01:43:06,350 --> 01:43:08,520
At that point, everyone...

2586
01:43:08,520 --> 01:43:11,190
was on the same page.

2587
01:43:11,520 --> 01:43:14,660
This was absolutely impossible...

2588
01:43:14,820 --> 01:43:16,220
for each team to solve on its own.

2589
01:43:16,220 --> 01:43:18,630
That was the conclusion we came to.

2590
01:43:18,660 --> 01:43:22,230
So we decided to use
collective intelligence.

2591
01:43:22,230 --> 01:43:23,970
(Residents share
their skill development questions.)

2592
01:43:23,970 --> 01:43:25,530
(Key: That day, we learned
a country could also default.)

2593
01:43:25,530 --> 01:43:27,000
(Lock: Once our culture and economy move
from rapid to relaxation growth...)

2594
01:43:27,000 --> 01:43:28,500
(Key: That winter, the beautiful windmill
burst with an enormous bubble.)

2595
01:43:28,500 --> 01:43:30,110
(Lock: Development and cuts to
ten resources have decreasing deadlines.)

2596
01:43:30,270 --> 01:43:32,570
- But we are not sharing our weapons.
- Yes.

2597
01:43:32,570 --> 01:43:34,010
Really? Should we tell you ours?

2598
01:43:34,010 --> 01:43:35,040
- Yes.
- Please tell us.

2599
01:43:35,040 --> 01:43:38,410
If we spend a lot of credits,

2600
01:43:39,050 --> 01:43:41,620
we can eliminate a lot of lives.

2601
01:43:41,680 --> 01:43:44,050
- Is it a bomb? A bomb?
- We can eliminate quite a few.

2602
01:43:44,050 --> 01:43:45,490
- Does it wipe out the reserves?
- The reserves...

2603
01:43:45,490 --> 01:43:47,290
- No, from the team that has them.
- The team that has them.

2604
01:43:47,290 --> 01:43:48,790
Our benefit is...

2605
01:43:48,790 --> 01:43:51,560
- Do you spend diamonds?
- Yes. They become digital currency.

2606
01:43:51,690 --> 01:43:53,400
Since we have to carry diamonds around...

2607
01:43:53,400 --> 01:43:55,030
- Physical currency.
- The diamonds get converted.

2608
01:43:55,230 --> 01:43:57,800
- We can issue currency without limits.
- Issue currency.

2609
01:43:57,930 --> 01:44:01,040
If we use our skill,

2610
01:44:01,040 --> 01:44:02,540
we can get information.

2611
01:44:02,740 --> 01:44:05,240
- But...
- But we have to spend lives.

2612
01:44:05,240 --> 01:44:08,680
- So to actually use the skill...
- To use the skill,

2613
01:44:08,680 --> 01:44:10,080
we need a lot of lives.

2614
01:44:10,080 --> 01:44:12,610
- Other teams' resource information.
- Yes.

2615
01:44:15,750 --> 01:44:17,920
- Where are you going?
- I will submit a random answer.

2616
01:44:19,450 --> 01:44:20,790
How many times have you tried?

2617
01:44:20,790 --> 01:44:21,790
- Us?
- Yes.

2618
01:44:21,790 --> 01:44:23,390
We tried about five times,

2619
01:44:23,390 --> 01:44:25,630
but it seemed so far-fetched...

2620
01:44:25,990 --> 01:44:27,400
that we gave up on it.

2621
01:44:27,700 --> 01:44:29,300
We had no idea at all.

2622
01:44:29,300 --> 01:44:30,970
- Yes, seriously.
- We had not even been trying.

2623
01:44:31,570 --> 01:44:33,640
- Someone who has tried it...
- Failed.

2624
01:44:34,670 --> 01:44:35,740
This is incredibly difficult.

2625
01:44:38,240 --> 01:44:41,240
(Team Blue's skill development attempt:
Restructuring)

2626
01:44:41,240 --> 01:44:43,580
Maybe it means dismantling things like
state-controlled finance...

2627
01:44:43,580 --> 01:44:46,350
Or making something more flexible...

2628
01:44:46,350 --> 01:44:47,780
- Are they solving the question?
- Yes.

2629
01:44:48,420 --> 01:44:50,590
Have you tried "increase life reserves"
for Team White?

2630
01:44:51,020 --> 01:44:52,750
- No.
- Just...

2631
01:44:52,750 --> 01:44:54,590
forget all the economics...

2632
01:44:54,760 --> 01:44:56,160
and write "increase life reserves."

2633
01:44:56,590 --> 01:44:58,360
Would that not increase life reserves?

2634
01:44:59,690 --> 01:45:01,600
- That could be it.
- It could be.

2635
01:45:02,300 --> 01:45:03,430
Shall I try it?

2636
01:45:04,670 --> 01:45:05,700
Let us do it.

2637
01:45:06,300 --> 01:45:08,240
We do not want them to solve it, right?

2638
01:45:08,240 --> 01:45:09,670
- Life...
- Increase life reserves.

2639
01:45:10,640 --> 01:45:11,910
This one is Team White's.

2640
01:45:11,910 --> 01:45:13,110
Increase life reserves.

2641
01:45:13,110 --> 01:45:14,140
But this is Team White's, so...

2642
01:45:14,140 --> 01:45:16,010
- Go give it a try.
- Try it.

2643
01:45:16,010 --> 01:45:17,110
- Try it.
- Shall I?

2644
01:45:17,750 --> 01:45:19,310
I don't know if that is right.

2645
01:45:20,980 --> 01:45:23,050
Actually, I...

2646
01:45:23,720 --> 01:45:25,950
was not really offering my own ideas.

2647
01:45:26,350 --> 01:45:27,690
I was watching how things were going.

2648
01:45:27,690 --> 01:45:30,290
I acted like a big fool
who knew nothing...

2649
01:45:30,530 --> 01:45:32,060
and kept watching everyone...

2650
01:45:32,060 --> 01:45:34,230
while listening to what Black was saying.

2651
01:45:34,500 --> 01:45:36,730
Then Maillard and Vector started saying...

2652
01:45:36,730 --> 01:45:39,470
"Could it be simpler than we think?"

2653
01:45:39,470 --> 01:45:40,940
They threw that idea out there,

2654
01:45:41,240 --> 01:45:44,170
and it matched exactly what I had thought
that morning.

2655
01:45:44,710 --> 01:45:45,740
I thought...

2656
01:45:46,510 --> 01:45:49,080
if oil reserves represent lives...

2657
01:45:49,640 --> 01:45:52,180
Oil reserves could mean life reserves.

2658
01:45:55,850 --> 01:45:56,850
Wrong?

2659
01:45:58,290 --> 01:45:59,550
- Are you going to submit something?
- Yes.

2660
01:46:00,760 --> 01:46:01,760
I am going to give it a try.

2661
01:46:02,220 --> 01:46:03,690
I am just writing down anything
that comes to mind.

2662
01:46:08,360 --> 01:46:09,430
What could it be?

2663
01:46:10,600 --> 01:46:11,700
Darn it.

2664
01:46:12,600 --> 01:46:15,570
(Team White's skill development attempt)

2665
01:46:20,610 --> 01:46:22,680
(Oil reserves, life reserves, increase)

2666
01:46:22,680 --> 01:46:26,250
(Team White's skill development attempt)

2667
01:46:26,250 --> 01:46:29,280
We are checking your answer.
Please wait a moment.

2668
01:46:32,850 --> 01:46:34,860
You are close to the correct answer.

2669
01:46:35,390 --> 01:46:37,590
Please pick up a new answer sheet.

2670
01:46:47,870 --> 01:46:49,040
I was close.

2671
01:46:51,640 --> 01:46:53,410
Honestly, I was not surprised at first.

2672
01:46:53,410 --> 01:46:56,310
It took me about five seconds
to realize it...

2673
01:46:56,480 --> 01:46:59,910
because all I had heard until then was
"That is incorrect."

2674
01:47:00,050 --> 01:47:02,720
That is incorrect.

2675
01:47:03,720 --> 01:47:06,090
Maybe we are not meant to solve it yet?

2676
01:47:06,550 --> 01:47:09,490
"You are close to the correct answer."

2677
01:47:09,490 --> 01:47:11,430
I think I was actually the first
to hear that.

2678
01:47:11,730 --> 01:47:13,830
So I was right.
It was simpler than I thought.

2679
01:47:13,930 --> 01:47:16,560
I should combine all the words
from the lock.

2680
01:47:16,730 --> 01:47:19,770
We will now reveal the answers
to the skill development questions.

2681
01:47:20,570 --> 01:47:21,900
This feels like Black Monday.

2682
01:47:22,100 --> 01:47:24,640
Black... Oh, Black Monday!

2683
01:47:25,610 --> 01:47:28,080
(Lock: Production of staples like ramen
and flour is tied to oil reserves...)

2684
01:47:28,080 --> 01:47:29,610
(Ra)

2685
01:47:29,610 --> 01:47:32,750
(9)

2686
01:47:32,750 --> 01:47:35,620
(E)

2687
01:47:35,620 --> 01:47:36,920
(P)

2688
01:47:36,920 --> 01:47:40,590
Team White's answer. "Life reserves."

2689
01:47:41,590 --> 01:47:44,790
(Key: That day, we learned
a country could also default.)

2690
01:47:44,790 --> 01:47:46,330
(The day Korea officially requested
bailout assistance from the IMF)

2691
01:47:46,330 --> 01:47:47,960
(Lock: Once our culture and economy move
from rapid to relaxation growth...)

2692
01:47:47,960 --> 01:47:50,100
(19971121)

2693
01:47:50,100 --> 01:47:51,770
(When this sentence is completed)

2694
01:47:51,770 --> 01:47:55,740
Team Blue's answer.
"When this sentence is completed."

2695
01:47:56,700 --> 01:47:58,440
(Key: That winter, the beautiful windmill
burst with an enormous bubble.)

2696
01:47:58,440 --> 01:48:00,010
(The day the Dutch tulip bubble crashed)

2697
01:48:00,010 --> 01:48:01,980
(16370203)

2698
01:48:01,980 --> 01:48:04,780
(Lock: Development and cuts to
ten resources have decreasing deadlines)

2699
01:48:04,810 --> 01:48:08,720
Team Red's answer. "Decrease by ten."

2700
01:48:10,490 --> 01:48:13,390
When a team's skill development question
is completed...

2701
01:48:13,520 --> 01:48:14,660
(When this sentence is completed)

2702
01:48:14,660 --> 01:48:15,890
(Life reserves)

2703
01:48:15,890 --> 01:48:17,160
(Decrease by ten)

2704
01:48:17,160 --> 01:48:20,800
The answer takes effect immediately
in Community Town.

2705
01:48:21,660 --> 01:48:24,200
Information for
each team's skill development...

2706
01:48:24,700 --> 01:48:27,670
can be found in the dormitory books.

2707
01:48:28,240 --> 01:48:29,240
("Market's Memory")

2708
01:48:30,370 --> 01:48:32,310
(IMF: November 21)

2709
01:48:32,310 --> 01:48:33,310
("Money: A Story of Humanity")

2710
01:48:34,280 --> 01:48:36,140
(February 3, 1637)

2711
01:48:39,810 --> 01:48:41,750
"From now on, if our country's culture
and economy..."

2712
01:48:41,750 --> 01:48:45,150
"go beyond rapid growth and reach
relaxation growth..."

2713
01:48:45,550 --> 01:48:47,090
- And that is where it ends.
- "If it reaches..."

2714
01:48:47,890 --> 01:48:50,930
Should we bring dinner and talk some more?

2715
01:48:51,230 --> 01:48:52,760
- If you have something for dinner...
- Do you?

2716
01:48:52,930 --> 01:48:54,400
If you do, please eat as much as you like.

2717
01:48:54,530 --> 01:48:56,730
Should we bring food and keep talking?

2718
01:48:56,730 --> 01:48:58,670
- Yes.
- Seriously...

2719
01:48:59,500 --> 01:49:00,700
Are they waiting for us?

2720
01:49:00,940 --> 01:49:02,440
Paul did something huge.

2721
01:49:02,440 --> 01:49:03,710
- Something huge?
- Paul did something huge.

2722
01:49:03,710 --> 01:49:05,540
- There must be something.
- Seems like it.

2723
01:49:06,940 --> 01:49:09,740
Did anyone get "You are close to
the correct answer" when they submitted?

2724
01:49:09,740 --> 01:49:11,180
- No.
- Mine said I was close.

2725
01:49:11,180 --> 01:49:13,550
That would drive you crazy, right?
It drove me crazy.

2726
01:49:13,720 --> 01:49:16,050
I just kept it really simple.

2727
01:49:16,380 --> 01:49:18,520
I wrote "oil reserves"
and then added parentheses...

2728
01:49:18,520 --> 01:49:20,890
and wrote, "life reserves increase."

2729
01:49:20,960 --> 01:49:23,560
But what if it decreases instead?

2730
01:49:24,030 --> 01:49:25,560
If it increases, everyone is happy.

2731
01:49:25,560 --> 01:49:27,100
Then our ultimate weapon is pointless.

2732
01:49:27,300 --> 01:49:30,900
But if oil reserves or production
falls drastically...

2733
01:49:31,100 --> 01:49:32,700
- Then we are doomed.
- Our inflation...

2734
01:49:32,700 --> 01:49:35,200
- gets even worse?
- Then we would have no choice but war.

2735
01:49:35,200 --> 01:49:36,570
- It would be unavoidable.
- Right.

2736
01:49:36,970 --> 01:49:40,280
If it decreases, there is no benefit.
Why would we do it?

2737
01:49:40,980 --> 01:49:42,410
Because it gives us
unlimited issuance rights.

2738
01:49:42,410 --> 01:49:44,250
The survivors on our team make more money.

2739
01:49:44,250 --> 01:49:45,780
- It would greatly benefit a few people.
- Exactly.

2740
01:49:46,250 --> 01:49:47,250
It would divide us internally.

2741
01:49:47,250 --> 01:49:49,480
It would completely divide Team White too.

2742
01:49:49,480 --> 01:49:50,550
- Right?
- Yes.

2743
01:49:51,050 --> 01:49:52,990
- Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

2744
01:49:52,990 --> 01:49:54,490
I am almost done eating.

2745
01:49:54,720 --> 01:49:57,430
You can keep eating.

2746
01:49:57,960 --> 01:50:00,300
Just listen
and make yourselves comfortable.

2747
01:50:00,600 --> 01:50:04,730
Is it really okay to let Team White...

2748
01:50:04,730 --> 01:50:06,270
develop its skill?

2749
01:50:07,140 --> 01:50:09,900
Because at first,

2750
01:50:09,900 --> 01:50:11,810
they made it sound as if,
out of generosity,

2751
01:50:11,970 --> 01:50:14,940
- they chose not to issue more diamonds.
- Yes.

2752
01:50:14,940 --> 01:50:17,280
- But it turned out there were limits.
- Why did they hide that from us?

2753
01:50:17,280 --> 01:50:19,250
They said the restrictions are lifted
after skill development, right?

2754
01:50:19,250 --> 01:50:21,780
- They said they could go without limits.
- But they said this too earlier.

2755
01:50:21,780 --> 01:50:23,450
If we push them too hard,

2756
01:50:23,450 --> 01:50:26,590
say only one or two of them are left,

2757
01:50:26,750 --> 01:50:29,990
they would not need any lives anymore...

2758
01:50:29,990 --> 01:50:30,990
or anything else.

2759
01:50:30,990 --> 01:50:33,460
They said,
"We can produce diamonds like mad..."

2760
01:50:33,700 --> 01:50:36,500
"and monopolize the prize."
They brought that up.

2761
01:50:36,500 --> 01:50:38,470
It had crossed their minds, right?

2762
01:50:38,930 --> 01:50:40,870
Of course staying alive matters right now.

2763
01:50:41,000 --> 01:50:44,110
But near the end,
only the one with a life will survive.

2764
01:50:44,210 --> 01:50:47,280
That very person could make your prize
worth just one cent.

2765
01:50:49,080 --> 01:50:51,650
Once the restrictions on issuance are
fully lifted,

2766
01:50:52,280 --> 01:50:55,150
the system will change
and allow that person to do that.

2767
01:50:55,320 --> 01:50:57,620
- That's why I'm being cautious.
- Hyperinflation.

2768
01:50:58,090 --> 01:50:59,320
- Hyperinflation.
- Yes.

2769
01:50:59,320 --> 01:51:00,660
Team White is evil.

2770
01:51:02,190 --> 01:51:03,390
- Right.
- Team Black is an angel.

2771
01:51:03,390 --> 01:51:04,660
Vector...

2772
01:51:05,960 --> 01:51:08,800
getting the answer as soon as possible
would greatly favor us...

2773
01:51:08,800 --> 01:51:10,570
- and not Team White.
- He must get the answer.

2774
01:51:12,030 --> 01:51:15,500
If anything pops into our heads,
let's tell Vector first.

2775
01:51:20,170 --> 01:51:21,280
Shall we go back?

2776
01:51:21,580 --> 01:51:23,040
We should read books or something.

2777
01:51:26,810 --> 01:51:29,120
It's a relief that
we have enough food to survive.

2778
01:51:29,120 --> 01:51:30,420
I know, right?

2779
01:51:30,820 --> 01:51:32,290
How did they move the fridge?

2780
01:51:32,750 --> 01:51:34,320
- What?
- How did they move the fridge?

2781
01:51:34,520 --> 01:51:36,320
Exactly. I mean, even the fridge?

2782
01:51:38,990 --> 01:51:41,560
- Let's cook first.
- Should I heat up some water?

2783
01:51:41,560 --> 01:51:43,230
I'll turn the kettle on
and then heat it up.

2784
01:51:43,230 --> 01:51:45,030
The ramyeon smells amazing.

2785
01:51:45,030 --> 01:51:46,700
- I'm starving.
- Gosh.

2786
01:51:47,270 --> 01:51:49,340
It's not bad, is it?
If you think about it...

2787
01:51:49,700 --> 01:51:50,770
It's so good.

2788
01:51:51,170 --> 01:51:53,370
- I love ramyeon.
- I don't really like ramyeon,

2789
01:51:53,910 --> 01:51:55,240
- but this is so good.
- For real.

2790
01:51:56,280 --> 01:51:58,710
- We look like bums. My nose is running.
- You can't just dig into it.

2791
01:51:58,710 --> 01:52:00,880
- You must savor it.
- Did Yukgaejang always taste like this?

2792
01:52:00,880 --> 01:52:02,520
- Isn't it delicious?
- The taste feels new.

2793
01:52:04,690 --> 01:52:05,690
Really.

2794
01:52:05,850 --> 01:52:06,950
- Yesterday...
- Isn't it good?

2795
01:52:07,390 --> 01:52:09,160
- It's delicious.
- Let's issue a load of currency today...

2796
01:52:09,360 --> 01:52:10,530
and spend a ton tomorrow.

2797
01:52:10,530 --> 01:52:12,030
Everyone is dead meat during lunch.

2798
01:52:12,590 --> 01:52:13,590
This is too good.

2799
01:52:13,590 --> 01:52:15,130
But then, we become dead meat.

2800
01:52:16,930 --> 01:52:18,230
We can't use our money despite having it.

2801
01:52:18,230 --> 01:52:20,100
Exactly. It's meaningless.

2802
01:52:20,540 --> 01:52:22,540
The fact that we have money
but can't actually use it right now...

2803
01:52:22,540 --> 01:52:23,910
- is a powerful lesson in itself.
- Can you give me some?

2804
01:52:24,910 --> 01:52:26,410
Team White.

2805
01:52:28,380 --> 01:52:30,910
In the worst-case scenario,

2806
01:52:31,250 --> 01:52:33,480
would you think about eliminating
one of us?

2807
01:52:33,750 --> 01:52:37,120
Here's what I thought.
Say that one of us survived.

2808
01:52:37,250 --> 01:52:39,950
As the leader, I use a life for myself...

2809
01:52:39,950 --> 01:52:42,390
but didn't for the rest,
and you two get eliminated.

2810
01:52:42,390 --> 01:52:44,560
In that case, I'd live alone
but wouldn't need the lives.

2811
01:52:44,560 --> 01:52:47,130
Some may think,
"I'll live until the end..."

2812
01:52:47,130 --> 01:52:49,130
- "even if someone attacks me."
- Of course.

2813
01:52:49,130 --> 01:52:50,800
But that's our decision to make.

2814
01:52:50,800 --> 01:52:52,970
Did you feel like there was no need now?

2815
01:52:53,130 --> 01:52:54,140
Need?

2816
01:52:54,140 --> 01:52:55,840
Shouldn't we see the situation first?

2817
01:52:56,100 --> 01:52:59,270
If the time comes when it's needed,
then of course,

2818
01:52:59,270 --> 01:53:01,510
my surviving is the most important thing.

2819
01:53:01,980 --> 01:53:05,780
But then again,
people's hearts are bound to waver.

2820
01:53:06,050 --> 01:53:08,480
The three of us are very different.

2821
01:53:08,480 --> 01:53:11,620
But we definitely make up for...

2822
01:53:11,620 --> 01:53:14,160
what each of us lacks.

2823
01:53:14,160 --> 01:53:17,490
Things are going forward
but while rattling.

2824
01:53:17,760 --> 01:53:20,130
If not, the three of us would be...

2825
01:53:20,130 --> 01:53:23,360
standing at different spots, isolated.

2826
01:53:23,530 --> 01:53:24,570
But we've come together...

2827
01:53:24,570 --> 01:53:27,770
and somehow, things are going forward,
but with slight difficulties.

2828
01:53:28,800 --> 01:53:32,340
It's strange. I feel this reassurance,

2829
01:53:32,340 --> 01:53:34,840
and yet, I'm not sure
if I should feel this warmth...

2830
01:53:34,840 --> 01:53:36,210
on a survival show.

2831
01:53:36,210 --> 01:53:39,980
I've always worked and played alone
on any survival shows.

2832
01:53:39,980 --> 01:53:41,720
(Genie, TV entertainer)

2833
01:53:41,720 --> 01:53:43,680
This is all just too awkward for me.

2834
01:53:45,520 --> 01:53:48,560
If one of us were able to cut someone off,

2835
01:53:48,560 --> 01:53:50,630
it'd be you.

2836
01:53:51,560 --> 01:53:53,390
- But I don't mean it in a mean way.
- Listen.

2837
01:53:53,390 --> 01:53:55,100
- You get it, right?
- I get it, you know?

2838
01:53:55,300 --> 01:53:58,530
- Everything was an individual game.
- Right.

2839
01:53:58,800 --> 01:54:02,570
My sole purpose was to survive all alone.

2840
01:54:02,570 --> 01:54:04,010
In a way, this is my first time playing...

2841
01:54:04,010 --> 01:54:05,670
- as a team.
- Right.

2842
01:54:05,840 --> 01:54:07,580
It's making my heart...

2843
01:54:07,580 --> 01:54:09,880
- all warm and fuzzy.
- I see.

2844
01:54:09,880 --> 01:54:12,580
I'm starting to doubt my character.

2845
01:54:15,750 --> 01:54:16,850
Soon,

2846
01:54:17,420 --> 01:54:20,820
today's Majority Rules Game will begin.

2847
01:54:21,160 --> 01:54:24,260
Residents, please gather at the Town Hall.

2848
01:54:24,260 --> 01:54:25,390
Good gracious.

2849
01:54:27,200 --> 01:54:28,860
- Hi. Sit.
- Today's speech...

2850
01:54:28,860 --> 01:54:30,500
might only last for 30 minutes.

2851
01:54:31,530 --> 01:54:33,330
- I like bananas.
- Honestly,

2852
01:54:33,570 --> 01:54:35,700
on the first day, I was like,
"Bananas? What? For real?"

2853
01:54:35,700 --> 01:54:37,710
- We were like, "Bananas? Why?"
- "What's up with the bananas?"

2854
01:54:37,710 --> 01:54:39,340
There was plenty left on Day One.

2855
01:54:39,340 --> 01:54:40,680
- Exactly.
- How many are left?

2856
01:54:40,940 --> 01:54:41,980
It must be good.

2857
01:54:41,980 --> 01:54:44,050
- Bananas!
- So devotedly...

2858
01:54:44,450 --> 01:54:46,950
- I don't see many bananas today.
- Bananas!

2859
01:54:46,950 --> 01:54:48,080
We have 15.

2860
01:54:48,420 --> 01:54:50,520
- This is bad.
- So one banana per person.

2861
01:54:50,520 --> 01:54:52,220
- It's one per person.
- Even the bananas?

2862
01:54:53,250 --> 01:54:56,220
- Let's leave this there.
- Seriously.

2863
01:54:56,790 --> 01:54:59,030
- Come on.
- Fine.

2864
01:54:59,030 --> 01:55:00,290
That was why? Go ahead.

2865
01:55:00,290 --> 01:55:02,530
- And so?
- No, I should think more about it.

2866
01:55:03,970 --> 01:55:06,300
The topic of
today's Majority Rules Game is,

2867
01:55:07,240 --> 01:55:10,070
"Before debating fairness and justice
in society,"

2868
01:55:10,570 --> 01:55:13,740
"securing my own financial freedom..."

2869
01:55:13,940 --> 01:55:16,980
"should be the top priority."

2870
01:55:17,480 --> 01:55:21,220
Looks like it'll be 9 to 1
in favor of practicality.

2871
01:55:21,220 --> 01:55:22,380
(Salt, Writer)

2872
01:55:22,380 --> 01:55:24,690
Based on the data I've collected so far...

2873
01:55:24,690 --> 01:55:27,320
from the Majority Rules Game,

2874
01:55:27,560 --> 01:55:29,420
the majority of us here...

2875
01:55:29,420 --> 01:55:33,230
will prioritize practicality.

2876
01:55:33,230 --> 01:55:34,260
Practicality.

2877
01:55:35,230 --> 01:55:37,060
(Meaning: Disagree, Practicality: Agree)

2878
01:55:37,060 --> 01:55:40,500
(In reality, the majority of residents
chose meaning.)

2879
01:55:42,970 --> 01:55:44,740
- May I make a short one?
- Of course.

2880
01:55:44,740 --> 01:55:45,770
Great.

2881
01:55:45,940 --> 01:55:47,240
Think about it.

2882
01:55:47,310 --> 01:55:50,850
The fewer resources we had today,

2883
01:55:51,550 --> 01:55:56,080
the decisions we made were
far from fair and just.

2884
01:55:56,450 --> 01:55:57,920
I'm not sure if it was a joke,

2885
01:55:57,920 --> 01:55:59,850
but people kept saying,
"Shall we go to war?"

2886
01:56:00,290 --> 01:56:01,990
"Who should we say goodbye to?
Who should we kill?"

2887
01:56:01,990 --> 01:56:03,520
Such questions were caused by...

2888
01:56:03,520 --> 01:56:06,360
- When did that happen?
- the lack of resources.

2889
01:56:06,490 --> 01:56:08,600
Financial freedom should be secured...

2890
01:56:08,800 --> 01:56:13,000
before going on about
a fair society and justice.

2891
01:56:13,300 --> 01:56:15,670
I went all out yesterday
and the day before...

2892
01:56:15,670 --> 01:56:17,140
during the Majority Rules Game.

2893
01:56:17,270 --> 01:56:20,140
If I go all out again,

2894
01:56:20,140 --> 01:56:24,050
I might become the target
when the values code...

2895
01:56:24,310 --> 01:56:25,810
comes into play.

2896
01:56:25,810 --> 01:56:27,550
So I decided to argue the opposing side.

2897
01:56:27,720 --> 01:56:29,220
It was to hide the code.

2898
01:56:29,280 --> 01:56:32,650
Having people find out about it
seemed like a bad idea.

2899
01:56:32,990 --> 01:56:36,190
So our plan was to argue
the opposite today.

2900
01:56:36,560 --> 01:56:39,290
For now, I'm calling dibs on the banana.

2901
01:56:39,630 --> 01:56:42,530
When you're already having a hard time
trying to make your ends meet,

2902
01:56:42,530 --> 01:56:45,170
helping others isn't easy at all.

2903
01:56:45,500 --> 01:56:47,670
In that sense,
the concept of the Invisible Hand is...

2904
01:56:47,670 --> 01:56:51,640
relying on and leaving it
to the people's financial greed,

2905
01:56:51,640 --> 01:56:54,780
which will eventually help
the market thrive.

2906
01:56:54,880 --> 01:56:57,880
Before we start debating
what's fair or what's just,

2907
01:56:57,980 --> 01:56:59,050
I think the market economy is...

2908
01:56:59,050 --> 01:57:03,020
a system that works well
when we leave it to the invisible hand...

2909
01:57:03,020 --> 01:57:04,690
and to people's desire to work hard...

2910
01:57:04,850 --> 01:57:07,360
and achieve financial freedom...

2911
01:57:07,360 --> 01:57:08,960
for themselves.

2912
01:57:09,020 --> 01:57:11,260
As Genie mentioned,
we should take care of ourselves first,

2913
01:57:11,260 --> 01:57:13,890
and then help others
when we have the means to. The end.

2914
01:57:13,890 --> 01:57:17,160
The top priority is my effort
and financial achievements.

2915
01:57:17,260 --> 01:57:20,030
Next is social fairness and justice.
If we keep it that way,

2916
01:57:20,100 --> 01:57:23,770
we wouldn't be trying to fill ourselves up
with bananas.

2917
01:57:23,940 --> 01:57:28,010
We'd be able to eat something
more delicious than that.

2918
01:57:28,110 --> 01:57:31,550
With that,
I'm taking the practicality side today.

2919
01:57:31,850 --> 01:57:35,250
Even Boss said, "I agree with Genie."

2920
01:57:35,250 --> 01:57:37,620
What Izaha said
was also the same as what I said.

2921
01:57:37,890 --> 01:57:39,950
What I brought up was...

2922
01:57:40,120 --> 01:57:42,720
on the right track...

2923
01:57:42,720 --> 01:57:46,030
since everyone was on the same track.

2924
01:57:46,730 --> 01:57:48,400
I need to munch on a banana.

2925
01:57:48,400 --> 01:57:52,400
In the end, if there's no fairness
or justice in society,

2926
01:57:52,670 --> 01:57:56,970
I find it meaningless to try to secure
our financial freedom.

2927
01:57:56,970 --> 01:57:59,770
If there's no meaning,

2928
01:57:59,770 --> 01:58:02,110
life becomes vague. The end.

2929
01:58:03,040 --> 01:58:04,410
(Pitou first spoke up about
what the code means to her.)

2930
01:58:04,410 --> 01:58:05,480
That was funny.

2931
01:58:06,150 --> 01:58:07,620
I love the way she talks.

2932
01:58:07,750 --> 01:58:09,280
I'll put it into simple words.

2933
01:58:09,280 --> 01:58:12,620
In short, we don't say
we've gained financial freedom...

2934
01:58:12,790 --> 01:58:15,860
when we break the rules to get it.

2935
01:58:15,990 --> 01:58:17,090
I'm on the disagreeing side.

2936
01:58:17,260 --> 01:58:19,060
We've seen too many countries.

2937
01:58:19,060 --> 01:58:20,730
We've seen far too many cases where,

2938
01:58:20,730 --> 01:58:22,900
in countries without fairness and justice,

2939
01:58:22,900 --> 01:58:25,970
people's economic freedom is crushed
or put at serious risk.

2940
01:58:25,970 --> 01:58:28,400
We can always work together.

2941
01:58:28,570 --> 01:58:30,970
I've become someone
who strives for meaning now.

2942
01:58:31,410 --> 01:58:33,440
I had an office job for years.

2943
01:58:33,740 --> 01:58:36,510
I had an office job for 6 to 7 years...

2944
01:58:36,510 --> 01:58:39,650
that's unrelated to my current job.

2945
01:58:40,250 --> 01:58:42,220
One day, I was suddenly hit with
such a thought.

2946
01:58:42,720 --> 01:58:45,690
Something along the lines of,
"I'm going to die one day."

2947
01:58:46,850 --> 01:58:48,260
"So why am I here, doing this?"

2948
01:58:48,660 --> 01:58:52,790
So I quit my job
and decided to pursue my dream...

2949
01:58:52,790 --> 01:58:55,000
of making board games,
which had always been my hobby.

2950
01:58:55,400 --> 01:58:57,770
"I see. The reason for existence is..."

2951
01:58:57,770 --> 01:59:00,430
"much more important to me."

2952
01:59:00,700 --> 01:59:03,200
What means more to me is the meaning.

2953
01:59:03,200 --> 01:59:04,840
That's what I can say to you.

2954
01:59:04,840 --> 01:59:07,640
I used to be someone
who was all about practicality...

2955
01:59:07,640 --> 01:59:09,480
up until a few years ago.

2956
01:59:10,210 --> 01:59:14,150
Gaining much financial freedom
was very important to me.

2957
01:59:14,150 --> 01:59:17,890
But at some point,
I had an experience that...

2958
01:59:17,890 --> 01:59:22,760
made me realize that
social security and stability...

2959
01:59:22,990 --> 01:59:25,490
can actually give me a greater sense of...

2960
01:59:25,490 --> 01:59:27,660
emotional comfort than financial freedom.

2961
01:59:28,200 --> 01:59:29,600
Financial freedom...

2962
01:59:29,600 --> 01:59:31,700
did not guarantee emotional stability.

2963
01:59:31,970 --> 01:59:35,170
You could say my perspective changed.

2964
01:59:35,540 --> 01:59:38,710
At first, we were losing.

2965
01:59:39,110 --> 01:59:42,010
But then,
things were dramatically turning around...

2966
01:59:42,010 --> 01:59:43,580
the more people started speaking up.

2967
01:59:43,980 --> 01:59:45,650
I never saw it coming.

2968
01:59:45,650 --> 01:59:48,320
People are full of surprises.
It's really interesting.

2969
01:59:48,650 --> 01:59:51,920
Those who want to discuss...

2970
01:59:51,920 --> 01:59:54,820
society's fairness and justice first...

2971
01:59:55,090 --> 01:59:57,590
are those who already have...

2972
01:59:57,590 --> 01:59:59,930
financial freedom.

2973
02:00:00,230 --> 02:00:02,600
Our society has already achieved...

2974
02:00:02,600 --> 02:00:05,600
a certain level of economic freedom,

2975
02:00:05,730 --> 02:00:07,170
which is why we have
the luxury of discussing...

2976
02:00:07,170 --> 02:00:09,200
fairness and justice in society.

2977
02:00:09,440 --> 02:00:12,010
You know how you can put
a mask on a child...

2978
02:00:12,010 --> 02:00:13,670
only after you put yours on...

2979
02:00:13,670 --> 02:00:16,080
on a plane about to crash?

2980
02:00:16,480 --> 02:00:18,910
The fact that you have the time
to think about it means...

2981
02:00:19,180 --> 02:00:21,950
you already have financial freedom.

2982
02:00:23,020 --> 02:00:25,050
Was it the movie "The Purge?"

2983
02:00:25,050 --> 02:00:28,160
There's a country
where one law is abolished every year.

2984
02:00:28,660 --> 02:00:30,590
No matter how rich you are,

2985
02:00:31,060 --> 02:00:34,700
just one day of injustice
and unfairness...

2986
02:00:34,700 --> 02:00:37,870
will make you live in fear.

2987
02:00:37,870 --> 02:00:40,730
Gaining financial freedom
in such a situation...

2988
02:00:40,730 --> 02:00:42,400
is meaningless.

2989
02:00:42,970 --> 02:00:44,810
I'm on the disagreeing side.

2990
02:00:45,010 --> 02:00:47,110
If it were the usual me,

2991
02:00:47,110 --> 02:00:49,210
I would've gone for the meaning,
at all costs.

2992
02:00:49,310 --> 02:00:52,250
But the thought that...

2993
02:00:52,250 --> 02:00:55,220
I wouldn't go for the meaning today
crossed my mind first.

2994
02:00:55,580 --> 02:00:58,320
When thinking about today's situation,

2995
02:00:58,490 --> 02:01:00,090
some teams...

2996
02:01:00,090 --> 02:01:02,360
had to appeal for fairness.

2997
02:01:02,360 --> 02:01:04,560
We were put in such a situation.

2998
02:01:04,960 --> 02:01:07,060
For those particular people,

2999
02:01:07,060 --> 02:01:10,230
pleading for justice or fairness was...

3000
02:01:10,230 --> 02:01:14,170
the only way
they'd secure financial freedom.

3001
02:01:14,300 --> 02:01:16,400
It was quite fascinating to see.

3002
02:01:16,400 --> 02:01:18,240
"In society, I'd choose A."

3003
02:01:18,240 --> 02:01:19,970
"But here, I'm choosing B."

3004
02:01:20,010 --> 02:01:23,510
I'm someone who believes that
making decisions gains momentum.

3005
02:01:23,740 --> 02:01:25,980
If it feels right, I rush things.

3006
02:01:25,980 --> 02:01:28,450
If it still feels right the next day,

3007
02:01:28,450 --> 02:01:31,250
I come to believe that
it's the forever right choice.

3008
02:01:31,290 --> 02:01:33,090
That's why I'm the type to sometimes...

3009
02:01:33,090 --> 02:01:35,490
put on the brakes
when making my decisions.

3010
02:01:35,490 --> 02:01:37,690
For those claiming practicality,

3011
02:01:37,690 --> 02:01:41,130
I hope you'd choose meaning
on some days...

3012
02:01:41,130 --> 02:01:44,500
and indulge in a little vanity
as complex beings.

3013
02:01:44,500 --> 02:01:47,670
I'll leave you
with this slightly strange thought.

3014
02:01:47,670 --> 02:01:49,000
- It's a tie.
- Gosh.

3015
02:01:49,100 --> 02:01:50,370
- Is it a tie?
- It's a tie.

3016
02:01:50,370 --> 02:01:52,010
- Is she the last in this tied situation?
- I'm nervous.

3017
02:01:52,010 --> 02:01:53,440
The casting vote.

3018
02:01:53,440 --> 02:01:54,480
No!

3019
02:01:54,480 --> 02:01:56,880
- I have a feeling she's on our side.
- I have a hunch.

3020
02:01:56,980 --> 02:01:58,610
- Let's see.
- I'm nervous.

3021
02:01:58,610 --> 02:01:59,850
- What is her choice?
- What is her choice?

3022
02:01:59,850 --> 02:02:02,920
(Fairness and justice: 6,
Financial freedom: 6)

3023
02:02:02,920 --> 02:02:04,850
I'll make the decisive move.

3024
02:02:05,620 --> 02:02:07,520
I'm going with meaning.

3025
02:02:08,060 --> 02:02:10,020
- Nice.
- Nice.

3026
02:02:10,320 --> 02:02:11,460
Nice.

3027
02:02:11,730 --> 02:02:14,330
If there were an invisible hand,

3028
02:02:14,330 --> 02:02:17,460
the market would thrive
depending on individuals' greed.

3029
02:02:17,460 --> 02:02:20,470
That's the great principle of capitalism.

3030
02:02:20,570 --> 02:02:22,240
But imagine...

3031
02:02:22,240 --> 02:02:24,570
we're in a state of war
of all against all.

3032
02:02:24,570 --> 02:02:26,210
We're in a state of nature.

3033
02:02:26,240 --> 02:02:29,180
Let's say I used my self-interest
to make money,

3034
02:02:29,280 --> 02:02:31,050
and then all of a sudden,
Paul comes along,

3035
02:02:31,050 --> 02:02:32,210
grabs me by the collar, and says,

3036
02:02:32,210 --> 02:02:33,480
"Give me everything you've got."

3037
02:02:33,480 --> 02:02:34,880
- I look like it.
- Say that it happened.

3038
02:02:34,880 --> 02:02:36,650
- How come?
- I look like I would do that.

3039
02:02:36,680 --> 02:02:38,590
But if there are no laws,

3040
02:02:38,590 --> 02:02:40,990
institutions,
or mechanisms to restrain Paul,

3041
02:02:41,020 --> 02:02:44,190
then I don't think my financial freedom
means anything.

3042
02:02:44,330 --> 02:02:47,860
What it means to live
in a capitalist society is...

3043
02:02:48,000 --> 02:02:49,600
existing within a system.

3044
02:02:49,600 --> 02:02:52,670
When discussing fairness
versus financial freedom in society,

3045
02:02:52,770 --> 02:02:55,740
who would even think about gaining it
by killing the person next to you?

3046
02:02:55,740 --> 02:02:57,770
"Do you die if it's not fair?"

3047
02:02:57,870 --> 02:03:01,180
It suddenly sounded very extreme.

3048
02:03:01,240 --> 02:03:04,850
In my opinion, she read too much into it,

3049
02:03:05,010 --> 02:03:07,280
and I wanted to say it.

3050
02:03:07,280 --> 02:03:08,680
I wanted to rebut so badly.

3051
02:03:08,820 --> 02:03:11,590
Someone brought up the idea of
self-interested individuals.

3052
02:03:11,690 --> 02:03:15,890
The economic actor Adam Smith described...

3053
02:03:15,920 --> 02:03:18,060
isn't simply a selfish individual.

3054
02:03:18,090 --> 02:03:20,260
It's a rational,
self-interested individual.

3055
02:03:20,360 --> 02:03:22,130
And that relationship
is built on mutual trust.

3056
02:03:22,230 --> 02:03:24,930
I wrote down every point...

3057
02:03:24,930 --> 02:03:27,070
Leia brought up and was like,

3058
02:03:27,070 --> 02:03:28,240
"That right there."

3059
02:03:28,240 --> 02:03:29,940
"I'm going to rebut it."

3060
02:03:29,940 --> 02:03:31,410
"I'm going to counter that point."

3061
02:03:31,410 --> 02:03:33,270
I was uneasy,

3062
02:03:33,270 --> 02:03:34,810
wanting to go up on the podium.

3063
02:03:34,910 --> 02:03:36,380
I hope you don't think of...

3064
02:03:36,380 --> 02:03:38,210
financial freedom as simply chasing money.

3065
02:03:38,210 --> 02:03:39,650
I want you to keep in mind that...

3066
02:03:39,650 --> 02:03:41,320
financial freedom can only be maximized...

3067
02:03:41,320 --> 02:03:43,650
when we have a system built on...

3068
02:03:43,650 --> 02:03:45,390
fairness and justice.

3069
02:03:45,390 --> 02:03:46,420
The end.

3070
02:03:46,420 --> 02:03:48,090
(Fairness and justice: 7,
Financial freedom: 6)

3071
02:03:48,090 --> 02:03:49,160
- Is everyone done?
- Go.

3072
02:03:49,160 --> 02:03:50,890
- Can I weigh in again?
- Go ahead.

3073
02:03:51,060 --> 02:03:53,830
Hearing that, I thought...

3074
02:03:53,890 --> 02:03:56,130
going as far as talking about survival...

3075
02:03:56,130 --> 02:03:59,370
when it comes to fairness and justice was
a little too extreme.

3076
02:03:59,370 --> 02:04:02,240
The justice and fairness
I had in mind were,

3077
02:04:02,540 --> 02:04:04,240
"People were given a fair chance
to take the test."

3078
02:04:04,240 --> 02:04:06,440
"Everyone had a fair chance to participate
in economic activity."

3079
02:04:06,440 --> 02:04:09,610
That was how far I thought those two went.

3080
02:04:09,940 --> 02:04:12,280
I couldn't help but wonder...

3081
02:04:12,280 --> 02:04:15,350
if this was something
to go to such extremes...

3082
02:04:15,350 --> 02:04:16,620
as to involve survival.

3083
02:04:16,820 --> 02:04:18,390
I'm sorry to interrupt.

3084
02:04:18,390 --> 02:04:21,020
Speaking up at the podium is all good,

3085
02:04:21,090 --> 02:04:22,790
but how about just chit-chatting...

3086
02:04:22,790 --> 02:04:24,930
- Like a casual discussion?
- after everyone has had a turn?

3087
02:04:25,430 --> 02:04:27,360
Let me add to what I said earlier.

3088
02:04:27,360 --> 02:04:29,330
Here's why I deliberately used
the survival metaphor.

3089
02:04:29,330 --> 02:04:32,270
At the very least, there are things
we can all agree on.

3090
02:04:32,330 --> 02:04:34,170
Like, "Come on,"

3091
02:04:34,170 --> 02:04:36,240
"protecting human life is fair and just."

3092
02:04:36,240 --> 02:04:37,640
"That's a basic human right."

3093
02:04:37,640 --> 02:04:39,640
So, the order of things
you're describing is this.

3094
02:04:39,640 --> 02:04:41,110
"This person, this person,
and this person are..."

3095
02:04:41,110 --> 02:04:42,280
"each pursuing their own self-interest,"

3096
02:04:42,280 --> 02:04:43,480
- "and in that process,"
- Yes.

3097
02:04:43,480 --> 02:04:45,180
"the system is formed."

3098
02:04:45,180 --> 02:04:46,180
- That's possible.
- Right?

3099
02:04:46,180 --> 02:04:47,710
- But...
- That's how the safety net...

3100
02:04:47,710 --> 02:04:49,220
- In the first place,
- and protective framework are created.

3101
02:04:49,220 --> 02:04:50,350
- if I...
- That's the order.

3102
02:04:50,350 --> 02:04:51,520
Hold on.

3103
02:04:51,520 --> 02:04:52,650
- This is a difference in perspective.
- True.

3104
02:04:52,650 --> 02:04:56,320
If all I cared about was practicality
and I had a narrow view of the world,

3105
02:04:56,390 --> 02:04:58,660
then think about the old days,
like tribal or class-based societies.

3106
02:04:58,660 --> 02:04:59,790
I'd work my butt off,

3107
02:04:59,790 --> 02:05:01,160
but the chief would take everything.

3108
02:05:01,500 --> 02:05:03,030
I'd think, "This feels wrong."

3109
02:05:03,030 --> 02:05:05,330
That's how people began questioning
the social classes.

3110
02:05:05,700 --> 02:05:07,230
Look at how she loves debates.

3111
02:05:07,230 --> 02:05:09,070
- But there won't be one tomorrow.
- Right?

3112
02:05:09,070 --> 02:05:10,800
- The final peace.
- There's no debate tomorrow.

3113
02:05:10,800 --> 02:05:11,910
There will only be war.

3114
02:05:14,480 --> 02:05:16,840
(Majority Rules Game)

3115
02:05:16,840 --> 02:05:20,510
You will now vote
for the Majority Rules Game.

3116
02:05:21,380 --> 02:05:23,850
Once all the residents
have cast their votes,

3117
02:05:24,220 --> 02:05:25,690
today's Majority...

3118
02:05:25,720 --> 02:05:28,720
and MVP will be announced shortly.

3119
02:05:29,660 --> 02:05:31,330
- What will it be?
- What will it be?

3120
02:05:31,330 --> 02:05:32,630
- What will it be?
- What will it be?

3121
02:05:32,630 --> 02:05:34,500
Don't tell me it's 11 to 2.

3122
02:05:34,500 --> 02:05:35,700
- Let's go.
- Let the disagreeing side win.

3123
02:05:35,700 --> 02:05:37,700
- Please.
- Please be 13 to 0. That'd practically...

3124
02:05:38,000 --> 02:05:39,100
- be funny.
- Please.

3125
02:05:41,070 --> 02:05:42,840
Gosh, did you see that? I got it right.

3126
02:05:43,840 --> 02:05:44,910
Eleven to two?

3127
02:05:44,910 --> 02:05:47,010
- Unbelievable.
- Only two?

3128
02:05:47,040 --> 02:05:48,180
Eleven to two?

3129
02:05:48,180 --> 02:05:49,710
- The two should be awarded.
- Right?

3130
02:05:50,080 --> 02:05:51,710
- The two.
- Those two are amazing.

3131
02:05:51,710 --> 02:05:52,850
They deserve an award.

3132
02:05:53,550 --> 02:05:54,680
Yes, Boss!

3133
02:05:56,250 --> 02:05:58,550
- That was cute!
- I didn't expect such a low number.

3134
02:05:58,550 --> 02:06:00,520
Goodness, these people.

3135
02:06:00,520 --> 02:06:01,690
To switch sides like that?

3136
02:06:01,720 --> 02:06:03,960
But they did exactly what the game...

3137
02:06:03,960 --> 02:06:05,560
was designed for.

3138
02:06:05,760 --> 02:06:09,300
Gaining points by switching sides is...

3139
02:06:09,300 --> 02:06:11,130
a much more beneficial move.

3140
02:06:11,430 --> 02:06:14,270
I did think it was foolish of me
not to switch sides.

3141
02:06:14,270 --> 02:06:15,940
But I'd rather be a fool...

3142
02:06:15,940 --> 02:06:18,410
and keep my belief.
That matters more to me.

3143
02:06:19,140 --> 02:06:21,410
To pursue practical interests today,

3144
02:06:21,410 --> 02:06:22,740
I went with the side
where I'd gain points,

3145
02:06:22,740 --> 02:06:23,940
even if it's just one.

3146
02:06:23,940 --> 02:06:25,910
With that, I chose the disagreeing side.

3147
02:06:25,910 --> 02:06:27,380
(Meaning: Salt, Pitou, Donkey, Izaha
Vector, Leia, Paul, Hamlet, Siseon, Boss)

3148
02:06:27,380 --> 02:06:28,450
(Practicality: Luna, Maillard, Genie)

3149
02:06:28,450 --> 02:06:29,450
(Meaning: Salt, Pitou, Genie, Donkey,)

3150
02:06:29,450 --> 02:06:30,550
(Izaha, Vector, Leia, Paul, Hamlet,
Siseon, Luna)

3151
02:06:30,550 --> 02:06:31,590
(Practicality: Maillard, Boss)

3152
02:06:31,890 --> 02:06:33,120
Who's that one person?

3153
02:06:33,120 --> 02:06:34,660
Today's MVP is...

3154
02:06:34,660 --> 02:06:35,990
Resident Leia.

3155
02:06:37,320 --> 02:06:38,930
Thank you.

3156
02:06:38,930 --> 02:06:40,260
- You're the MVP.
- Thank you.

3157
02:06:40,260 --> 02:06:41,400
What a relief.

3158
02:06:41,400 --> 02:06:43,100
It's a relief that we have one MVP.

3159
02:06:43,830 --> 02:06:45,070
It made me happy.

3160
02:06:45,130 --> 02:06:48,570
Unfortunately, it was nullified yesterday.

3161
02:06:48,640 --> 02:06:52,310
"What she's saying is worth
thinking about."

3162
02:06:52,410 --> 02:06:55,110
I think that's why people chose me as MVP.

3163
02:06:55,240 --> 02:06:56,680
I'm happy with that.

3164
02:06:57,580 --> 02:07:00,680
The leader negotiation will be held soon.

3165
02:07:00,780 --> 02:07:02,920
All team leaders,

3166
02:07:02,920 --> 02:07:05,420
please gather at the Community Center.

3167
02:07:05,890 --> 02:07:07,790
I don't know about anything else,

3168
02:07:07,790 --> 02:07:08,820
but being a leader feels pretty good.

3169
02:07:09,660 --> 02:07:11,790
Being the queen must be your thing.

3170
02:07:11,990 --> 02:07:13,130
I'm off.

3171
02:07:13,130 --> 02:07:14,630
- Take care.
- Bye.

3172
02:07:14,630 --> 02:07:16,530
- Hi.
- Hi.

3173
02:07:16,530 --> 02:07:17,630
Hi.

3174
02:07:18,030 --> 02:07:20,770
The Leader Negotiation will begin now.

3175
02:07:21,340 --> 02:07:23,300
Here's the pollution index...

3176
02:07:23,300 --> 02:07:25,310
for the entire Community Town.

3177
02:07:26,040 --> 02:07:27,940
- It used to be 15.
- The total pollution index...

3178
02:07:27,940 --> 02:07:29,080
accumulated over the past three days...

3179
02:07:29,210 --> 02:07:31,180
is 28.

3180
02:07:31,380 --> 02:07:33,250
Please note that once...

3181
02:07:33,250 --> 02:07:36,650
the pollution index reaches 100,
the town will be considered saturated.

3182
02:07:39,350 --> 02:07:41,020
It's indeed a linear relationship.

3183
02:07:41,020 --> 02:07:42,490
- We used three,
- Yes.

3184
02:07:42,490 --> 02:07:43,620
while Team Blue used ten.

3185
02:07:43,620 --> 02:07:45,560
- Did you not use any?
- No, I used five.

3186
02:07:45,560 --> 02:07:47,830
- But those were pollution-free credits.
- Right, you used pollution-free credits.

3187
02:07:47,830 --> 02:07:50,730
- Increasing by one seems right.
- Right.

3188
02:07:50,730 --> 02:07:52,870
My team will earn
pollution credits tomorrow.

3189
02:07:52,870 --> 02:07:54,740
We're short on credits right now.

3190
02:07:54,740 --> 02:07:56,970
- That seems like the right move for now.
- Right.

3191
02:07:57,340 --> 02:07:59,140
We could use another 70.

3192
02:07:59,410 --> 02:08:01,580
The higher the pollution index gets,

3193
02:08:01,640 --> 02:08:02,810
the happier I get.

3194
02:08:03,010 --> 02:08:04,750
A big amount of damage is good news to me.

3195
02:08:04,750 --> 02:08:05,850
The more danger they are in,

3196
02:08:05,850 --> 02:08:08,320
the more likely they'd break out into war,
the last resort.

3197
02:08:08,320 --> 02:08:09,620
Frequent wars are...

3198
02:08:09,620 --> 02:08:11,350
a big prize for me.

3199
02:08:11,520 --> 02:08:13,190
Okay, pollution. Let's go!

3200
02:08:14,250 --> 02:08:15,760
- Excuse me?
- Yes!

3201
02:08:15,990 --> 02:08:17,590
Here's the first agenda item.

3202
02:08:17,860 --> 02:08:21,260
It's about providing a life
for tomorrow's supermarket.

3203
02:08:21,600 --> 02:08:24,230
If the majority of leaders present agree,

3204
02:08:24,260 --> 02:08:26,200
a life will be provided.

3205
02:08:26,230 --> 02:08:28,770
However, the team providing the life...

3206
02:08:28,770 --> 02:08:30,770
must also give its consent.

3207
02:08:31,840 --> 02:08:34,070
I have a question regarding this.

3208
02:08:34,070 --> 02:08:35,210
I wasn't here...

3209
02:08:35,210 --> 02:08:36,780
- at the leader negotiation yesterday.
- Right.

3210
02:08:36,780 --> 02:08:40,450
The team providing the life...

3211
02:08:40,450 --> 02:08:41,880
will most likely be us.

3212
02:08:41,880 --> 02:08:43,620
What do...

3213
02:08:43,620 --> 02:08:45,850
the other two teams think about...

3214
02:08:45,920 --> 02:08:48,060
what our team gains from that?

3215
02:08:48,060 --> 02:08:49,220
- Either way...
- Your team...

3216
02:08:49,220 --> 02:08:51,560
was supposed to agree on that...

3217
02:08:51,560 --> 02:08:54,060
before coming here today.

3218
02:08:55,060 --> 02:08:56,230
Sorry?

3219
02:08:56,560 --> 02:08:58,030
- I heard nothing about it.
- The reward.

3220
02:08:58,030 --> 02:09:01,130
How your team wants
the rewards to be measured.

3221
02:09:01,230 --> 02:09:04,070
The leader said she couldn't decide on...

3222
02:09:04,300 --> 02:09:05,770
the exact number on her own.

3223
02:09:06,140 --> 02:09:09,240
(During yesterday's leader negotiation)

3224
02:09:09,240 --> 02:09:11,240
So before coming here,

3225
02:09:11,310 --> 02:09:13,380
I told them
I wouldn't commit to anything...

3226
02:09:13,380 --> 02:09:15,320
- we didn't agree on first.
- I see.

3227
02:09:16,550 --> 02:09:22,120
(Salt was supposed to negotiate
compensation for the life.)

3228
02:09:22,660 --> 02:09:25,960
Salt said she'd bring
the desired percentage.

3229
02:09:26,090 --> 02:09:28,730
I wonder why I never heard of this.

3230
02:09:29,130 --> 02:09:31,000
Then they suddenly started talking...

3231
02:09:31,000 --> 02:09:33,370
as if I should have come prepared
with an estimate for it.

3232
02:09:33,970 --> 02:09:35,270
But no one told me anything.

3233
02:09:35,340 --> 02:09:36,600
How was I supposed to know?

3234
02:09:36,600 --> 02:09:39,770
I don't know if Salt
simply failed to pass...

3235
02:09:39,770 --> 02:09:40,840
the information along...

3236
02:09:40,840 --> 02:09:42,980
or just didn't understand it properly
and forgot to tell me.

3237
02:09:42,980 --> 02:09:45,580
Either way, they were saying
I should've come prepared...

3238
02:09:45,580 --> 02:09:47,910
with an estimate of
what one life was worth,

3239
02:09:48,150 --> 02:09:50,080
and I was completely caught off guard.

3240
02:09:50,150 --> 02:09:52,620
I went there thinking,
"I'll return after giving him a life."

3241
02:09:52,620 --> 02:09:55,360
Salt only told me to talk things over
with Black.

3242
02:09:55,420 --> 02:09:58,530
So I was like, "I'm getting
a free meal tomorrow!" and went off.

3243
02:09:58,660 --> 02:10:01,160
I heard nothing about it.

3244
02:10:01,190 --> 02:10:03,800
Here's what I think.

3245
02:10:03,830 --> 02:10:07,500
Everyone here should contribute equally.

3246
02:10:07,500 --> 02:10:09,940
Team Blue should also bear
a quarter of it.

3247
02:10:09,940 --> 02:10:11,770
Of course Team Blue would take part in it.

3248
02:10:11,940 --> 02:10:15,580
Team Blue could buy food
when the supermarket opens.

3249
02:10:15,710 --> 02:10:16,940
- Right?
- Yes.

3250
02:10:17,180 --> 02:10:19,250
So let's break down the value of one life,

3251
02:10:19,250 --> 02:10:22,720
and each pays 0.25 of that value.

3252
02:10:24,820 --> 02:10:27,650
But here's the problem with that.

3253
02:10:27,720 --> 02:10:30,020
No diamonds were traded today,

3254
02:10:30,020 --> 02:10:32,330
so we can't put a value on one life...

3255
02:10:32,330 --> 02:10:33,830
in terms of diamonds yet.

3256
02:10:33,960 --> 02:10:35,460
We can't use yesterday's value.

3257
02:10:35,460 --> 02:10:37,300
Why don't the leaders
come to an agreement now...

3258
02:10:37,300 --> 02:10:39,170
on how much one life is worth?

3259
02:10:39,170 --> 02:10:41,370
Because the value will change tomorrow.

3260
02:10:42,500 --> 02:10:44,170
If you two settle it now,

3261
02:10:44,170 --> 02:10:46,310
I'll give you a discount based on that.

3262
02:10:46,340 --> 02:10:48,410
That's what I'm talking about.

3263
02:10:48,410 --> 02:10:50,210
I'll be flexible.

3264
02:10:50,210 --> 02:10:51,650
No matter how many...

3265
02:10:52,150 --> 02:10:54,680
So you want to know
how many I was planning to pay...

3266
02:10:54,680 --> 02:10:55,850
per life?

3267
02:10:56,250 --> 02:10:57,320
Yes.

3268
02:11:10,160 --> 02:11:12,600
Then can you tell me first?

3269
02:11:14,500 --> 02:11:17,700
I don't know...

3270
02:11:17,700 --> 02:11:19,410
how much the currency value changed. So...

3271
02:11:19,410 --> 02:11:21,410
Because we've been spending the minimum,

3272
02:11:21,410 --> 02:11:23,710
it hasn't changed much since yesterday.

3273
02:11:23,710 --> 02:11:26,280
I can't tell you the exact number anyway.

3274
02:11:27,410 --> 02:11:29,520
- Then...
- If I make a suggestion,

3275
02:11:29,520 --> 02:11:31,920
will you give it to me for the price
you offered on the first day?

3276
02:11:32,590 --> 02:11:34,720
- And...
- But...

3277
02:11:36,860 --> 02:11:39,260
I can't do that.
I can't give it to you for that price.

3278
02:11:39,260 --> 02:11:41,290
- From what I remember, it was ten.
- Yes.

3279
02:11:41,290 --> 02:11:42,860
I can't give it to you for ten.

3280
02:11:42,860 --> 02:11:45,300
We only use a little...

3281
02:11:45,300 --> 02:11:47,600
because when we divide it by person,

3282
02:11:47,600 --> 02:11:49,070
we get the least amount.

3283
02:11:49,740 --> 02:11:53,270
When we convert it to the actual prize,
we don't get much.

3284
02:11:53,770 --> 02:11:56,610
Is communism Team White's concept?

3285
02:11:56,610 --> 02:12:00,610
Why are they dividing all resources
by person?

3286
02:12:00,810 --> 02:12:02,720
If they don't stop thinking...

3287
02:12:02,720 --> 02:12:06,390
everyone will get a share,

3288
02:12:06,750 --> 02:12:08,590
Team White needs a new leader.

3289
02:12:09,160 --> 02:12:10,820
That's not going to happen in this game.

3290
02:12:11,390 --> 02:12:12,830
Can the basic currency issue...

3291
02:12:12,830 --> 02:12:15,630
be smaller than the amount
you first received?

3292
02:12:15,630 --> 02:12:16,730
Of course.

3293
02:12:16,730 --> 02:12:18,060
Really? Then...

3294
02:12:18,060 --> 02:12:20,630
the price per one would be very weird.

3295
02:12:20,770 --> 02:12:22,000
It is weird.

3296
02:12:22,000 --> 02:12:23,740
Then...

3297
02:12:23,740 --> 02:12:26,840
were you expecting it to double
every time?

3298
02:12:26,840 --> 02:12:29,010
Anything lower than 200...

3299
02:12:29,180 --> 02:12:30,940
makes the value of the diamond weird.

3300
02:12:30,940 --> 02:12:33,250
It's way lower than that.

3301
02:12:33,250 --> 02:12:34,350
- Really?
- Yes.

3302
02:12:34,350 --> 02:12:36,580
- I've been trying to tell you that.
- But then the price...

3303
02:12:37,280 --> 02:12:40,290
I didn't know you were worried this much.

3304
02:12:40,290 --> 02:12:42,090
If it keeps doubling...

3305
02:12:42,090 --> 02:12:43,260
For example,

3306
02:12:43,260 --> 02:12:45,130
if 200 were issued yesterday,

3307
02:12:45,130 --> 02:12:46,930
but 400 were issued today,

3308
02:12:47,430 --> 02:12:49,130
they might have 800.

3309
02:12:49,130 --> 02:12:50,300
So we never know.

3310
02:12:50,300 --> 02:12:53,470
I told you we weren't going to do that
at first.

3311
02:12:53,470 --> 02:12:57,170
So, receiving 10 just like the 1st day...

3312
02:12:57,170 --> 02:13:00,340
is not completely unreasonable.

3313
02:13:02,340 --> 02:13:03,640
But not now.

3314
02:13:04,140 --> 02:13:06,350
- How many are you expecting then?
- That's not the case right now.

3315
02:13:06,880 --> 02:13:08,980
I can't go any lower than ten.

3316
02:13:08,980 --> 02:13:10,620
Then make an offer.

3317
02:13:15,290 --> 02:13:16,820
At least 16.

3318
02:13:16,820 --> 02:13:20,630
That makes no sense to us.

3319
02:13:20,730 --> 02:13:22,900
I'm not saying that's how much
it's going to be worth tomorrow too.

3320
02:13:22,900 --> 02:13:24,630
Considering the current value of a life,

3321
02:13:24,630 --> 02:13:26,170
I need at least 16.

3322
02:13:26,170 --> 02:13:29,570
You're saying that because your idea
of how much a diamond is worth...

3323
02:13:29,570 --> 02:13:31,910
is different from mine.

3324
02:13:32,170 --> 02:13:35,040
I know 16 was unreasonable.

3325
02:13:35,480 --> 02:13:38,210
I couldn't really argue with her,

3326
02:13:38,410 --> 02:13:39,680
logically speaking.

3327
02:13:39,680 --> 02:13:41,720
So I kept the stance, "Whatever."

3328
02:13:41,820 --> 02:13:43,250
I acted boldly.

3329
02:13:43,750 --> 02:13:45,650
As of today,

3330
02:13:45,650 --> 02:13:47,520
I'm saying I need at least 16.

3331
02:13:47,520 --> 02:13:49,160
Are you saying if we made a deal today,

3332
02:13:49,160 --> 02:13:51,360
you would've traded 1 life
for 16 diamonds?

3333
02:13:52,660 --> 02:13:54,430
That's what you're doing right now.

3334
02:13:59,670 --> 02:14:02,000
- They don't get along.
- Those two?

3335
02:14:02,000 --> 02:14:03,070
- Yes.
- They don't get along.

3336
02:14:03,070 --> 02:14:04,100
A war is better.

3337
02:14:06,070 --> 02:14:07,940
Even if we divide that by four...

3338
02:14:07,940 --> 02:14:10,040
and get a discount,
we only end up with four.

3339
02:14:11,910 --> 02:14:13,010
That's still a lot.

3340
02:14:13,280 --> 02:14:15,180
You said you'd raise the price tomorrow.

3341
02:14:15,180 --> 02:14:17,320
I'm going to raise the price really high.
I'm warning you.

3342
02:14:17,320 --> 02:14:18,850
Considering all these circumstances,

3343
02:14:18,850 --> 02:14:21,590
if we don't get four each,
we're basically left with no reward.

3344
02:14:24,060 --> 02:14:25,590
Sixteen per life,

3345
02:14:25,590 --> 02:14:27,190
and it's divided by four.

3346
02:14:30,430 --> 02:14:31,460
Okay.

3347
02:14:31,460 --> 02:14:34,470
Are you saying I can give you more...

3348
02:14:34,470 --> 02:14:36,640
- when we make a trade tomorrow?
- Yes.

3349
02:14:37,140 --> 02:14:39,010
And I'm saying I need
a four diamond discount...

3350
02:14:39,010 --> 02:14:40,540
- from him.
- I'll take four diamonds off.

3351
02:14:40,540 --> 02:14:43,180
I'll talk to you about the credits later.

3352
02:14:43,180 --> 02:14:44,940
- Because it's iffy.
- Okay.

3353
02:14:45,050 --> 02:14:46,650
Okay. Fine.

3354
02:14:47,750 --> 02:14:49,950
Team White didn't have to do that today...

3355
02:14:50,150 --> 02:14:52,050
from what I've seen.

3356
02:14:52,050 --> 02:14:53,050
But she went on with it.

3357
02:14:54,220 --> 02:14:55,760
How nice of her.

3358
02:14:56,220 --> 02:14:58,060
Do you all agree with it?

3359
02:14:58,060 --> 02:14:59,630
- I do.
- Yes, I do.

3360
02:14:59,630 --> 02:15:01,460
Because all four teams agreed...

3361
02:15:01,460 --> 02:15:02,600
It'll be provided.

3362
02:15:02,600 --> 02:15:04,330
Negotiation complete.

3363
02:15:04,500 --> 02:15:08,000
The team leader who provides a life
for Black to run the supermarket...

3364
02:15:08,570 --> 02:15:12,140
- must provide a life immediately.
- The store will finally open.

3365
02:15:13,240 --> 02:15:14,410
I'm starving.

3366
02:15:20,350 --> 02:15:21,950
(Provide 1 life to run a supermarket
the next day.)

3367
02:15:21,950 --> 02:15:25,650
A life's been provided
to run a supermarket the next day.

3368
02:15:25,820 --> 02:15:28,790
- The supermarket will open tomorrow.
- What happened yesterday?

3369
02:15:28,960 --> 02:15:32,430
I was shocked that it was closed today.

3370
02:15:34,090 --> 02:15:35,700
The second item on the agenda.

3371
02:15:35,700 --> 02:15:39,000
This concerns the decision
to provide aid or impose sanctions.

3372
02:15:39,130 --> 02:15:41,800
If a majority of the leaders agree,

3373
02:15:41,800 --> 02:15:43,600
resources currently in their possession...

3374
02:15:43,600 --> 02:15:45,110
may be transferred between two teams...

3375
02:15:45,110 --> 02:15:46,610
without spending any credits.

3376
02:15:47,140 --> 02:15:50,480
Only one kind of resource
can be transferred...

3377
02:15:50,480 --> 02:15:52,480
from one team to the other.

3378
02:15:52,850 --> 02:15:54,810
There is no limit in quantity.

3379
02:15:54,810 --> 02:15:56,120
- Only one?
- It's one way.

3380
02:15:56,620 --> 02:15:59,120
However, if you decide to provide aid,

3381
02:15:59,120 --> 02:16:01,190
the team leader providing the resource...

3382
02:16:01,190 --> 02:16:03,690
must agree.

3383
02:16:03,690 --> 02:16:04,960
Okay.

3384
02:16:05,290 --> 02:16:07,190
Next is sanctions.

3385
02:16:07,330 --> 02:16:09,700
If a majority of the leaders agree,

3386
02:16:09,700 --> 02:16:13,830
one team will be prohibited from using
the Trading Station for the following day.

3387
02:16:13,830 --> 02:16:14,870
Oh, my gosh.

3388
02:16:15,800 --> 02:16:19,140
We made a verbal agreement...

3389
02:16:19,140 --> 02:16:21,470
- between Team Blue and Team White.
- Yes.

3390
02:16:21,470 --> 02:16:23,310
Anyone else who needs...

3391
02:16:23,310 --> 02:16:25,350
aid or sanction?

3392
02:16:25,350 --> 02:16:27,510
I have nothing to transfer.

3393
02:16:27,510 --> 02:16:28,550
- What about you?
- I agree.

3394
02:16:28,550 --> 02:16:29,920
- Yes. Me too.
- Me too.

3395
02:16:29,920 --> 02:16:31,180
I agree with providing aid.

3396
02:16:31,180 --> 02:16:33,290
You have agreed on providing aid.

3397
02:16:33,290 --> 02:16:35,420
Team White will aid Team Blue...

3398
02:16:35,420 --> 02:16:37,520
with one credit.

3399
02:16:37,520 --> 02:16:40,030
(1 credit)

3400
02:16:40,030 --> 02:16:41,360
Thanks for the cool trade.

3401
02:16:41,360 --> 02:16:43,660
- All negotiations are complete.
- Yes.

3402
02:16:43,660 --> 02:16:46,870
We'll move on to today's life submission.

3403
02:16:46,870 --> 02:16:47,930
Okay.

3404
02:16:47,930 --> 02:16:49,000
Good job.

3405
02:16:49,000 --> 02:16:50,500
- Good job.
- Good job.

3406
02:16:53,810 --> 02:16:56,110
(Life Submission)

3407
02:16:56,480 --> 02:17:00,010
(Team Blue and Team Red submit lives.)

3408
02:17:00,910 --> 02:17:02,280
(Everyone in Team Blue survives.)

3409
02:17:02,280 --> 02:17:04,280
Another day gone.

3410
02:17:05,190 --> 02:17:06,620
Team White, you can go.

3411
02:17:06,620 --> 02:17:09,660
Me? Actually,

3412
02:17:10,190 --> 02:17:14,390
each diamond still has a very high value.

3413
02:17:14,390 --> 02:17:18,030
Isn't it better to lower it?

3414
02:17:18,030 --> 02:17:20,700
So can I issue more?

3415
02:17:21,630 --> 02:17:23,270
But we wouldn't want to...

3416
02:17:23,270 --> 02:17:24,740
- No?
- do that.

3417
02:17:24,740 --> 02:17:27,740
That means Team White isn't using
their right.

3418
02:17:27,740 --> 02:17:31,280
- It's your choice.
- Well, that's up to us.

3419
02:17:31,280 --> 02:17:34,450
But I'm not sure what's more convenient
for the members.

3420
02:17:35,150 --> 02:17:37,120
I don't know why you're discussing it
with us.

3421
02:17:37,120 --> 02:17:39,920
I noticed earlier...

3422
02:17:39,920 --> 02:17:42,420
that we had completely different ideas.

3423
02:17:42,420 --> 02:17:44,420
I also want to make you trust me.

3424
02:17:44,420 --> 02:17:46,060
So you're doing that to build trust?

3425
02:17:46,060 --> 02:17:47,390
Because I need to make trades.

3426
02:17:47,390 --> 02:17:50,330
If that's what you want,

3427
02:17:50,330 --> 02:17:52,430
you shouldn't raise too many
compared to today.

3428
02:17:52,430 --> 02:17:53,900
Okay.

3429
02:17:53,900 --> 02:17:55,770
Then I'll trade with you.

3430
02:17:55,770 --> 02:17:56,800
Yes, please.

3431
02:17:56,800 --> 02:17:57,800
If you remove a few.

3432
02:17:57,970 --> 02:17:59,610
What do you mean?

3433
02:17:59,940 --> 02:18:00,940
- What?
- No.

3434
02:18:00,940 --> 02:18:02,510
He's the worst.

3435
02:18:02,510 --> 02:18:04,080
- Just remove a few.
- What does he mean by that?

3436
02:18:04,080 --> 02:18:05,850
- The lives.
- He's saying...

3437
02:18:05,850 --> 02:18:07,410
- remove a few lives.
- He's telling me to reduce my members.

3438
02:18:07,910 --> 02:18:09,820
Just reduce the number of people to feed.

3439
02:18:10,020 --> 02:18:11,120
How cruel.

3440
02:18:13,690 --> 02:18:16,460
Team White will submit lives.

3441
02:18:20,830 --> 02:18:22,760
(Everyone in Team White survives.)

3442
02:18:28,670 --> 02:18:32,040
I will issue 166 diamonds.

3443
02:18:32,770 --> 02:18:35,310
Actually, before the leader negotiation,

3444
02:18:35,310 --> 02:18:37,180
I already wrote a crazy number...

3445
02:18:37,180 --> 02:18:39,880
on the diamond issuance voucher.

3446
02:18:40,780 --> 02:18:42,950
- Are we issuing the currency today?
- We should.

3447
02:18:42,950 --> 02:18:44,220
How many today?

3448
02:18:44,480 --> 02:18:46,620
I'm thinking 166 for today.

3449
02:18:46,890 --> 02:18:48,690
- You're going to make it 400?
- Yes.

3450
02:18:48,690 --> 02:18:51,290
I'm going to reduce the value by half...

3451
02:18:51,290 --> 02:18:52,830
compared to the first day.

3452
02:18:52,830 --> 02:18:55,160
So if I issue enough to make 400 in total,

3453
02:18:55,160 --> 02:18:59,800
the value of the currency will become
half of the first day.

3454
02:18:59,800 --> 02:19:01,570
- The supermarket was closed today.
- Right.

3455
02:19:01,570 --> 02:19:03,200
When the price goes up tomorrow,

3456
02:19:03,200 --> 02:19:06,410
- Right. We won't be blamed.
- we won't be blamed.

3457
02:19:06,410 --> 02:19:07,610
- That's true.
- Then...

3458
02:19:07,610 --> 02:19:09,340
we should submit 166...

3459
02:19:09,340 --> 02:19:11,040
to make it 400 like you said.

3460
02:19:11,040 --> 02:19:12,410
(Team White had already chosen
the volume.)

3461
02:19:13,250 --> 02:19:16,720
I know it wasn't a conscientious act.

3462
02:19:16,720 --> 02:19:19,320
But I realized Team Blue...

3463
02:19:19,320 --> 02:19:22,660
had a communication problem.

3464
02:19:22,660 --> 02:19:24,520
I knew they'd be confused.

3465
02:19:24,660 --> 02:19:26,430
So I decided to lowball the value.

3466
02:19:26,430 --> 02:19:29,500
From Team Blue's perspective,
they got what they wanted.

3467
02:19:29,500 --> 02:19:32,000
But I didn't just say okay.

3468
02:19:32,000 --> 02:19:34,200
I kept the deal pretty tense.

3469
02:19:34,200 --> 02:19:37,870
I'm sure that made them realize...

3470
02:19:37,870 --> 02:19:40,110
the diamonds are currently very valuable.

3471
02:19:40,810 --> 02:19:42,780
(166 diamonds have been issued.)

3472
02:19:45,880 --> 02:19:47,410
Why are there so many?

3473
02:19:48,080 --> 02:19:49,880
This is a lot.

3474
02:19:50,250 --> 02:19:52,250
I issued 166.

3475
02:19:52,250 --> 02:19:54,050
There were four boxes of them.

3476
02:19:54,920 --> 02:19:57,890
I moved them before anyone saw.

3477
02:20:03,560 --> 02:20:05,470
I'm acting like a total jerk.

3478
02:20:17,710 --> 02:20:20,080
This should be okay.

3479
02:20:31,960 --> 02:20:34,730
I might as well switch
to digital diamonds soon.

3480
02:20:39,230 --> 02:20:40,630
- She's back.
- She's back.

3481
02:20:40,630 --> 02:20:41,770
- Welcome back.
- Thank you.

3482
02:20:41,770 --> 02:20:43,970
- Welcome back.
- Welcome back.

3483
02:20:44,170 --> 02:20:46,210
You look happy today.

3484
02:20:46,210 --> 02:20:48,440
Really? I'm very unhappy right now.

3485
02:20:48,440 --> 02:20:49,440
- Why?
- Why?

3486
02:20:49,440 --> 02:20:50,510
I just...

3487
02:20:50,610 --> 02:20:52,750
feel like such a bad person.

3488
02:20:52,750 --> 02:20:54,350
- That's okay.
- Really?

3489
02:20:55,010 --> 02:20:56,150
Also,

3490
02:20:56,450 --> 02:20:59,090
they think
we didn't increase the value very much.

3491
02:20:59,090 --> 02:21:00,190
I see.

3492
02:21:00,190 --> 02:21:02,190
- That's why you're not happy.
- Yes.

3493
02:21:02,190 --> 02:21:06,030
Also, I was being very stubborn there.

3494
02:21:06,160 --> 02:21:08,030
I thought I needed to lowball them.

3495
02:21:08,030 --> 02:21:10,260
Because it was Pitou.

3496
02:21:10,260 --> 02:21:12,470
I thought I could lowball her
if I tried a bit.

3497
02:21:12,470 --> 02:21:14,770
So I spent a lot of time there.

3498
02:21:15,330 --> 02:21:17,170
- Did you know that?
- What?

3499
02:21:17,170 --> 02:21:19,310
That only you live
if you use only one life?

3500
02:21:20,110 --> 02:21:21,710
- Of course, I didn't.
- You didn't?

3501
02:21:22,280 --> 02:21:23,840
- They didn't tell you that.
- The fact that information...

3502
02:21:23,840 --> 02:21:26,980
wasn't shared was my first worry.

3503
02:21:26,980 --> 02:21:28,710
I was shocked too.

3504
02:21:28,710 --> 02:21:30,420
- But first...
- Yes?

3505
02:21:30,420 --> 02:21:34,620
Should we make Salt,
who'll get us to coexist, the leader...

3506
02:21:34,620 --> 02:21:35,720
Because it seems she'll do that?

3507
02:21:35,720 --> 02:21:38,220
Would it be best to trust her
and go with that decision or...

3508
02:21:38,220 --> 02:21:40,460
First of all, I don't plan to stay alone.

3509
02:21:40,460 --> 02:21:43,630
- Because even if I do...
- There are those diamonds.

3510
02:21:44,100 --> 02:21:45,730
You could take all of that for yourself.

3511
02:21:46,670 --> 02:21:50,700
What stance is Team White
taking right now?

3512
02:21:50,970 --> 02:21:52,840
Team White will go to war
if productive activities...

3513
02:21:52,840 --> 02:21:54,710
don't go well tomorrow.

3514
02:21:55,240 --> 02:21:59,050
But we can't make a deal with them
in this situation.

3515
02:22:01,850 --> 02:22:03,680
If you don't, there'll be war.
Are you okay with that?

3516
02:22:03,850 --> 02:22:06,090
I'm saying it's better for us
if a war breaks out.

3517
02:22:06,090 --> 02:22:07,220
- It's better?
- Yes.

3518
02:22:08,720 --> 02:22:11,020
So there could be a war tomorrow.

3519
02:22:11,020 --> 02:22:13,860
- There's a high possibility.
- Yes.

3520
02:22:14,030 --> 02:22:16,860
Team Red is even thinking
of attacking first right now.

3521
02:22:20,100 --> 02:22:22,440
About that,

3522
02:22:22,440 --> 02:22:24,140
I mean, I'm sure you know...

3523
02:22:24,140 --> 02:22:25,370
I won't say anything.

3524
02:22:25,370 --> 02:22:27,740
- Tomorrow, without our teams...
- If I say...

